thub-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/furystack/furystack/commit/29eed541452b2e56c016316fcaf74c896a084afe","node_id":"C_kwDOCYZLQNoAKDI5ZWVkNTQxNDUyYjJlNTZjMDE2MzE2ZmNhZjc0Yzg5NmEwODRhZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/furystack/furystack/commit/e6794d260ee31e5bd100bc7705471bb77a3bdd16","sha":"e6794d260ee31e5bd100bc7705471bb77a3bdd16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/commits/e6794d260ee31e5bd100bc7705471bb77a3bdd16"}],"sha":"29eed541452b2e56c016316fcaf74c896a084afe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/commits/29eed541452b2e56c016316fcaf74c896a084afe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16716099?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gallayl","id":16716099,"login":"gallayl","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzE2MDk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/commits/e6794d260ee31e5bd100bc7705471bb77a3bdd16/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-21T14:46:10Z","email":"gallayl@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Lajos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-21T14:46:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix/form updates (#647)\n\n## 🐛 Summary\n\nFixes form integration for `Checkbox`, `Radio`, and `Switch` in\n`@furystack/shades-common-components`:\n\n- `Checkbox` was calling `ev.stopPropagation()` on the inner input''s\n`change`\nevent, which prevented the parent `<Form>` from ever seeing the change\nand\n  left `rawFormData` stale.\n- `Radio` and `Switch` were wiring `onchange={props.onchange}` on the\ninner\ninput *and* relying on Shade''s `attachProps` to mirror `onchange` onto\nthe\n  host element, causing `props.onchange` to fire twice per change.\n- All three components were forcing `value=\"\"` on the inner input when\nthe\ncaller omitted `value`, breaking the browser''s native `\"on\"` default in\n  `FormData`.\n\nThe fix:\n\n- Removes manual `onchange` wiring from the inner inputs; the host-level\n`onchange` (set by `attachProps`) handles user callbacks and the native\n  event continues bubbling to `<Form>`.\n- Keeps a local `handleChange` in `Checkbox` only to restore the\n  `indeterminate` visual state across toggles.\n- Spreads `value` conditionally so omitting the prop yields the native\n  `\"on\"` default.\n\n## ✅ Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit specs for Checkbox / Radio / Switch covering:\n      Form propagation (rawFormData updates), single-call `onchange`,\n      and native `\"on\"` default when `value` is omitted.\n- [x] E2E spec in `shades-showcase-app` toggling Workshops / Networking\ncheckboxes and the Notifications switch, asserting the `#raw` block\n      on the advanced form.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"c87f694889055e10298eebdd55d83c81cce16528","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/git/trees/c87f694889055e10298eebdd55d83c81cce16528"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/git/commits/e6794d260ee31e5bd100bc7705471bb77a3bdd16","verification":{"payload":"tree c87f694889055e10298eebdd55d83c81cce16528\nparent a985aad9fc895944ac37a0f584bf4760f12cbf45\nauthor Lajos <gallayl@users.noreply.github.com> 1779374770 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779374770 +0000\n\nFix/form updates (#647)\n\n## 🐛 Summary\n\nFixes form integration for `Checkbox`, `Radio`, and `Switch` in\n`@furystack/shades-common-components`:\n\n- `Checkbox` was calling `ev.stopPropagation()` on the inner input''s\n`change`\nevent, which prevented the parent `<Form>` from ever seeing the change\nand\n  left `rawFormData` stale.\n- `Radio` and `Switch` were wiring `onchange={props.onchange}` on the\ninner\ninput *and* relying on Shade''s `attachProps` to mirror `onchange` onto\nthe\n  host element, causing `props.onchange` to fire twice per change.\n- All three components were forcing `value=\"\"` on the inner input when\nthe\ncaller omitted `value`, breaking the browser''s native `\"on\"` default in\n  `FormData`.\n\nThe fix:\n\n- Removes manual `onchange` wiring from the inner inputs; the host-level\n`onchange` (set by `attachProps`) handles user callbacks and the native\n  event continues bubbling to `<Form>`.\n- Keeps a local `handleChange` in `Checkbox` only to restore the\n  `indeterminate` visual state across toggles.\n- Spreads `value` conditionally so omitting the prop yields the native\n  `\"on\"` default.\n\n## ✅ Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit specs for Checkbox / Radio / Switch covering:\n      Form propagation (rawFormData updates), single-call `onchange`,\n      and native `\"on\"` default when `value` is omitted.\n- [x] E2E spec in `shades-showcase-app` toggling Workshops / Networking\ncheckboxes and the Notifications switch, asserting the `#raw` block\n      on the advanced form.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reaso