https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/furystack/furystack/commit/94796caecc1f9308c789ce9e38c0a13e9741a70d","node_id":"C_kwDOCYZLQNoAKDk0Nzk2Y2FlY2MxZjkzMDhjNzg5Y2U5ZTM4YzBhMTNlOTc0MWE3MGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/furystack/furystack/commit/b2191ea49f58c8718351585a72175fb85d0e2ae0","sha":"b2191ea49f58c8718351585a72175fb85d0e2ae0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/commits/b2191ea49f58c8718351585a72175fb85d0e2ae0"}],"sha":"94796caecc1f9308c789ce9e38c0a13e9741a70d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/commits/94796caecc1f9308c789ce9e38c0a13e9741a70d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16716099?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gallayl","id":16716099,"login":"gallayl","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzE2MDk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/commits/b2191ea49f58c8718351585a72175fb85d0e2ae0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-17T12:55:32Z","email":"gallayl@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Lajos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-17T12:55:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/collection service id reconciliation (#634)\n\n## 🧭 Overview\n\nAdds an opt‑in `idField` to `CollectionServiceOptions` in\n`@furystack/shades-common-components`. When provided,\n`CollectionService` reconciles `focusedEntry` and `selection` against\nthe new entries array on every `data` change, swapping stale object\nreferences for their id‑matched counterparts and dropping entries whose\nid disappeared.\n\n## ✨ What changes\n\n- New `CollectionServiceOptions.idField?: keyof T` option.\n- Internal `reconcileRefs(entries)` helper + `data` subscription wired\nin the constructor when `idField` is set.\n- Subscription is disposed in `Symbol.dispose`.\n- Behavior is unchanged when `idField` is omitted.\n\n## 🎯 Why\n\nKeyboard navigation and selection silently break when the backing data\narray is rebuilt with new object instances (e.g. after a refetch),\nbecause the held references no longer exist in the new array.\nReconciling by id restores the expected UX without requiring callers to\nre‑apply focus/selection manually.\n\n## 🧪 Tests\n\n7 new unit tests under `idField auto-reconciliation` covering\nfocus/selection reconcile, stale removal, opt‑out, reference‑equality\nshort‑circuit, and end‑to‑end keyboard nav after refresh.","tree":{"sha":"e59029c9d284f31c8f91718ba49332a5e47d3a30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/git/trees/e59029c9d284f31c8f91718ba49332a5e47d3a30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/git/commits/b2191ea49f58c8718351585a72175fb85d0e2ae0","verification":{"payload":"tree e59029c9d284f31c8f91718ba49332a5e47d3a30\nparent 6642a3d1af0ae353b29faf56a1dd17ac558ba140\nauthor Lajos <gallayl@users.noreply.github.com> 1776430532 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776430532 +0000\n\nFeat/collection service id reconciliation (#634)\n\n## 🧭 Overview\n\nAdds an opt‑in `idField` to `CollectionServiceOptions` in\n`@furystack/shades-common-components`. When provided,\n`CollectionService` reconciles `focusedEntry` and `selection` against\nthe new entries array on every `data` change, swapping stale object\nreferences for their id‑matched counterparts and dropping entries whose\nid disappeared.\n\n## ✨ What changes\n\n- New `CollectionServiceOptions.idField?: keyof T` option.\n- Internal `reconcileRefs(entries)` helper + `data` subscription wired\nin the constructor when `idField` is set.\n- Subscription is disposed in `Symbol.dispose`.\n- Behavior is unchanged when `idField` is omitted.\n\n## 🎯 Why\n\nKeyboard navigation and selection silently break when the backing data\narray is rebuilt with new object instances (e.g. after a refetch),\nbecause the held references no longer exist in the new array.\nReconciling by id restores the expected UX without requiring callers to\nre‑apply focus/selection manually.\n\n## 🧪 Tests\n\n7 new unit tests under `idField auto-reconciliation` covering\nfocus/selection reconcile, stale removal, opt‑out, reference‑equality\nshort‑circuit, and end‑to‑end keyboard nav after refresh.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp4i3ECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALdgQAB0VrK7nY6DsytddBVm9o12w\nkK0MiFFvKuKA3GcKQ8/cTUKwMOPtzh5B6VUKFmVx5DoGmyxjI723ldiBB+w9cfVQ\nkQtV7IARmqIxmOFIsSW9y6fw3mcO+9u8xDZqWAkaoKUDS/A9AtH1pnpgYN8FHQda\noHfi5ZeY8IgcmLdeMRrsmHHESJTnLAEBylITE1hma7ifMI3yHTgbV6H0SqBMHn5I\nvzdxx1MrYS3q74ugpw49Q4uFehzvliXYJ5eQDd1J+VGLylgk4PBaLQYhcGCBh64T\nAfXyqzWYhWZ0WQGxh3DbXpjdkcpfNZK+pTRSsTRgcEiqamxnpcYh5J0DBVUPEoyM\nzQAJIbRBBmE8EmYyKjgU9eIspHehq8Fwa88sCYwi/IFphTRBvtxqUJX3xPx7Ex5Y\nkZwBxoP2jVGu3/OxYV6pZzN2vtEdD1s0hqnj63YMiXfiacdu2b4C6MAZ5BUI0qRj\n6Y1E7BWHhwiU21Xq7dCsSp/2vfpYAFr7Zu0HqXq2IUFuohdacJalfEO/PLvibkgr\n8w+sHjAEpyenYx+a4sDkf2DjmQNGuVQeXMlk8xB8y3TeLT88K5m/UxmF11PE2oWV\nWKTK1yb22DfNnPnptzcZlWpUGlBfHAPFCHWvTkPU60zLhnHxx6a8WJD/RXL0eea2\nwjMqmb0JFMZQEmtfumxW\n=eyqU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-17T12:55:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users