ub.com/users/gallayl/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/commits/d3f60c49f52befbc8b592466e4e2c6aa1c81a018/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-27T15:39:17Z","email":"gallayl@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Lajos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-27T15:39:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix/nested router type safety (#630)\n\n## 🧭 Type-safe programmatic navigation for NestedRouter\n\nAdds `nestedNavigate()` and `createNestedNavigate()` for programmatic\nSPA navigation within the nested router system, with the same\ntype-safety guarantees as `NestedRouteLink` / `createNestedRouteLink`.\n\nAlso fixes a type inference bug where `ExtractRoutePaths` and\n`createNestedRouteLink` failed to work with routes that have concrete\nmatch parameter types (e.g. `NestedRoute<{ stackName: string }>`), by\ncorrecting the generic constraint from `NestedRoute<unknown>` to\n`NestedRoute<any>`.\n\n## ✨ New API\n\n- `nestedNavigate(injector, path, params?)` — navigates using\n`LocationService`, with optional route parameter compilation\n- `createNestedNavigate<typeof routes>()` — returns a type-safe wrapper\nthat restricts paths to valid routes and requires `params` when\nparameterized\n\n## 🐛 Fix\n\n- Generic constraint on `ExtractRoutePaths` and `createNestedRouteLink`\nchanged from `NestedRoute<unknown>` to `NestedRoute<any>` to fix type\ninference with typed route components","tree":{"sha":"5ece4e8345406bc673edd8ea247ed5adb359bc7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/git/trees/5ece4e8345406bc673edd8ea247ed5adb359bc7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/git/commits/d3f60c49f52befbc8b592466e4e2c6aa1c81a018","verification":{"payload":"tree 5ece4e8345406bc673edd8ea247ed5adb359bc7a\nparent 600c285708f83fb0033bf0d71dff65e8076372cd\nauthor Lajos <gallayl@users.noreply.github.com> 1774625957 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774625957 +0000\n\nFix/nested router type safety (#630)\n\n## 🧭 Type-safe programmatic navigation for NestedRouter\n\nAdds `nestedNavigate()` and `createNestedNavigate()` for programmatic\nSPA navigation within the nested router system, with the same\ntype-safety guarantees as `NestedRouteLink` / `createNestedRouteLink`.\n\nAlso fixes a type inference bug where `ExtractRoutePaths` and\n`createNestedRouteLink` failed to work with routes that have concrete\nmatch parameter types (e.g. `NestedRoute<{ stackName: string }>`), by\ncorrecting the generic constraint from `NestedRoute<unknown>` to\n`NestedRoute<any>`.\n\n## ✨ New API\n\n- `nestedNavigate(injector, path, params?)` — navigates using\n`LocationService`, with optional route parameter compilation\n- `createNestedNavigate<typeof routes>()` — returns a type-safe wrapper\nthat restricts paths to valid routes and requires `params` when\nparameterized\n\n## 🐛 Fix\n\n- Generic constraint on `ExtractRoutePaths` and `createNestedRouteLink`\nchanged from `NestedRoute<unknown>` to `NestedRoute<any>` to fix type\ninference with typed route components","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpxqSlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1QsQABVGB2r/OoLJyiVKIVdX5uO6\nGxmwMMKJmwzHO3RyAV/fdXjAtdbmgyUzvCPYTE5370ZVmg6LnwFe79R19Yb8SbEw\nSiOBjMQBwEPNqgSqZqTDesEVKOyIFNfx3K1oxP0o3SjPSrOUt17Pc6rv7rPt5Zyy\nE4GjSzhpAfRrM4ur+Of9kBffPuu7zmsdEzWJGURv/qDXzxm4NmwOPn8JEvValb1I\nJoAwJDtnEJbzSATckYs1wXd3BEDsuEY7ZlBDTDfz0ZGAexfVEuS9E4Nc1zea2WqZ\n3kMcHrg/SxC0SViykycM62R9TmLQTsja8/cY1P6Wp/n/D82fcJpggdLZRpK+PUv1\nsgZq6wvZKjGrDqstAXeyDcuoFP3v/Gl39V0/acGbGqA/QnGry7zihGMrRR97RhNv\nsmKYy2dURh0FTNfv4iUdT94DAoBPeiYk5ob9jaQ5K04Y2P8hxgVHgJn3hUOR3KJ6\ngE