omment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-07T14:25:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(Shades): Shades cleanups and rewamps (#620)\n\n## 🔧 Shades API cleanups and terminology correction\n\nRenames `shadowDomName` to `customElementName` throughout the Shades\nframework to correctly reflect that Shades uses Custom Elements, not\nShadow DOM. Also refactors DataGrid and progress components to use a\ncontrolled-component pattern (plain values + callbacks) instead of\n`ObservableValue` props, simplifying the consumer API.\n\n### ✨ Highlights\n- **Terminology fix:** `shadowDomName` → `customElementName` in\n`ShadeOptions` and all components\n- **DataGrid:** `findOptions` is now a plain value prop with\n`onFindOptionsChange` callback\n- **Progress:** `CircularProgress` and `LinearProgress` accept `value:\nnumber` directly\n- **ESLint:** New `valid-custom-element-name` rule + auto-fix for\n`shadowDomName` → `customElementName`\n\n### 💥 Breaking Changes\n- `ShadeOptions.shadowDomName` renamed to `customElementName`\n- `DataGrid`/`DataGridHeader`/`DataGridFooter`/filters: `findOptions` is\nno longer `ObservableValue`\n- `CircularProgress`/`LinearProgress`: `value` is `number`, not\n`ObservableValue<number>`\n- ESLint rule `valid-shadow-dom-name` removed, replaced by\n`valid-custom-element-name`","tree":{"sha":"77decce766ea52728f6b691417853143ecb9622e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/git/trees/77decce766ea52728f6b691417853143ecb9622e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/git/commits/cbaa9e191c81f269bba552713173478ba0441e9c","verification":{"payload":"tree 77decce766ea52728f6b691417853143ecb9622e\nparent 25971f20d86d73c7c592f96e5225b127b65c7029\nauthor Lajos <gallayl@users.noreply.github.com> 1772893504 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772893504 +0100\n\nfeat(Shades): Shades cleanups and rewamps (#620)\n\n## 🔧 Shades API cleanups and terminology correction\n\nRenames `shadowDomName` to `customElementName` throughout the Shades\nframework to correctly reflect that Shades uses Custom Elements, not\nShadow DOM. Also refactors DataGrid and progress components to use a\ncontrolled-component pattern (plain values + callbacks) instead of\n`ObservableValue` props, simplifying the consumer API.\n\n### ✨ Highlights\n- **Terminology fix:** `shadowDomName` → `customElementName` in\n`ShadeOptions` and all components\n- **DataGrid:** `findOptions` is now a plain value prop with\n`onFindOptionsChange` callback\n- **Progress:** `CircularProgress` and `LinearProgress` accept `value:\nnumber` directly\n- **ESLint:** New `valid-custom-element-name` rule + auto-fix for\n`shadowDomName` → `customElementName`\n\n### 💥 Breaking Changes\n- `ShadeOptions.shadowDomName` renamed to `customElementName`\n- `DataGrid`/`DataGridHeader`/`DataGridFooter`/filters: `findOptions` is\nno longer `ObservableValue`\n- `CircularProgress`/`LinearProgress`: `value` is `number`, not\n`ObservableValue<number>`\n- ESLint rule `valid-shadow-dom-name` removed, replaced by\n`valid-custom-element-name`","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJprDVACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMCIQAADyo7ieGq4B+8MaX7gt7HHZ\nj1tG5Cwiw7wLJtORVwGyd3P8mWhshnh/nPI06pAnKGOpzR3O1IiV3tAD7OFFM8Dj\nyR9aOV0LLzYRXVtJseQMyhRzmSSae69V7zB+SLenSUe3i635ZpQrT2DgCoNVvUl6\nWeX6tTHfnsdiSrRXMQFnWYOH3YSyxiBSob6bXKJ9T962yuU9vQaG5NQi92Ys8BDa\nVFmr/FDCkVbCOQvyzUHcjprS6Mw37+o3qqEapvZVm1yvWO+DiW29Yl1Q68XqOMbW\nr9l+2HnJSeozmIBy8zomgqt4ImgZy0WmJ7/xB7Qw6pqLPUWVugJvRA6zADtfBX/H\nXk0lPmM/nw94hhf615/B5nENK8cVPmUWCpmC8Xn2lFDxOK3Al/M2/fkFQy3xvxpT\nONOidiLUmZVhpRTzKTR0J+FbkRX/rK+kbHya7c6N1SF9jMbiCUUVYX9tRr8ZMdjK\n0MWNXVyDuWrfSGHPzOur+5gJzjpkvPX7it5GwsIVxkJcWbsh0q/Ip3Vtu2SLP0OQ\n9Np7a45bK4soVmY114kWhLJAMFJbNz0VmtDyDtcfBPKwQmQU0aioYW7BxUZtA5aQ\nZMKwp9zXIdQ3Y5eEjl5N4CBWk189z42E76OZR69B3KJ2gMRE/+Gj60kR+EPCx7Av\nM0ro9mrjUZkWibDNBkML\n=cmDj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-07T14:25:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/furystack/furystack/commit/cbaa9e191c81f269bba552713173478ba0441e9c","node_id":"C_kwDOCYZLQNoAKGNiYWE5ZTE5MWM4MWYyNjliYmE1NTI3MTMxNzM0NzhiYTA0NDFlOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/furystack/furystack/commit/25971f20d86d73c7c592f96e5225b127b65c7029","sha":"25971f20d86d73c7c592f96e5225b127b65c7029","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/commits/25971f20d86d73c7c592f96e5225b127b65c7029"}],"sha":"cbaa9e191c81f269bba552713173478ba0441e9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/commits/cbaa9e191c81f269bba552713173478ba0441e9c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16716099?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gallayl","id":16716099,"login":"gallayl","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzE2MDk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gallayl","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/commits/25971f20d86d73c7c592f96e5225b127b65c7029/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-07T13:16:59Z","email":"gallayl@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Lajos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-07T13:16:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/openapi support (#619)\n\n## 🔄 Bidirectional OpenAPI 3.1 Support\n\nAdds full OpenAPI 3.1 support to `@furystack/rest` and\n`@furystack/rest-service`, enabling both **consuming** external OpenAPI\ndocuments and **producing** rich OpenAPI output from FuryStack APIs.\n\n### ✨ New Features\n\n- **Type-level**: `OpenApiToRestApi<T>` extracts a strongly-typed\n`RestApi` from an `as const` OpenAPI document, with support for `$ref`,\n`allOf`/`oneOf`/`anyOf`, nullable types, `const`, enums, path/query/body\nextraction, and metadata\n- **Runtime**: `openApiToSchema()` and `resolveOpenApiRefs()` convert\nOpenAPI documents to FuryStack''s `ApiEndpointSchema` for use with the\nruntime pipeline\n- **Generation**: `generateOpenApiDocument()` now produces request\nbodies, query/header parameters, operation metadata (tags, deprecated,\nsummary, description), document metadata (servers, contact, license,\nsecurity schemes), and proper security per-operation\n- **Auth mapping**: `mapProvidersToSecuritySchemes()` auto-detects\nconfigured FuryStack authentication providers and maps them to OpenAPI\nsecurity schemes\n\n### 🔧 Refactors\n\n- Renamed all \"Swagger\" references to \"OpenAPI\" with backward-compatible\ndeprecated re-exports\n- `/swagger.json` still served with `Deprecation` header, redirecting to\n`/openapi.json`\n\n### 🧪 Tests\n\n- 170+ new tests covering type-level extraction, runtime conversion,\nround-trip fidelity, and $ref resolution\n- Three JSON fixtures (example, CRUD, advanced) exercising progressively\nmore OpenAPI features","tree":{"sha":"e2519a372d7d3df7810f29f68ade70aefb52cd1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/git/trees/e2519a372d7d3df7810f29f68ade70aefb52cd1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/furystack/furystack/git/commits/25971f20d86d73c7c592f96e5225b127b65c7029","verification":{"payload":"tree e2519a372d7d3df7810f29f68ade70aefb52cd1a\nparent 46f006280315328f443088fb288dba44013a1d9c\nauthor Lajos <gallayl@users.noreply.github.com> 1772889419 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772889419 +0000\n\nFeat/openapi support (#619)\n\n## 🔄 Bidirectional OpenAPI 3.1 Support\n\nAdds full OpenAPI 3.1 support to `@furystack/rest` and\n`@furystack/rest-service`, enabling both **consuming** external OpenAPI\ndocuments and **producing** rich OpenAPI output from FuryStack APIs.\n\n### ✨ New Features\n\n- **Type-level**: `OpenApiToRestApi<T>` extracts a strongly-typed\n`RestApi` from an `as const` OpenAPI document, with support for `$ref`,\n`allOf`/`oneOf`/`anyOf`, nullable types, `const`, enums, path/query/body\nextraction, and metadata\n- **Runtime**: `openApiToSchema()` and `resolveOpenApiRefs()` convert\nOpenAPI documents to FuryStack''s `ApiEndpointSchema` for use with the\nruntime pipeline\n- **Generation**: `generateOpenApiDocument()` now produces request\nbodies, query/header parameters, operation metadata (tags, deprecated,\nsummary, description), document metadata (servers, contact, license,\nsecurity schemes), and proper security per-operation\n- **Auth mapping**: `mapProvidersToSecuritySchemes()` auto-detects\nconfigured FuryStack authentication providers and maps them to OpenAPI\nsecurity schemes\n\n### 🔧 Refactors\n\n- Renamed all \"Swagger\" references to \"OpenAPI\" with backward-compatible\ndeprecated re-exports\n- `/swagger.json` still served with `Deprecation` header, redirecting to\n`/openapi.json`\n\n### 🧪 Tests\n\n- 170+ new tests covering type-level extraction, runtime conversion,\nround-trip fidelity, and $ref resolution\n- Three JSON fixtures (example, CRUD, advanced) exercising progressively\nmore OpenAPI features","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJprCVLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUYAQAC4Rsun1SQrQvpfgd5H07aJb\nwCh0tIqU7UKwJxase+huX2eyOA0cmnXWU2l7p8bEwYsxCw+LpZzjCnd0yZQM6ocj\nuzhosD2R8ZpB5YZa9D46rQn87TeUntvchfk1mLz5IruGk9mjBA1u1PSZsolfQx7W\nAxhePCWgMbRPldGkzaPgXdJI+/4YJNHZObLj825xw5lFUTyFWAa+2odX/Ly6s8UZ\nspV0tHDRg8MxQ5KMKA5PupYYcFYkUogTSGEpz7oekHsvOAqYKjwVuNFwepD0n4z8\ntB8E7JaQljNEJt/pVVZf3XJGMNPrWVB6WQytoPRBObcB4gW3pJC39dgC7mkV8LMB\nkRb9cMcUxd0ZjHyV4oRigfZzqRVV0YGjwqsTVRCB+4rU97HY0pjdSpMLdxlKZgFI\n+62DMULNxeJmVBy7AdBD86MKCK2IdHL+YS8SfiBXxdYSqfE5n4GIIb2oM82baHgX\nS+rEZfTXEQY6cIlBu0HFAG1Y5bOKYwwWLzFATnrvakuqnosrDnLZmUM+Kg4hVuEm\nvlLvK6C8aDlatpoy1m7NDsnAii28+qegjcSCc7D7vZWo+joRxSv0ujtSd7aYqPdy\nsh/VEG7IIGASfWpzWdPEr3b97bXgJzSO4gxndyNny96XcO0vGOnyl8SdnocnBqRD\nwBRnN1ODz0687x2VbFJ9\n=+041\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-07T13:16:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events"