l":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/commit/55b47630b4845f159a8377593721cd03b1bde227","node_id":"C_kwDOCc39_NoAKDU1YjQ3NjMwYjQ4NDVmMTU5YTgzNzc1OTM3MjFjZDAzYjFiZGUyMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/commit/b37861d2aff294577762e5e47c00f1f9fb0eacb3","sha":"b37861d2aff294577762e5e47c00f1f9fb0eacb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/commits/b37861d2aff294577762e5e47c00f1f9fb0eacb3"}],"sha":"55b47630b4845f159a8377593721cd03b1bde227","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/commits/55b47630b4845f159a8377593721cd03b1bde227"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11976694?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Apollon77","id":11976694,"login":"Apollon77","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTc2Njk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/commits/b37861d2aff294577762e5e47c00f1f9fb0eacb3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T19:39:39Z","email":"github@fischer-ka.de","name":"Ingo Fischer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T19:39:39Z","email":"github@fischer-ka.de","name":"Ingo Fischer"},"message":"fix: drop a deferred home read a push has already answered\n\nA SECURITY_JOURNAL_CHANGED or HOME_CHANGED event that carries the home\npublishes the alarm fields itself, so a read deferred by an earlier event\nhas nothing left to fetch - but its timer stayed armed and pulled the whole\nconfiguration once the interval was over.\n\nOnly a push drops it, and only one that carries SECURITY_AND_ALARM. The\nread publishes the same fields from a response the cloud composed before\nthe deferred event arrived, so it cannot answer that event, and a home\nwithout the alarm section answers nothing at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ea76d75953f145aec67bb7ebd3bb7837b7177620","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/git/trees/ea76d75953f145aec67bb7ebd3bb7837b7177620"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/git/commits/b37861d2aff294577762e5e47c00f1f9fb0eacb3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11976694?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Apollon77","id":11976694,"login":"Apollon77","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTc2Njk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/commit/b37861d2aff294577762e5e47c00f1f9fb0eacb3","node_id":"C_kwDOCc39_NoAKGIzNzg2MWQyYWZmMjk0NTc3NzYyZTVlNDdjMDBmMWY5ZmIwZWFjYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/commit/e6cee8981cd70005b60b617bde827a782ee48f41","sha":"e6cee8981cd70005b60b617bde827a782ee48f41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/commits/e6cee8981cd70005b60b617bde827a782ee48f41"}],"sha":"b37861d2aff294577762e5e47c00f1f9fb0eacb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/commits/b37861d2aff294577762e5e47c00f1f9fb0eacb3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11976694?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Apollon77","id":11976694,"login":"Apollon77","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTc2Njk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/commits/e6cee8981cd70005b60b617bde827a782ee48f41/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T17:43:16Z","email":"github@fischer-ka.de","name":"Ingo Fischer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T17:43:16Z","email":"github@fischer-ka.de","name":"Ingo Fischer"},"message":"feat: report and set the armed state of the alarm system on the home\n\nThe armed state was readable only as the \"active\" flag of a security zone\ngroup, whose id is opaque and whose label differs between panel generations:\nINTERNAL/EXTERNAL on the classic dashboard, ABSENCE/PRESENCE on the\nrequest-based one. A script could not find it without knowing which\ndashboard the home has.\n\nThe home now carries securityZonesArmedMode plus internalZoneArmed and\nexternalZoneArmed, mapped onto the classic pair the way the write path\nalready maps it, and refreshed from the zone group events a panel sends\nwhen it arms. A home carrying both zone families reads the armed zones of\neither, rather than reporting a disarmed home because the family it looked\nat is not the one in use.\n\nactivateSecurityZones arms by mode name. Its mode list is deliberately\nindependent of the panel a home has today: extendObject merges, so a list\nnarrowed for one dashboard could never drop the other''s keys again.\n\nReading the home stays throttled rather than removed. Only a full\ngetCurrentState carries the home''s alarm fields, and the security journal\nevent that announces them arrives every few minutes on some homes, so the\nread happens at most once every five minutes; an event inside that window\ndefers to the end of it, and a read that answered nothing reserves 30\nseconds so the fields are not silenced for the full interval. The response\nnow also refreshes the cached configuration, because the states published\nfrom it are derived from that cache.\n\nRefs #1038\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ea5bd70d2a283572528528e2c4241f31fd9643fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/git/trees/ea5bd70d2a283572528528e2c4241f31fd9643fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/git/commits/e6cee8981cd70005b60b617bde827a782ee48f41","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11976694?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Apollon77","id":11976694,"login":"Apollon77","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTc2Njk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/commit/e6cee8981cd70005b60b617bde827a782ee48f41","node_id":"C_kwDOCc39_NoAKGU2Y2VlODk4MWNkNzAwMDViNjBiNjE3YmRlODI3YTc4MmVlNDhmNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/commit/104bdaca5ae5eeb558d8296285be4c7b2e7136ff","sha":"104bdaca5ae5eeb558d8296285be4c7b2e7136ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/commits/104bdaca5ae5eeb558d8296285be4c7b2e7136ff"}],"sha":"e6cee8981cd70005b60b617bde827a782ee48f41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/commits/e6cee8981cd70005b60b617bde827a782ee48f41"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcm1957","id":28575778,"login":"mcm1957","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTc1Nzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcm1957","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/commits/104bdaca5ae5eeb558d8296285be4c7b2e7136ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T19:22:31Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T19:22:31Z","email":"mcm57@gmx.at","name":"Martin M."},"message":"chore: release v3.0.0\n\n- (@Apollon77) **Breaking:** shutterLevel, slatsLevel, dimLevel, primaryShadingLevel, secondaryShadingLevel and minimumFloorHeatingValvePosition now report 0..100 on the channels that declare that range, matching the ioBroker convention and the range the datapoint has always advertised. They previously advertised 0..100 but reported the cloud''s 0..1 fraction. Writing is unchanged: a value above 1 is read as a percentage, anything else as a fraction\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed arming/disarming the alarm system on the new request-based security dashboard (ABSENCE/PRESENCE security zones)\n- (@Apollon77) On the request-based security dashboard a blocked alarm activation is now logged with the devices that prevented it, instead of looking like it succeeded\n- (@Apollon77) On the request-based security dashboard a low battery no longer blocks arming; the affected devices are logged as a warning instead\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed removed groups and clients being deleted from the wrong internal cache\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed particulateNumberConcentrationTen never being filled on the HmIP-SFD, a mistyped state name wrote it to a nonexistent datapoint\n- (@Apollon77) Added support for 45 further device channel types with 343 new states, covering the door lock pro, the keypads, the wired Wiegand interface, the watering actuator, the water supply stop, the soil moisture sensor, the universal actuator and dimmer, the wall switch status LEDs, the glass displays and thermostats, and devices bridged through the HCU including their weather, energy and battery readings\n- (@Apollon77) Every device now reports its own hardware faults: overheated, overloaded, undervoltage, temperature out of range and the three co-processor states\n- (@Apollon77) 3 channel types that carry no value of their own are no longer reported as unknown\n- (@Apollon77) All device channel handling now comes from one table instead of 122 hand-written methods, with no change to any object or value\n- (@Apollon77) The newly supported channels can now be controlled, not only read: the wall switch status LEDs, the display backlight, the universal dimmer and actuator, the door lock pro, the door opener, the watering actuator, bridged switches and lights, and bridged window coverings\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed hue, saturationLevel and colorTemperature on universal lights, which were writable but dispatched to a command that did not exist (HmIP-RGBW)\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed inAppWaterAlarmTrigger, which was writable but never sent to the cloud\n- (@Apollon77) 18 states that were writable with no command behind them are now read-only, and changeOverDelay no longer throws when written\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed the stop and resetEnergyCounter buttons being labelled \"on\" in the admin UI\n- (@Apollon77) Added the remaining commands the HomematicIP cloud offers, 88 endpoints in total, and exposed the ones with a datapoint to attach to\n- (@Apollon77) Switching groups can now be switched, and their shutter and slats levels set - the group on/off datapoint never reached the cloud before\n- (@Apollon77) New controls: motion detection on and off, pull latch, watering toggle and water volume reset, passage counter reset, favourite shading position, MP3 sound file and volume, light scenes, whole-home cooling and the alarm zone activation delay\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed the misspelled setNotificationSoundTyp endpoint, which meant the notification sound was never set\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed motionBufferActive, endpositionAutoDetectionEnabled, dim2WarmActive and humanCentricLightActive, which switched the device on or off instead of doing what their name says\n- (@Apollon77) Dimming, colour, optical signals and watering can now be given a time: set controlOnTime and/or controlRampTime on the channel and the command ramps instead of jumping. Both default to 0, which keeps the previous behaviour\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed the dim level never being scaled for RGB and optical signal commands, where a state object was compared against a number\n- (@Apollon77) Corrected the role of 54 writable datapoints, which carried a read-only role and so were not recognised by the ioBroker type detector - dimmers, blinds, switches and timers are now typed as such\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed the dim level being sent unscaled by the light scene, hue/saturation and colour temperature commands, so a percentage reached a cloud endpoint that expects a fraction\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed a valve with no reported position being published as 0 percent, and one that reports nothing at all as NaN\n- (@Apollon77) A level command with a control time is no longer suppressed when the level is unchanged, so \"switch on for 30 seconds\" works at the level the device already has\n- (@Apollon77) Silent alarm can now be set per zone, and each security zone reports its silent, window, motion, presence and sabotage state\n- (@Apollon77) Heating profile mode can now be set on hot water and shutter profile groups, and those two group types are now supported\n- (@Apollon77) Extended linked switching and notification groups are now supported, including their on time\n- (@Apollon77) The home now reports its power meter currency, and its unit price can be set\n- (@Apollon77) The security journal is now available (issue #31): the full list as JSON plus the newest entry split into its own datapoints, refreshed when the cloud announces a change and on demand\n- (@Apollon77) Automation rules are now visible under `rules.<id>` and simple rules can be enabled, disabled and relabelled - the rule metadata the cloud sends was previously discarded\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed vacation mode never working: the temperature was read off a promise instead of the state, the end time was sent under the wrong name, and the temperature datapoint could not be set at all\n- (@Apollon77) A websocket the cloud drops silently is now noticed and reconnected, instead of leaving the adapter connected but permanently silent\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed the websocket auto-reconnect being disabled for good after the first internal reconnect\n- (@Apollon77) A home the cloud sends without functional homes no longer crashes the adapter\n- (@Apollon77) Debounced writes no longer outlive the adapter being stopped\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed datapoints that an earlier version published as writable still sending their old command after an upgrade, even though they are now read-only - writing a diagnostic datapoint could switch the device\n- (@Apollon77) Corrected the role of 25 read-only datapoints that carried a controllable role, and made 2 datapoints readable that were published as neither readable nor writable\n- (@Apollon77) A command meant for the channel''s groups now reports that the channel belongs to none, instead of failing silently\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed locking a door failing when no authorization PIN had been set\n- (@Apollon77) On the request-based security dashboard an activation the panel accepts without reporting any detail is now logged as unconfirmed, instead of being reported as armed and possibly carrying a low-battery warning that implied it armed\n- (@Apollon77) **Breaking:** valvePosition on a heating thermostat now reports 0..100 with a unit, like the floor terminal block already did - the cloud sends a 0..1 fraction for both and only one of them was scaled. The internal switch channel now reports its valvePosition too\n- (@Apollon77) Rain counters now report the millimetres the sensor measured instead of the cloud''s accumulated floating point drift, so 0.3 mm no longer arrives as 0.3000000000001819, and all nine of them carry the mm unit\n- (@Apollon77) Fixed the device that raised an alarm never being reported: the cloud names it only inside alarmEventDeviceChannel, so alarmEventDeviceId was always empty and the channel datapoint was fed an object it could not hold. Both are filled now, and the device''s label is published beside them","tree":{"sha":"45acda3f692d7d6bacd3bed8ada0a99cdf3469ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/git/trees/45acda3f692d7d6bacd3bed8ada0a99cdf3469ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.hmip/git/commits/104bdaca5ae5eeb558d8296285be4c7b2e7136ff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28575778?v=4"