s://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/c284987aadf08b4c065ba892b753c16620d22bd3","sha":"c284987aadf08b4c065ba892b753c16620d22bd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/c284987aadf08b4c065ba892b753c16620d22bd3"}],"sha":"e0b0e864cf456cfbd3e7b7927279b43eeb836c4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/e0b0e864cf456cfbd3e7b7927279b43eeb836c4d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29783151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/c284987aadf08b4c065ba892b753c16620d22bd3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T04:18:43Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T04:18:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(fhir): updating an existing resource through the facade saves only what changed (#4648)\n\n* fix(fhir): updating an existing resource through the facade saves only what changed\n\nPUT of a resource read from the facade failed or corrupted data:\n\n- Patient: 500 when the patient had no emergency contact; otherwise the\n  update copied the patient''s own name and phone over the emergency\n  contact, turned the published \"commune: X\" address line into the street\n  address (growing on every PUT), and erased GPS coordinates and every\n  identity a FHIR Patient cannot carry (occupation, AKA, mother''s name,\n  notes, programme...). Create recorded the patient as its own emergency\n  contact and dropped state, postal code and country.\n- ServiceRequest: 400 with no diagnostics on any update that kept the\n  test (no sample XML), and on any order whose accession predates the\n  current format. Once past that, the order details were rebuilt from the\n  resource alone, blanking program, payment status and next visit date and\n  resetting the request date to today (authoredOn was the time of the\n  read). A code change silently added a second specimen and analyses;\n  it is now refused with 422, as are an unknown code, requester or a\n  location that is not a referring site.\n- Specimen: 500 on the published accession identifier (ACC-n). With the\n  bare accession, the sort order became the sample id, notes doubled the\n  collection conditions, rejected items became entered, cancelled items\n  became rejected, and times lost their fraction of a second.\n- Observation: an unchanged PUT recorded a result modification; text on\n  a numeric test was stored and made the Observation unreadable; a\n  validation failure answered 500.\n\nUnchanged round trips are now no-ops; edits change only their own\ncolumns. Blank telecom values are no longer published, and the Specimen\ncollector is.\n\n* fix(fhir): text-only ServiceRequest codes and padded person columns round-trip\n\nA test with no LOINC code or terminology mapping is published by name only,\nand the update refused that same code. An update now accepts a code equal to\nwhat the read publishes for the analysis and keeps its test.\n\nAn unchanged Patient update still rewrote the padded postal code, blank\nstrings and, because the primary phone is published as the mobile phone,\nreplaced a stored cell phone with it. Stored contact and address values the\nupdate sends back unchanged are now kept, so the update writes nothing.","tree":{"sha":"ba0a0507997382e5312d88eacb7d5e572d3c0370","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/ba0a0507997382e5312d88eacb7d5e572d3c0370"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/c284987aadf08b4c065ba892b753c16620d22bd3","verification":{"payload":"tree ba0a0507997382e5312d88eacb7d5e572d3c0370\nparent 76c6d625ad4ede8ddb627246c3a4927f038a29e6\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1791433123 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791433123 +0300\n\nfix(fhir): updating an existing resource through the facade saves only what changed (#4648)\n\n* fix(fhir): updating an existing resource through the facade saves only what changed\n\nPUT of a resource read from the facade failed or corrupted data:\n\n- Patient: 500 when the patient had no emergency contact; otherwise the\n  update copied the patient''s own name and phone over the emergency\n  contact, turned the published \"commune: X\" address line into the street\n  address (growing on every PUT), and erased GPS coordinates and every\n  identity a FHIR Patient cannot carry (occupation, AKA, mother''s name,\n  notes, programme...). Create recorded the patient as its own emergency\n  contact and dropped state, postal code and country.\n- ServiceRequest: 400 with no diagnostics on any update that kept the\n  test (no sample XML), and on any order whose accession predates the\n  current format. Once past that, the order details were rebuilt from the\n  resource alone, blanking program, payment status and next visit date and\n  resetting the request date to today (authoredOn was the time of the\n  read). A code change silently added a second specimen and analyses;\n  it is now refused with 422, as are an unknown code, requester or a\n  location that is not a referring site.\n- Specimen: 500 on the published accession identifier (ACC-n). With the\n  bare accession, the sort order became the sample id, notes doubled the\n  collection conditions, rejected items became entered, cancelled items\n  became rejected, and times lost their fraction of a second.\n- Observation: an unchanged PUT recorded a result modification; text on\n  a numeric test was stored and made the Observation unreadable; a\n  validation failure answered 500.\n\nUnchanged round trips are now no-ops; edits change only their own\ncolumns. Blank telecom values are no longer published, and the Specimen\ncollector is.\n\n* fix(fhir): text-only ServiceRequest codes and padded person columns round-trip\n\nA test with no LOINC code or terminology mapping is published by name only,\nand the update refused that same code. An update now accepts a code equal to\nwhat the read publishes for the analysis and keeps its test.\n\nAn unchanged Patient update still rewrote the padded postal code, blank\nstrings and, because the primary phone is published as the mobile phone,\nreplaced a stored cell phone with it. Stored contact and address values the\nupdate sends back unchanged are now kept, so the update writes nothing.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxxmjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwIUQAJjjY4ovAK+GLXl+FEMliKaL\nS/iO3N3q97El1TZZUHrhWcYaMXLJS/mEFafO/pI4y7iIeFdij3RKVGIJJJYe3MnE\nl5vLQRF9DmhTJJTuYkUPAhf6Hrw43Q7pQAMknUitVsfxQWpAzE3X5R13b3rviSHm\nHKZfXGJxFQ8t5KQNacRQ3G4BQ7No2WwFVZeE0dCp8GjqLW7tmGKL1AVSx8NINLld\n858b/aSPI+HjGCZOdkAXNqfVdO3NKcDQ6pSMtmb9CBhNJIuuiE0JLkf7xBi2QkKX\nB5GwQ0KPVyDovWeZXSn3WMZfTfMSx7CIeACP9LUCKuyGNgSfkakh7PL7Ko2JjiBY\nK2F7CMIwzf4MHJcdFc3r8OpLCSZmzkLNDNdarHz2MRPJLLnpNSmwCPnfpG4ewZwG\n6KoS5faZ1+ETSXc9IA9P2uv/ZLT7drSUsLCP7o3F8OstGlFKqB+EGL18ZUE9qdYh\n5wEYT3d8dYe3s7f5zLBJVcWblFD0Xj013rIPg35R6JW58z2D/p2Lc1RMx2KLv369\nmdan+sj8ck6BJjJnqKTNBF18kziBXX9BCicQOYnoVDjo68nXO/VnfpgBgLdK+zJo\nGJGa2Oys3ZHU