+mozzy11@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxuloCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAez4QAFmOKj6BuWrdytDNl7G9sioY\ntSmHytKXtRCHXy28Hg24WCy7rz67OVjweGxz0qhLUsBNwDM+njifG/T/o9liCXMb\nkAyHda3jZk1UFKY9A9zRzW84VfLXL2URHNP5rQ3NcdwIcldElP7cToVo1kPgzvgl\nO38d5eNRvwtI0bTdHad6fR/y2ymELyMdgwJaZSUuZUfsd8ACpDxRapmfwO82ECLu\nKMW5sFp/9UfRYDZJ371Bqm3djPWvLs4EBwsQ3nDhbKeT5bysKo3C0uKWg5Wy56r1\ntAiEs1aXD2L2kt17GS/XAovxgY/ISt87UqcTyU0HZ0QOVovZDHTco3ip2HbBNQb1\nhvAe4bjMdqUBs7BGo2EF8HogrIzeyf7Nu9KF5TLsLWTRHmVVDxPTc8Nt+5BZi2Mf\nIdZnP5IPz+vPsQy5iGeORfnMFZGU51KW2cf6wHMY1g7mIM2w2Vecbu+pzbcuqbF/\nUldzjnnVNPA00NbulT/RG+GRMBhBTEwmxopnvm5AelnlHvsBTHwZMcvCweXuh8xH\n+uoB7wrYf8RZ/6vEKNm2vAOcdlVwtGHOquLUawbAnovIN7TeF8HaokvwFtaMifId\npFNhS5242+9ZC4tF6+SX0Xk5MNxVywI2UQUOlRU1xH8wfqFSVHZHOc2ctCE2coJ+\n8x6oIaZnYKda3ictBAgK\n=xrvV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T00:52:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/76c6d625ad4ede8ddb627246c3a4927f038a29e6","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDc2YzZkNjI1YWQ0ZWRlOGRkYjYyNzI0NmMzYTQ5MjdmMDM4YTI5ZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/53a8f78d686bd88f7bde01eb4b7a62cba18b755e","sha":"53a8f78d686bd88f7bde01eb4b7a62cba18b755e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/53a8f78d686bd88f7bde01eb4b7a62cba18b755e"}],"sha":"76c6d625ad4ede8ddb627246c3a4927f038a29e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/76c6d625ad4ede8ddb627246c3a4927f038a29e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/150329678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isabirye1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isabirye1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isabirye1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isabirye1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Isabirye1515","id":150329678,"login":"Isabirye1515","node_id":"U_kgDOCPXZTg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isabirye1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isabirye1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isabirye1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isabirye1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isabirye1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Isabirye1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/53a8f78d686bd88f7bde01eb4b7a62cba18b755e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:08:58Z","email":"150329678+Isabirye1515@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Elijah"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:08:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(fhir): reject search parameters the facade cannot honour; patient address and telecom search (#4236)\n\n* Added the telecome email and phone params to patient search\n\n* Reverse adding address parameters to Practitioner search\n\n* revert Add city, state, postalCode, and country fields\n\n* Afew minor fixes\n\n* added tests\n\n* fix(fhir): reject search parameters the facade cannot honour\n\nA search with a parameter the facade could not apply used to return every\nresource of the type with HTTP 200, indistinguishable from a real match:\nan unknown underscore parameter (_foo, _has, _text), _sort (no DAO applies\nit), the :missing modifier, a chained parameter, a token with a system and\nno code (identifier=sys|), and on telecom/phone/email a system the\nparameter cannot hold (phone=email|x, telecom=sms|x).\n\nStrictSearchParameterInterceptor, registered on the FHIR server beside\nHAPI''s SearchPreferHandlingInterceptor, checks each type search against\nwhat the provider''s @Search method declares and answers 400 with an\nOperationOutcome naming the parameter. HAPI''s interceptor only checks plain\nnames, skips underscore names and never reads values, hence both. Empty\nvalues are still ignored, as the FHIR rules require, and a client can send\nPrefer: handling=lenient for the old behaviour.\n\nContact points: a system the parameter cannot hold matches nothing, and\nsystem|  (no value) matches people holding that kind of contact. The name\nand contact-point helpers move from FacadeHelperDao into BaseFhirDao,\nwhich both Patient and Practitioner DAOs extend; the separate bean is gone.\n\nPatients, sample items, analyses and results without fhir_uuid are left\nout of searches and totals: their transforms have no id fallback, and one\nsuch row made HAPI fail every page that reached it (HAPI-0435).\n\n* fix(fhir): validate search values and malformed ids, page Location by offset\n\nSearch values the facade cannot honour now answer 400 with an\nOperationOutcome instead of an empty or complete bundle:\n- a code outside the required FHIR value set of gender, every status\n  parameter and Organization.active (codes read from HAPI''s R4 enums);\n- a reference to a type that is not a FHIR resource or that the parameter\n  cannot point at (targets from HAPI''s RuntimeSearchParam), or one that\n  names no id: subject=Patient/ used to match every resource;\n- a malformed token (a|b|c) and a negative _count.\n\nLenient handling moves into the interceptor, before the method is\nselected, and drops what cannot be applied. HAPI''s\nSearchPreferHandlingInterceptor is no longer registered: it removes a\nmodified parameter (gender:missing) by its bare name, so lenient\nrequests carrying one still failed.\n\nRead, update and delete with a malformed id answer 400 on Patient,\nPractitioner, Organization, ServiceRequest and Observation instead of\n500, and updating an unknown Practitioner answers 404.\n\nLocation?_offset without _count answered 500 (offset with no page size);\nit now pages with the default size like every other resource, and a\nnegative _offset is a 400.\n\n* style(fhir): format the missing-uuid patient fixture\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: mozzy11 <mozzy@uwdigi.org>","tree":{"sha":"f1507981210e454c4e0fa8960548395f6efa0240","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/f1507981210e454c4e0fa8960548395f6efa0240"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/53a8f78d686bd88f7bde01eb4b7a62cba18b755e","verification":{"payload":"tree f1507981210e454c4e0fa8960548395f6efa0240\nparent e74beea0c9ba82a61dcfa4022ec64a13f929f5be\nauthor Elijah <150329678+Isabirye1515@users.noreply.github.com> 1791360538 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791360538 +0300\n\nfix(fhir): reject search parameters the facade cannot honour; patient address and telecom search (#4236)\n\n* Added the telecome email and phone params to patient search\n\n* Reverse adding address parameters to Practitioner search\n\n* revert Add city, state, postalCode, and country fields\n\n* Afew minor fixes\n\n* added tests\n\n* fix(fhir): reject search parameters the facade cannot honour\n\nA search with a parameter the facade could not apply used to return every\nresource of the type with HTTP 200, indistinguishable from a real match:\nan unknown underscore parameter (_foo, _has, _text), _sort (no DAO applies\nit), the :missing modifier, a chained parameter, a token with a system and\nno code (identifier=sys|), and on telecom/phone/email a system the\nparameter cannot hold (phone=email|x, telecom=sms|x).\n\nStrictSearchParameterInterceptor, registered on the FHIR server beside\nHAPI''s SearchPreferHandlingInterceptor, checks each type search against\nwhat the provider''s @Search method declares and answers 400 with an\nOperationOutcome naming the parameter. HAPI''s interceptor only checks plain\nnames, skips underscore names and never reads values, hence both. Empty\nvalues are still ignored, as the FHIR rules require, and a client can send\nPrefer: handling=lenient for the old behaviour.\n\nContact points: a system the parameter cannot hold matches nothing, and\nsystem|  (no value) matches people holding that kind of contact. The name\nand contact-point helpers move from FacadeHelperDao into BaseFhirDao,\nwhich both Patient and Practitioner DAOs extend; the separate bean is gone.\n\nPatients, sample items, analyses and results without fhir_uuid are left\nout of searches and totals: their transforms have no id fallback, and one\nsuch row made HAPI fail every page that reached it (HAPI-0435).\n\n* fix(fhir): validate search values and malformed ids, page Location by offset\n\nSearch values the facade cannot honour now answer 400 with an\nOperationOutcome instead of an empty or complete bundle:\n- a code outside the required FHIR value set of gender, every status\n  parameter and Organization.active (codes read from HAPI''s R4 enums);\n- a reference to a type that is not a FHIR resource or that the parameter\n  cannot point at (targets from HAPI''s RuntimeSearchParam), or one that\n  names no id: subject=Patient/ used to match every resource;\n- a malformed token (a|b|c) and a negative _count.\n\nLenient handling moves into the interceptor, before the method is\nselected, and drops what cannot be applied. HAPI''s\nSearchPreferHandlingInterceptor is no longer registered: it removes a\nmodified parameter (gender:missing) by its bare name, so lenient\nrequests carrying one still failed.\n\nRead, update and delete with a malformed id answer 400 on Patient,\nPractitioner, Organization, ServiceRequest and Observation instead of\n500, and updating an unknown Practitioner answers 404.\n\nLocation?_offset without _count answered 500 (offset with no page size);\nit now pages with the default size like every other resource, and a\nnegative _offset is a 400.\n\n* style(fhir): format the missing-uuid patient fixture\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: mozzy11 <mozzy@uwdigi.org>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxf4aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4gIQACz+Z6qIa8jLEBCDVkK0d32s\nDiz13vt7Jh0xMp5BE0+9Tb39jaffwDITuRXzquW/3gFiZfHC327N5mbjIwhxrqxX\ny1yThNiwy8q5Ihoz42/OCiVTwKRSFRlylhRKzLfaikNMQSiIW94OXF1MCcheqYf/\nJzQatnfkUyaSBMAp3EBZo+TpK18DGMLn0cheM3svLFJdXza5k8tcD5Z66vnk0QJT\nx4hl49x0zYjwXGt01JAey0jMLZMs9NasGNNJy9je0wOX33AnQa3IQVfoTUv0Vome\nbIR4Dkbl/8u/qgoURo/+HO20+e6Gz9kBOe+CgHDSGXzgBdElThC3xoRb1lzO12Pr\nSHjRFKrRna46m/AZUiY74h1B+TBBYJI4pKR5LfIOeHhPfgay8pu24BIG+pjyTy4U\nZx+HD1OBqgVr9EMJ5QnagXlbFC8oA6fq9q8ub59Y1jVaZzKYM54dJUqqxe749UmH\nQ6z70yokNJ3XCwMuiajGXEILlmkgsqu3X/TUnG9F/N1iZHWPoYIFQmUGyD+ue2/E\ns0CdznWlgqUQ7reyISqgDWo9qZXtZIwgZbF5fYl5EIJwXlCqFTotWunl1GCtPHwX\n9ww/NAUGdraBEUjsw8/ZemTVZvDPXU+p7xSWrbgXVwWBNiIVBHNw6MGZMd6kWQZK\nTjDZkb7EGb0msLwl4AEl\n=9iyq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T08:08:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/53a8f78d686bd88f7bde01eb4b7a62cba18b755e","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDUzYThmNzhkNjg2YmQ4OGY3YmRlMDFlYjRiN2E2MmNiYTE4Yjc1NWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/e74beea0c9ba82a61dcfa4022ec64a13f929f5be","sha":"e74beea0c9ba82a61dcfa4022ec64a13f929f5be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/e74beea0c9ba82a61dcfa4022ec64a13f929f5be"}],"sha":"53a8f78d686bd88f7bde01eb4b7a62cba18b755e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/53a8f78d686bd88f7bde01eb4b7a62cba18b755e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19221635?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WodPachua","id":19221635,"login":"WodPachua","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjIxNjM1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/e74beea0c9ba82a61dcfa4022ec64a13f929f5be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T06:18:07Z","email":"molarag21996@gmail.com","name":"OLARA Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T06:18:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(pathology): case view opens on the shared case-view shell (OGC-264) (#4392)\n\n* feat(pathology): case view DTO gains the FR-1 specimen facts (OGC-264)\n\nSlice S3 of the case view rebuild needs what its Case Information section\nshows, and nothing more.\n\nPathologyCaseViewDisplayItem gains receivedDate (sample.received_date, the\nspecimen arrival date, distinct from the request date) and specimenTypes (one\nlocalized type-of-sample name per sample item). The requester was built as\nlastName + \" \" + firstName with no null check, so an order without a requester\nrendered the literal \"null null\"; it is null now.\n\nBoth dates (requestDate, receivedDate) are LocalDate values computed in the\nserver''s zone: the JSON layer formats a Date in UTC, so a specimen received at\nlocal midnight in Nairobi printed the day before. Same yyyy-MM-dd string on\nthe wire.\n\nhasOpenRequests leaves both DTOs. The dashboard read nothing from it and it\ncost one lazy SELECT per row on the unpaginated list; the case view needs the\nrequest names, which only the request rows carry, so the rows are the contract.\n\nTests: PathologyCaseViewDisplayTest (5) seeds its sample items in setup rather\nthan through the DBUnit fixture, because a fixture that names type_of_sample\ntruncates localization for the rest of the fork, and pins the JVM zone east of\nGreenwich so a UTC runner cannot pass the old code. PathologyCaseViewOpenRequestsTest\nserializes both DTOs and asserts the flag is off the wire and the request\nstatuses are on it.\n\n* fix(pathology): stage switch help text matches the case view (OGC-264)\n\nThe seven pathology.stage.<STAGE>.enabled switches promised that a disabled\nstage \"is skipped and shown as not applicable\". Nothing skips a stage\nautomatically: a maintainer switched Microtomy off on a deployed build and the\ncase view still offered it and stored a case at it.\n\nThe message bundle text and, through changeset 037, the seven site_information\ndescriptions that 036 wrote now describe what ships: the case view marks the\nstage not applicable on its rail, locks the section as not tracked at this\nlaboratory, and stops offering it in the stage selector. 036 is untouched\nbecause it has run on deployments.\n\n037 is tested by running it: a database-upgrades boundary fixture stops the\nchangelog just before 037, switches Coverslipping off as an administrator\nwould, runs the rest, and asserts the seven descriptions changed and the seven\nvalues did not. PathologyStageEnablementFlagsTest re-seeds the corrected\nwording so it stays order-independent.\n\n* feat(pathology): case view opens on the shared case-view shell (OGC-264)\n\nSlice S3 of Pathology Case View v2: the flat form becomes the shell #4321\nadded.\n\nScreen (PathologyCaseView.jsx, 1,317 to 715 lines):\n- eleven CaseSections in bench order; state from deriveCaseSections over\n  caseInfo.status, the Pathologist role and the stage switches; nothing is\n  hidden by status or role\n- the accordion mounts only once the case has arrived, because CaseSection\n  seeds its open state at mount\n- one updateCase funnel marks the form dirty; loading and reloading clear it;\n  the multiselects are keyed on a load counter so Discard resets them\n- Save draft re-reads the case, so a release shows the stage the server moved\n  it to\n- the stage selector sits in the action bar''s status slot, omits stages the\n  laboratory switched off unless the case is at one, and carries a hint that\n  transitions come later. It is a Carbon Dropdown opening upward, because the\n  bar is at the foot of a long page where a native select''s menu was clipped\n  against the window.\n\nSections (sections/*.jsx): Case Information (FR-1 rows, not-recorded hint,\nquestionnaire), Grossing (description, blocks, technician), Microtomy\n(slides), Pathologist Review (pathologist, requests), Findings\n(microscopyExam, techniques, conclusions, IHC referral, Release), Reports,\nand one placeholder body for the five stages nothing records yet.\n\nA section header badges what its rows say: Complete for grossing under\nFR-3.4 (a description that is not only whitespace, and a block), otherwise\n\"{n} blocks\" or \"{n} slides\" when rows exist, nothing when none do. The rail\nticks grossing and microtomy on the same rules and reports on a report\nexisting; the five stages OpenELIS records no work at tick on the case having\npassed them, the only fact there is. Derived from position alone, as before,\nthe screen told a pathologist a case at the reading had been decalcified,\nprocessed and embedded under bodies saying nothing is recorded there yet. The\nseven single-stage sections are titled by the stage''s own key, so the rail,\nthe header and the locked hint cannot call one stage two things.\n\nLayout: the title and patient band are nested two Sections deep, the idiom\nevery other case view here sizes its title with, inside a Stack that gives\nthe page its vertical rhythm; the sub-headings and the summary title take\ntheir level from that context. The shell''s grid draws on the page''s own\nbackground colour, because inside this application''s white theme zone a\nfield, a tile and the content area are all near the same light grey, and a\nform laid straight on the page had inputs nobody could see until one was\nfocused; every other form screen sits on a white body card for the same\nreason.\n\npathologyCaseView.scss: the sections sit in the shell''s nine of sixteen\ncolumns, so the sixteen-column Grid rows they were written as wrapped inside\nit and drew their controls over one another. Each repeating row is one\nwrapping flex line instead, with its labels shown and its buttons following\nthe fields as one group; Carbon''s file uploader renders an empty description\nparagraph above its button, which is hidden so the button lines up with its\nneighbours. Grossing leads with the macroscopic description, the work the\nbench is doing, rather than with the technician dropdown. A row''s remove\ncontrol is a ghost button carrying \"Remove Block\" in text; as an IconButton\nthe word was laid over the glyph and clipped. The chips are DismissibleTag,\nwhose dismiss label is localized, rather than the deprecated filter Tag with\nCarbon''s English default. The pickers show \"Select\" as placeholder.\n\nPatientHeader: the stage tag and the assigned-staff lines are stacked with a\ngap and the tag keeps its own width; the identifier pills are a wrapping flex\nrow with a gap, on every screen that renders the band.\n\nRelease is rendered whether or not the case can be released, disabled and\nnaming the assignment that is actually missing, rather than absent until both\nexist. Reports says it holds none rather than showing an empty list.\n\npathologySections.js: the section list, stage gating, switch reading, rail\nitems and badge kinds, pure, shared by the screen and its tests. The rail\nshows two outstanding requests and counts the rest, because three names\nwrapped onto three lines inside a Carbon step and overran the step below, and\ncarries all of them on the step''s hover title, which the box does not bound.\n\nCaseSummaryPanel renders booleans as Yes and No, where React rendered nothing\nfor either value, and a row can name what its count counted. The value of the\nshared key pathology.label.slide.number is \"Slide number\", capitalised like\nits block twin.\n\nFixed in passing: labels now point at their inputs (the TextAreas had no id\nand every block row shared one), the conclusions pager is a span rather than\nan unfocusable Link, three hardcoded strings use existing keys.\n\nThe rail sits in a titled tile like the summary, and the shell''s grid draws\non the page background so fields and tiles are visible against the content\narea. PatientHeader''s stage tag and staff lines are stacked with a gap and its\nidentifier pills gain one, on every screen that renders the band.\n\nTests: pathologySections.test.js (44), PathologyCaseView.sections.test.jsx\n(48), PathologyCaseView.test.jsx (3), CaseSummaryPanel.test.jsx (+4),\nCaseSection.test.jsx (+1), CaseViewLayout.test.jsx (+1), ProgressRail.test.jsx\n(+1), CaseActionBar.test.jsx (+2). 17 en.json keys.\n\n* test(pathology): case view end-to-end coverage on the shell (OGC-264)\n\nNine tests in pathology-case-view.spec.ts (core-app) walk a fresh case on a\ndeployed stack: the eleven sections and rail items in order, Case Information\ncollapsed with the seeded lab number and specimen type, locked sections naming\nthe stage they wait for, the stage moved by hand and the summary following it,\nDiscard reloading the saved case, Save draft persisting and the page reloading\nat the new stage, a slide row whose controls are measured not to overlap, a\nrail click scrolling to Reports, and a stage switched off on the admin page\nrendering N/A, locking its section and leaving the selector (restored in\nfinally).\n\nseed-pathology-data.ts places the order through the same REST call the Add\nOrder screen makes and reads the case id back from the dashboard search, since\nthe order save does not return it. Every id is discovered on the running\nstack: the programme whose name contains \"pathology\" (this stack calls it\nHistopathology), the first sample type whose tests include \"Histopathology\nexamination\", the first provider, and no referring site, because a site id\nthe stack does not know is what makes the save fail with a 500.\n\nWhat unit tests cannot prove and this does: the stylesheets load, the row\ncontrols are laid out side by side rather than over one another, the accordion\nids resolve for the rail, the admin switch reaches the case view after a\nreload, and the console stays free of page errors and 5xx responses.\n\n* test(pathology): seed the case with the provider''s person id\n\nThe case-view spec orders its case through the same form the order screen\nposts. The seed took the first provider from /rest/provider/search and sent\nthat provider''s id as both providerId and providerPersonId. The save resolves\nproviderPersonId as a person, so the order only saved where the provider and\nits person happened to share an id. On the dev stack they do (both 2); on the\nCI database they do not, and the first test failed with HTTP 500 while the\nserver logged \"No row with the given identifier exists: Person#2\", taking the\nother eight tests down as skipped.\n\nThe search already returns personId next to id, and the order screen sends\nproviderId from the one and providerPersonId from the other. The seed now\ndoes the same and skips a provider that has no person behind it.\n\nVerified by pointing provider 2 at a copied person with a different id on a\nlocal stack: the old seed fails with the CI error, the new one passes, and\nthe three pathology specs pass on both that database and the original one.\n\n* test(pathology): read the paged dashboard in the seed helper (OGC-264)\n\nSince #4405 /rest/pathology/dashboard answers {items, paging, totalItems}\ninstead of a bare array, so the Playwright seed helper found no case and\nthe case-view spec failed at its first step. The helper now reads the\nitems page, the shape PathologyDashboard.jsx reads.\n\nTests: the three pathology specs pass twice against a stack built from\nthe branch after the develop merge, 15 passed each run.\n\n* test(pathology): drive the program case spec through the shell (OGC-264)\n\nDevelop''s pathology-ihc-cytology-case spec was written against the flat\npathology case view: a native stage select, a #pathology_save2 button and\nassignment controls that are always in reach. This branch replaces that\nscreen with the case-view shell, where the stage is a Dropdown in the\naction bar, the technician, pathologist and release controls sit in\naccordion sections that unlock with the stage, and the case is saved with\nSave draft, so the spec could not drive it.\n\nEach program now names a screen driver. Immunohistochemistry and Cytology\nkeep the native-select driver unchanged. Pathology''s driver sets the stage\nthrough the Dropdown, expands the section that holds a control before\nreturning it, and saves from the action bar. Its working stage becomes\nReady for Pathologist, the stage at which the shell offers the pathologist\nselect; the release test moves the case there first. The shared\nfirst-option helper now skips options with an empty value, since the\nshell''s selects carry a \"Select\" placeholder with real text. The shell\nreads the saved case back after every save, so the pathology driver also\nwaits for that read before a test reloads or leaves the page; without it\nthe navigation aborted the read and the browser console logged a fetch\nerror on every save.\n\nTests: the spec''s nine tests pass on four consecutive runs against a stack\nbuilt from this branch with the CI foundational fixtures loaded, alongside\nthe three existing pathology specs (24 passed per run); the last two runs\nshow no fetch error in the console.\n\n* fix(pathology): keep request statuses, controlled case fields (OGC-264)\n\nPicking a second request in the review multiselect reset every earlier\nrequest''s status to Opened, because Carbon hands back the objects it was\ngiven at mount. A request already on the case now keeps the status it\nholds there; only a new pick is stamped Opened.\n\nThe gross, microscopy and conclusion text areas and the block and slide\nlocation inputs start controlled, so React no longer warns when a case\nwithout those values is edited. The auto-assigned technician and\npathologist read \"Last,First\" like the names the server returns.\n\nThe program case spec repeats the dashboard''s \"All\" pick until it holds,\nsince the dashboard''s first load could put its own grouping back.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: mozzy11 <mozzy@uwdigi.org>\nCo-authored-by: Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"3851d944f3584cf9aacd274dc593eebe63218a0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/3851d944f3584cf9aacd274dc593eebe63218a0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/e74beea0c9ba82a61dcfa4022ec64a13f929f5be","verification":{"payload":"tree 3851d944f3584cf9aacd274dc593eebe63218a0c\nparent b470bd330957229b4e31f46f247f70638504651d\nauthor OLARA Moses <molarag21996@gmail.com> 1791353887 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791353887 +0300\n\nfeat(pathology): case view opens on the shared case-view shell (OGC-264) (#4392)\n\n* feat(pathology): case view DTO gains the FR-1 specimen facts (OGC-264)\n\nSlice S3 of the case view rebuild needs what its Case Information section\nshows, and nothing more.\n\nPathologyCaseViewDisplayItem gains receivedDate (sample.received_date, the\nspecimen arrival date, distinct from the request date) and specimenTypes (one\nlocalized type-of-sample name per sample item). The requester was built as\nlastName + \" \" + firstName with no null check, so an order without a requester\nrendered the literal \"null null\"; it is null now.\n\nBoth dates (requestDate, receivedDate) are LocalDate values computed in the\nserver''s zone: the JSON layer formats a Date in UTC, so a specimen received at\nlocal midnight in Nairobi printed the day before. Same yyyy-MM-dd string on\nthe wire.\n\nhasOpenRequests leaves both DTOs. The dashboard read nothing from it and it\ncost one lazy SELECT per row on the unpaginated list; the case view needs the\nrequest names, which only the request rows carry, so the rows are the contract.\n\nTests: PathologyCaseViewDisplayTest (5) seeds its sample items in setup rather\nthan through the DBUnit fixture, because a fixture that names type_of_sample\ntruncates localization for the rest of the fork, and pins the JVM zone east of\nGreenwich so a UTC runner cannot pass the old code. PathologyCaseViewOpenRequestsTest\nserializes both DTOs and asserts the flag is off the wire and the request\nstatuses are on it.\n\n* fix(pathology): stage switch help text matches the case view (OGC-264)\n\nThe seven pathology.stage.<STAGE>.enabled switches promised that a disabled\nstage \"is skipped and shown as not applicable\". Nothing skips a stage\nautomatically: a maintainer switched Microtomy off on a deployed build and the\ncase view still offered it and stored a case at it.\n\nThe message bundle text and, through changeset 037, the seven site_information\ndescriptions that 036 wrote now describe what ships: the case view marks the\nstage not applicable on its rail, locks the section as not tracked at this\nlaboratory, and stops offering it in the stage selector. 036 is untouched\nbecause it has run on deployments.\n\n037 is tested by running it: a database-upgrades boundary fixture stops the\nchangelog just before 037, switches Coverslipping off as an administrator\nwould, runs the rest, and asserts the seven descriptions changed and the seven\nvalues did not. PathologyStageEnablementFlagsTest re-seeds the corrected\nwording so it stays order-independent.\n\n* feat(pathology): case view opens on the shared case-view shell (OGC-264)\n\nSlice S3 of Pathology Case View v2: the flat form becomes the shell #4321\nadded.\n\nScreen (PathologyCaseView.jsx, 1,317 to 715 lines):\n- eleven CaseSections in bench order; state from deriveCaseSections over\n  caseInfo.status, the Pathologist role and the stage switches; nothing is\n  hidden by status or role\n- the accordion mounts only once the case has arrived, because CaseSection\n  seeds its open state at mount\n- one updateCase funnel marks the form dirty; loading and reloading clear it;\n  the multiselects are keyed on a load counter so Discard resets them\n- Save draft re-reads the case, so a release shows the stage the server moved\n  it to\n- the stage selector sits in the action bar''s status slot, omits stages the\n  laboratory switched off unless the case is at one, and carries a hint that\n  transitions come later. It is a Carbon Dropdown opening upward, because the\n  bar is at the foot of a long page where a native select''s menu was clipped\n  against the window.\n\nSections (sections/*.jsx): Case Information (FR-1 rows, not-recorded hint,\nquestionnaire), Grossing (description, blocks, technician), Microtomy\n(slides), Pathologist Review (pathologist, requests), Findings\n(microscopyExam, techniques, conclusions, IHC referral, Release), Reports,\nand one placeholder body for the five stages nothing records yet.\n\nA section header badges what its rows say: Complete for grossing under\nFR-3.4 (a description that is not only whitespace, and a block), otherwise\n\"{n} blocks\" or \"{n} slides\" when rows exist, nothing when none do. The rail\nticks grossing and microtomy on the same rules and reports on a report\nexisting; the five stages OpenELIS records no work at tick on the case having\npassed them, the only fact there is. Derived from position alone, as before,\nthe screen told a pathologist a case at the reading had been decalcified,\nprocessed and embedded under bodies saying nothing is recorded there yet. The\nseven single-stage sections are titled by the stage''s own key, so the rail,\nthe header and the locked hint cannot call one stage two things.\n\nLayout: the title and patient band are nested two Sections deep, the idiom\nevery other case view here sizes its title with, inside a Stack that gives\nthe page its vertical rhythm; the sub-headings and the summary title take\ntheir level from that context. The shell''s grid draws on the page''s own\nbackground colour, because inside this application''s white theme zone a\nfield, a tile and the content area are all near the same light grey, and a\nform laid straight on the page had inputs nobody could see until one was\nfocused; every other form screen sits on a white body card for the same\nreason.\n\npathologyCaseView.scss: the sections sit in the shell''s nine of sixteen\ncolumns, so the sixteen-column Grid rows they were written as wrapped inside\nit and drew their controls over one another. Each repeating row is one\nwrapping flex line instead, with its labels shown and its buttons following\nthe fields as one group; Carbon''s file uploader renders an empty description\nparagraph above its button, which is hidden so the button lines up with its\nneighbours. Grossing leads with the macroscopic description, the work the\nbench is doing, rather than with the technician dropdown. A row''s remove\ncontrol is a ghost button carrying \"Remove Block\" in text; as an IconButton\nthe word was laid over the glyph and clipped. The chips are DismissibleTag,\nwhose dismiss label is localized, rather than the deprecated filter Tag with\nCarbon''s English default. The pickers show \"Select\" as placeholder.\n\nPatientHeader: the stage tag and the assigned-staff lines are stacked with a\ngap and the tag keeps its own width; the identifier pills are a wrapping flex\nrow with a gap, on every screen that renders the band.\n\nRelease is rendered whether or not the case can be released, disabled and\nnaming the assignment that is actually missing, rather than absent until both\nexist. Reports says it holds none rather than showing an empty list.\n\npathologySections.js: the section list, stage gating, switch reading, rail\nitems and badge kinds, pure, shared by the screen and its tests. The rail\nshows two outstanding requests and counts the rest, because three names\nwrapped onto three lines inside a Carbon step and overran the step below, and\ncarries all of them on the step''s hover title, which the box does not bound.\n\nCaseSummaryPanel renders booleans as Yes and No, where React rendered nothing\nfor either value, and a row can name what its count counted. The value of the\nshared key pathology.label.slide.number is \"Slide number\", capitalised like\nits block twin.\n\nFixed in passing: labels now point at their inputs (the TextAreas had no id\nand every block row shared one), the conclusions pager is a span rather than\nan unfocusable Link, three hardcoded strings use existing keys.\n\nThe rail sits in a titled tile like the summary, and the shell''s grid draws\non the page background so fields and tiles are visible against the content\narea. PatientHeader''s stage tag and staff lines are stacked with a gap and its\nidentifier pills gain one, on every screen that renders the band.\n\nTests: pathologySections.test.js (44), PathologyCaseView.sections.test.jsx\n(48), PathologyCaseView.test.jsx (3), CaseSummaryPanel.test.jsx (+4),\nCaseSection.test.jsx (+1), CaseViewLayout.test.jsx (+1), ProgressRail.test.jsx\n(+1), CaseActionBar.test.jsx (+2). 17 en.json keys.\n\n* test(pathology): case view end-to-end coverage on the shell (OGC-264)\n\nNine tests in pathology-case-view.spec.ts (core-app) walk a fresh case on a\ndeployed stack: the eleven sections and rail items in order, Case Information\ncollapsed with the seeded lab number and specimen type, locked sections naming\nthe stage they wait for, the stage moved by hand and the summary following it,\nDiscard reloading the saved case, Save draft persisting and the page reloading\nat the new stage, a slide row whose controls are measured not to overlap, a\nrail click scrolling to Reports, and a stage switched off on the admin page\nrendering N/A, locking its section and leaving the selector (restored in\nfinally).\n\nseed-pathology-data.ts places the order through the same REST call the Add\nOrder screen makes and reads the case id back from the dashboard search, since\nthe order save does not return it. Every id is discovered on the running\nstack: the programme whose name contains \"pathology\" (this stack calls it\nHistopathology), the first sample type whose tests include \"Histopathology\nexamination\", the first provider, and no referring site, because a site id\nthe stack does not know is what makes the save fail with a 500.\n\nWhat unit tests cannot prove and this does: the stylesheets load, the row\ncontrols are laid out side by side rather than over one another, the accordion\nids resolve for the rail, the admin switch reaches the case view after a\nreload, and the console stays free of page errors and 5xx responses.\n\n* test(pathology): seed the case with the provider''s person id\n\nThe case-view spec orders its case through the same form the order screen\nposts. The seed took the first provider from /rest/provider/search and sent\nthat provider''s id as both providerId and providerPersonId. The save resolves\nproviderPersonId as a person, so the order only saved where the provider and\nits person happened to share an id. On the dev stack they do (both 2); on the\nCI database they do not, and the first test failed with HTTP 500 while the\nserver logged \"No row with the given identifier exists: Person#2\", taking the\nother eight tests down as skipped.\n\nThe search already returns personId next to id, and the order screen sends\nproviderId from the one and providerPersonId from the other. The seed now\ndoes the same and skips a provider that has no person behind it.\n\nVerified by pointing provider 2 at a copied person with a different id on a\nlocal stack: the old seed fails with the CI error, the new one passes, and\nthe three pathology specs pass on both that database and the original one.\n\n* test(pathology): read the paged dashboard in the seed helper (OGC-264)\n\nSince #4405 /rest/pathology/dashboard answers {items, paging, totalItems}\ninstead of a bare array, so the Playwright seed helper found no case and\nthe case-view spec failed at its first step. The helper now reads the\nitems page, the shape PathologyDashboard.jsx reads.\n\nTests: the three pathology specs pass twice against a stack built from\nthe branch after the develop merge, 15 passed each run.\n\n* test(pathology): drive the program case spec through the shell (OGC-264)\n\nDevelop''s pathology-ihc-cytology-case spec was written against the flat\npathology case view: a native stage select, a #pathology_save2 button and\nassignment controls that are always in reach. This branch replaces that\nscreen with the case-view shell, where the stage is a Dropdown in the\naction bar, the technician, pathologist and release controls sit in\naccordion sections that unlock with the stage, and the case is saved with\nSave draft, so the spec could not drive it.\n\nEach program now names a screen driver. Immunohistochemistry and Cytology\nkeep the native-select driver unchanged. Pathology''s driver sets the stage\nthrough the Dropdown, expands the section that holds a control before\nreturning it, and saves from the action bar. Its working stage becomes\nReady for Pathologist, the stage at which the shell offers the pathologist\nselect; the release test moves the case there first. The shared\nfirst-option helper now skips options with an empty value, since the\nshell''s selects carry a \"Select\" placeholder with real text. The shell\nreads the saved case back after every save, so the pathology driver also\nwaits for that read before a test reloads or leaves the page; without it\nthe navigation aborted the read and the browser console logged a fetch\nerror on every save.\n\nTests: the spec''s nine tests pass on four consecutive runs against a stack\nbuilt from this branch with the CI foundational fixtures loaded, alongside\nthe three existing pathology specs (24 passed per run); the last two runs\nshow no fetch error in the console.\n\n* fix(pathology): keep request statuses, controlled case fields (OGC-264)\n\nPicking a second request in the review multiselect reset every earlier\nrequest''s status to Opened, because Carbon hands back the objects it was\ngiven at mount. A request already on the case now keeps the status it\nholds there; only a new pick is stamped Opened.\n\nThe gross, microscopy and conclusion text areas and the block and slide\nlocation inputs start controlled, so React no longer warns when a case\nwithout those values is edited. The auto-assigned technician and\npathologist read \"Last,First\" like the names the server returns.\n\nThe program case spec repeats the dashboard''s \"All\" pick until it holds,\nsince the dashboard''s first load could put its own grouping back.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: mozzy11 <mozzy@uwdigi.org>\nCo-authored-by: Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxeQgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyskQAJPXC/5vqpluQzIkEFbTi88f\nqNq0roSZM4mellqBP3wIeKjro5A+Myoft3IeYkhjzomFmR0EN+K3JAdcyMw5OQJg\nDb9BZAUjgDTTdIhn0IpL/ZjqIYhgysC6R5CWJnjq1rZWWARJm8zUi4ipdh6pjDXj\ny2Qs8x9+mznA4tcOeBO9ka/iOGfjZoLDsMTMM8hC7zETK8jGZz0dPwbFcPWhh5sc\nQKQJQb8wIrT+WiWGazjK6vlesODe4rrAwRUtx7cNGa2deAchggegjEIlt5+SxP4J\nwDGq2HFN+Tw0M20HZr3ftEWyhsKoWuxNKssJmVoBu1RX0DrBYx0/XIULU1G91A4i\nxtEHTvDx2Fwt92ODAuyctaTq8Do+GzCzZ7Zg5zQc0riRd1wIdZYZC53L6v9E6GC8\nRDUNOSLu8gMSn2YTuTUewdCmazdZO6r1d/3Y+nrsZ0+dPCy++8bu0EcG7g31kfv/\nga0NT7jJmzle/AAzPnx5sc5O8Rp6vj0h6d5amo3Az+GnsExLO150C+Dqu7YSER8V\n/W6N9sNfrg//kLd1cAuYBXy117DOnJKJK2cN9nqqlDKfAfqN7iqaV4dOckLPJNb0\nGVpiXMI6t+DtdOBDPdKesRBvkVMoyhzks+KSMPt4kti5PtnXuoz2A8Mk9lWlnyLY\n4KkTnvP4i0vvaixjTSCw\n=Br6D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T06:18:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/e74beea0c9ba82a61dcfa4022ec64a13f929f5be","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKGU3NGJlZWEwYzliYTgyYTYxZGNmYTQwMjJlYzY0YTEzZjkyOWY1YmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/b470bd330957229b4e31f46f247f70638504651d","sha":"b470bd330957229b4e31f46f247f70638504651d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/b470bd330957229b4e31f46f247f70638504651d"}],"sha":"e74beea0c9ba82a61dcfa4022ec64a13f929f5be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/e74beea0c9ba82a61dcfa4022ec64a13f929f5be"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19221635?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WodPachua","id":19221635,"login":"WodPachua","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjIxNjM1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WodPachua","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/b470bd330957229b4e31f46f247f70638504651d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T05:23:35Z","email":"molarag21996@gmail.com","name":"OLARA Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T05:23:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(order): localize the close button on selected test and panel tags (#4416)\n\nThe six DismissibleTags on the order entry sample step and the collect\nstep (SampleTestSection, CollectTestPickerSection) passed only\ndismissTooltipLabel. Carbon names the close button from `title` and\nreads dismissTooltipLabel only once the tag text has been ellipsised, so\nin the normal case every close button announced Carbon''s English\n\"Dismiss\" whatever the user''s language. Both props now carry the same\n\"Remove {name}\" string from common.removeSelection, defined once per\ncomponent instead of inlined at each tag.\n\nTests: SampleTestSection.test.jsx +2 (one per render path; the standard\nsample list and the environmental manifest picker hold two tags each) and\nCollectTestPickerSection.test.jsx +1, each asserting a close button\nnamed \"Remove <name>\" exists and none named \"Dismiss\". All three fail on\nthe previous source.\n\nThe microbiology order-entry Playwright helper looked tests up with a\nnon-exact getByLabel, which the renamed close button (\"Remove <name>\")\nnow also matches; those four lookups are exact.\n\nCo-authored-by: Agaba Derrick <agabaderrick18@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"4cb801a2a73e88822d8f7dec545ab6cbc45332b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/4cb801a2a73e88822d8f7dec545ab6cbc45332b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/b470bd330957229b4e31f46f247f70638504651d","verification":{"payload":"tree 4cb801a2a73e88822d8f7dec545ab6cbc45332b3\nparent 4eb9af64a6ee1a3ee0c76c654b40eb57a868f646\nauthor OLARA Moses <molarag21996@gmail.com> 1791350615 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791350615 +0300\n\nfix(order): localize the close button on selected test and panel tags (#4416)\n\nThe six DismissibleTags on the order entry sample step and the collect\nstep (SampleTestSection, CollectTestPickerSection) passed only\ndismissTooltipLabel. Carbon names the close button from `title` and\nreads dismissTooltipLabel only once the tag text has been ellipsised, so\nin the normal case every close button announced Carbon''s English\n\"Dismiss\" whatever the user''s language. Both props now carry the same\n\"Remove {name}\" string from common.removeSelection, defined once per\ncomponent instead of inlined at each tag.\n\nTests: SampleTestSection.test.jsx +2 (one per render path; the standard\nsample list and the environmental manifest picker hold two tags each) and\nCollectTestPickerSection.test.jsx +1, each asserting a close button\nnamed \"Remove <name>\" exists and none named \"Dismiss\". All three fail on\nthe previous source.\n\nThe microbiology order-entry Playwright helper looked tests up with a\nnon-exact getByLabel, which the renamed close button (\"Remove <name>\")\nnow also matches; those four lookups are exact.\n\nCo-authored-by: Agaba Derrick <agabaderrick18@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxddXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAC/oQAE85PzlGIRdvNmbUecpvY+lc\n3/wA9xl4ahwvKZ771diNTdrceuGaG5rT7EgvNA8KNVEoIQEY9Yv7DOEUnDfoeZlx\nhmQQ/4x391ZO4TwmGD1w/8b6zJp3i4cj4VEezF8s