repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/4eb9af64a6ee1a3ee0c76c654b40eb57a868f646"}],"sha":"b470bd330957229b4e31f46f247f70638504651d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/b470bd330957229b4e31f46f247f70638504651d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29783151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/4eb9af64a6ee1a3ee0c76c654b40eb57a868f646/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:00:12Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:00:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(order): possible matches before create, Handling group, tested elsewhere and fewer low-value fields (OGC-1424) (#4608)\n\n* feat(order): possible matches before create, Handling group, tested elsewhere and fewer low-value fields in clinical order entry (OGC-1424)\n\nFRS clinical order entry v4, slice M14.\n\n- Create patient, Add new organization and Add new provider first ask the\n  server for up to five similar records (names misspelled, sounding alike or\n  swapped, birth date within a year, identifier one character off, facility\n  names equal apart from case, punctuation and common words). Use this one\n  picks the existing record; Create new anyway is confirmed and recorded in\n  possible_match_override.\n- Fax fields show only when the new showFaxFields setting is on; a new\n  provider takes a title from the provider title list; Payment status shows\n  only with trackPayment, the billing reference only with billingRefNumber.\n- Tested elsewhere moves to the test row''s More actions menu on Prepare\n  Samples with a purple tag, reported value and laboratory picker\n  (order_test_tested_elsewhere).\n- Received by {name} (you) with Change; the receiver is stored per sample.\n- The clinical sample row drops specimen origin, collection conditions,\n  free-text temperature and lab performed sampling (saved values read-only\n  under \"Recorded before this version\") and gains a Handling group: the\n  catalog requirement, Arrived as with measured temperature, Same for all\n  samples, Stored at with the device temperature, and a warm-gray Handling\n  mismatch tag offering a prefilled non-conformity report.\n- The dead OrderEnter.jsx with its unwired print shortcut is removed.\n- A step save of an existing sample now keeps every collection detail it\n  sends; collection method, GPS and legacy fields were silently dropped.\n\n* fix(order): review follow-up for clinical order entry clean-up (OGC-1424)\n\n- A second possible-match check after Create new anyway opened straight on\n  the confirmation; the dialog now starts fresh for every check.\n- A measured temperature outside -100 to 60 °C was dropped silently and\n  cleared the stored value. The field now says what is accepted, the To\n  continue checklist lists it, and a rejected value never clears the stored\n  temperature.\n- Payment status options read raw codes (normalCash): the generic\n  localization backfill had copied each dictionary code in as its English\n  name. A changeset gives the patientPayment entries their labels in English\n  and French, leaving names an administrator changed alone.\n- A receiver that only defaulted to the saving user was written on samples\n  received earlier; it is now stored only when the receipt is recorded in\n  that save.\n- Use this one is disabled for an inactive facility, which stays listed and\n  tagged Inactive.\n\n* test(order): microbiology spec no longer ticks the retired clinical Lab performed sampling; payment labels test seeds its own rows (OGC-1424)\n\nThe microbiology order entry spec ticked Lab performed sampling on the\nclinical sample card to complete Prepare Samples; FR-C9 retires that box\non clinical samples and OGC-1419 already made the collector optional, so\nthe step completes on collection date and time.\n\nPaymentStatusLabelsMigrationTest read the boot-time rows, which sibling\nfixtures that replace the localization tables wipe; it now seeds or\nborrows the patientPayment rows, runs the changeset SQL and restores\nwhat it found.\n\n* fix(test-catalog): result options with the same sort order keep a stable order by id (OGC-1424)\n\nOptions sharing a sortOrder came back in database order, so a test copied\nfrom another test could list Invalid first instead of last, which the\nogc-1234 catalog spec caught on CI. Ties now fall back to the numeric id.","tree":{"sha":"0e0e692468035d862c1574321b05932852427f03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/0e0e692468035d862c1574321b05932852427f03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/4eb9af64a6ee1a3ee0c76c654b40eb57a868f646","verification":{"payload":"tree 0e0e692468035d862c1574321b05932852427f03\nparent afc9b8c65eab5a0f331a676860dc3f1d5518faa3\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1791338412 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791338412 +0300\n\nfeat(order): possible matches before create, Handling group, tested elsewhere and fewer low-value fields (OGC-1424) (#4608)\n\n* feat(order): possible matches before create, Handling group, tested elsewhere and fewer low-value fields in clinical order entry (OGC-1424)\n\nFRS clinical order entry v4, slice M14.\n\n- Create patient, Add new organization and Add new provider first ask the\n  server for up to five similar records (names misspelled, sounding alike or\n  swapped, birth date within a year, identifier one character off, facility\n  names equal apart from case, punctuation and common words). Use this one\n  picks the existing record; Create new anyway is confirmed and recorded in\n  possible_match_override.\n- Fax fields show only when the new showFaxFields setting is on; a new\n  provider takes a title from the provider title list; Payment status shows\n  only with trackPayment, the billing reference only with billingRefNumber.\n- Tested elsewhere moves to the test row''s More actions menu on Prepare\n  Samples with a purple tag, reported value and laboratory picker\n  (order_test_tested_elsewhere).\n- Received by {name} (you) with Change; the receiver is stored per sample.\n- The clinical sample row drops specimen origin, collection conditions,\n  free-text temperature and lab performed sampling (saved values read-only\n  under \"Recorded before this version\") and gains a Handling group: the\n  catalog requirement, Arrived as with measured temperature, Same for all\n  samples, Stored at with the device temperature, and a warm-gray Handling\n  mismatch tag offering a prefilled non-conformity report.\n- The dead OrderEnter.jsx with its unwired print shortcut is removed.\n- A step save of an existing sample now keeps every collection detail it\n  sends; collection method, GPS and legacy fields were silently dropped.\n\n* fix(order): review follow-up for clinical order entry clean-up (OGC-1424)\n\n- A second possible-match check after Create new anyway opened straight on\n  the confirmation; the dialog now starts fresh for every check.\n- A measured temperature outside -100 to 60 °C was dropped silently and\n  cleared the stored value. The field now says what is accepted, the To\n  continue checklist lists it, and a rejected value never clears the stored\n  temperature.\n- Payment status options read raw codes (normalCash): the generic\n  localization backfill had copied each dictionary code in as its English\n  name. A changeset gives the patientPayment entries their labels in English\n  and French, leaving names an administrator changed alone.\n- A receiver that only defaulted to the saving user was written on samples\n  received earlier; it is now stored only when the receipt is recorded in\n  that save.\n- Use this one is disabled for an inactive facility, which stays listed and\n  tagged Inactive.\n\n* test(order): microbiology spec no longer ticks the retired clinical Lab performed sampling; payment labels test seeds its own rows (OGC-1424)\n\nThe microbiology order entry spec ticked Lab performed sampling on the\nclinical sample card to complete Prepare Samples; FR-C9 retires that box\non clinical samples and OGC-1419 already made the collector optional, so\nthe step completes on collection date and time.\n\nPaymentStatusLabelsMigrationTest read the boot-time rows, which sibling\nfixtures that replace the localization tables wipe; it now seeds or\nborrows the patientPayment rows, runs the changeset SQL and restores\nwhat it found.\n\n* fix(test-catalog): result options with the same sort order keep a stable order by id (OGC-1424)\n\nOptions sharing a sortOrder came back in database order, so a test copied\nfrom another test could list Invalid first instead of last, which the\nogc-1234 catalog spec caught on CI. Ties now fall back to the numeric id.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxaesCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwvYQAImBCiW1cK+wtwJVqgJ2t2OE\nnXdhSm3EAkVoHMlTRheMQpOiGFv/Qus3syW7RPZircL78YZ7+hg5hS9O7gOS+wEc\nA6vULwx0QKbInNJ2pyptaBLlEh7X7c1O5r4mPV3O/DhTBTHSy+PKc0mG1Q8XKfdQ\n4