://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/cf5faf2c03aa773da476fd567d1a965ba5b24a36","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKGNmNWZhZjJjMDNhYTc3M2RhNDc2ZmQ1NjdkMWE5NjViYTViMjRhMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/dc7dd348ff47eebb3c16f9abf4529fbabc6a284f","sha":"dc7dd348ff47eebb3c16f9abf4529fbabc6a284f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/dc7dd348ff47eebb3c16f9abf4529fbabc6a284f"}],"sha":"cf5faf2c03aa773da476fd567d1a965ba5b24a36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/cf5faf2c03aa773da476fd567d1a965ba5b24a36"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29783151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/dc7dd348ff47eebb3c16f9abf4529fbabc6a284f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:01:46Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:01:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(label-presets): per-preset content fields editor, Lab Number first, seeded defaults and named fields on printed labels (OGC-1218) (#4600)\n\n* feat(label-presets): per-preset content fields editor, Lab Number first, seeded defaults and named fields on printed labels (OGC-1218)\n\nThe data model shipped with OGC-285 but the editor never rendered it: every\nsystem preset carried LAB_NUMBER alone and a printed label showed the raw key.\nThe preset editor gains a Content fields section (Lab Number locked at position\n1, fifteen catalogued fields added from a picker, reordered with buttons,\noptionally required, with a soft fit hint that never blocks). The server keeps\nLab Number first and required on every save, renumbers the rest and refuses\nunknown keys with a 422. Liquibase 3.6.x.x/009 fills the block changeset 031\ndeferred: each system preset receives the fields the retired Barcode\nConfiguration screen printed for it, read from the legacy site_information\nelement keys, only while it still carries Lab Number alone. Snapshot labels\nfreeze the human field names and print the value the order knows next to each;\na field the order cannot fill prints as a line to write on.\n\n* fix(label-presets): legacy label renderers follow the preset''s content fields; fit hint counts selectable fields (OGC-1218 review)\n\nThe Print Bar Code Labels page, the label servlet, batch entry and the\nenvironmental and vector Label step still printed from the 25 retired\nsite_information element keys, which the redirected Barcode Configuration\nscreen can no longer change. OrderLabel, SpecimenLabel, SlideLabel,\nBlockLabel and FreezerLabel now read their field switches through\nLabelFieldPolicy, which asks the matching system preset and falls back to\nthe legacy key only where the preset gives no answer.\n\nThe fit hint no longer counts Lab Number (the barcode''s own text) and uses\nthe renderer''s real scaling, so the shipped Specimen default opens without\na warning; the sentence is pluralised.","tree":{"sha":"bb6dabd4bc66bcf28dc079e19b4bfb1d5a132fab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/bb6dabd4bc66bcf28dc079e19b4bfb1d5a132fab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/dc7dd348ff47eebb3c16f9abf4529fbabc6a284f","verification":{"payload":"tree bb6dabd4bc66bcf28dc079e19b4bfb1d5a132fab\nparent e75b01088ec708c7e7a9eec177598b074210533f\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1791313306 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791313306 +0300\n\nfeat(label-presets): per-preset content fields editor, Lab Number first, seeded defaults and named fields on printed labels (OGC-1218) (#4600)\n\n* feat(label-presets): per-preset content fields editor, Lab Number first, seeded defaults and named fields on printed labels (OGC-1218)\n\nThe data model shipped with OGC-285 but the editor never rendered it: every\nsystem preset carried LAB_NUMBER alone and a printed label showed the raw key.\nThe preset editor gains a Content fields section (Lab Number locked at position\n1, fifteen catalogued fields added from a picker, reordered with buttons,\noptionally required, with a soft fit hint that never blocks). The server keeps\nLab Number first and required on every save, renumbers the rest and refuses\nunknown keys with a 422. Liquibase 3.6.x.x/009 fills the block changeset 031\ndeferred: each system preset receives the fields the retired Barcode\nConfiguration screen printed for it, read from the legacy site_information\nelement keys, only while it still carries Lab Number alone. Snapshot labels\nfreeze the human field names and print the value the order knows next to each;\na field the order cannot fill prints as a line to write on.\n\n* fix(label-presets): legacy label renderers follow the preset''s content fields; fit hint counts selectable fields (OGC-1218 review)\n\nThe Print Bar Code Labels page, the label servlet, batch entry and the\nenvironmental and vector Label step still printed from the 25 retired\nsite_information element keys, which the redirected Barcode Configuration\nscreen can no longer change. OrderLabel, SpecimenLabel, SlideLabel,\nBlockLabel and FreezerLabel now read their field switches through\nLabelFieldPolicy, which asks the matching system preset and falls back to\nthe legacy key only where the preset gives no answer.\n\nThe fit hint no longer counts Lab Number (the barcode''s own text) and uses\nthe renderer''s real scaling, so the shipped Specimen default opens without\na warning; the sentence is pluralised.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxUWaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlc8QAESxsPu2pAdKgeo2NPh06G8r\nunkDuMNxfLt8rWIVjja88NVDwN9gT2ZOH5OMYA1KvrniPkhjQEpontjIEL+gpg78\n55yZgY2SPvUuIOOJ/sBnDdbFRQsFwVfJgCUl0xqVMzS0mgfNHGfkTwNPJ2FYBEzq\nElmy54m36DHHUpoh0Fz7PNw6qtHQychZgs7BHsshhJpy0tEWVngUi5KGxTa4D6LK\nylqwTOjtYzEDn8ZOgARIzEgP4xBigsO9D7hS1r6qaYZ2b1c3UTfLjhdIMJmfreKd\n49yO+HS72viFIx0V4ZGRhniP/5o0qLGY1HZEiBMLD32NRV6IEizknSvF/MRSN4+5\nLVifLroGsLTqsV0CGcAc5UotONDu/kaTrgXHG7qP0UsEnbJcoUb/b+UKNLWE5+Q6\npPHp8CHu4SFM1l4NHAKnCi+GISJ0+NIDom+kT8yTt703xGDQ9PkRyWqNZr+W3MRJ\nYeAne3UCo4xspVL4bEWSSxx7v4LQctOBzvMgZUHqQo8X17N967iTdShYJxSE7Gsm\ndBbY1CnY+kwRKY9sktVdf74o+d8+6ceN75cFsrC15h+TP3ZO1XNCmASwAdp8DFg/\n6teLwTVOMrh/lciLFuyoBbIFZ/OUiu+9a51EeBbdNcoWeICBGcrL/sFWHuiE92l1\nF97JIEAzpDih4OYIyAw+\n=AU2n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T19:01:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/dc7dd348ff47eebb3c16f9abf4529fbabc6a284f","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKGRjN2RkMzQ4ZmY0N2VlYmIzYzE2ZjlhYmY0NTI5ZmJhYmM2YTI4NGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/e75b01088ec708c7e7a9eec177598b074210533f","sha":"e75b01088ec708c7e7a9eec177598b074210533f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/e75b01088ec708c7e7a9eec177598b074210533f"}],"sha":"dc7dd348ff47eebb3c16f9abf4529fbabc6a284f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/dc7dd348ff47eebb3c16f9abf4529fbabc6a284f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29783151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/e75b01088ec708c7e7a9eec177598b074210533f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:10:04Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:10:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(label-presets): surface the site-wide pre-printed accession setting on the Label Presets page (OGC-1217) (#4598)\n\n* feat(label-presets): surface the site-wide pre-printed accession setting on the Label Presets page (OGC-1217)\n\nThe setting shipped with OGC-285 in SiteWideBarcodeSettingsRestController but no\nscreen rendered it, so whatever a site had stored was invisible and frozen.\nLabel Presets now opens with a Site-wide Barcode Settings card above the list:\npre-printed label numbers come from the order entry format and pool, or from a\nseparate pre-printed series with a 4-character prefix (enabled only for that\nchoice, refused on the page when it is not 4 letters or digits). The controller\nvalidates the prefix for the separate series (422 with the field and a text\ntag), trims it and always returns a string. Pre-printed numbers of the series\nare accepted at order entry only while the choice is active; the Playwright\nspec prints a set, attaches the printed number to a new order and checks the\nformat is refused again on the order entry pool.\n\n* fix(label-presets): store the pre-printed prefix in capitals and keep the dashboard keys in place\n\nReview follow-up on OGC-1217. The card only produces capital letters and digits\nwhile the API accepted a lower-case prefix, and lab numbers are compared\nexactly, so the stored prefix could drift from the labels already printed; the\ncontroller now upper-cases the trimmed prefix before validating and storing it.\nThe en.json diff is back to the keys this PR adds.","tree":{"sha":"9e6937696d615754c04cd54d4e12483329f288de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/9e6937696d615754c04cd54d4e12483329f288de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/e75b01088ec708c7e7a9eec177598b074210533f","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e6937696d615754c04cd54d4e12483329f288de\nparent 38e56f79ea8c0afdb0362b30ba15e5f3e1e636d4\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1791306604 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791306604 +0300\n\nfeat(label-presets): surface the site-wide pre-printed accession setting on the Label Presets page (OGC-1217) (#4598)\n\n* feat(label-presets): surface the site-wide pre-printed accession setting on the Label Presets page (OGC-1217)\n\nThe setting shipped with OGC-285 in SiteWideBarcodeSettingsRestController but no\nscreen rendered it, so whatever a site had stored was invisible and frozen.\nLabel Presets now opens with a Site-wide Barcode Settings card above the list:\npre-printed label numbers come from the order entry format and pool, or from a\nseparate pre-printed series with a 4-character prefix (enabled only for that\nchoice, refused on the page when it is not 4 letters or digits). The controller\nvalidates the prefix for the separate series (422 with the field and a text\ntag), trims it and always returns a string. Pre-printed numbers of the series\nare accepted at order entry only while the choice is active; the Playwright\nspec prints a set, attaches the printed number to a new order and checks the\nformat is refused again on the order entry pool.\n\n* fix(label-presets): store the pre-printed prefix in capitals and keep the dashboard keys in place\n\nReview follow-up on OGC-1217. The card only produces capital letters and digits\nwhile the API accepted a lower-case prefix, and lab numbers are compared\nexactly, so the stored prefix could drift from the labels already printed; the\ncontroller now upper-cases the trimmed prefix before validating and storing it.\nThe en.json diff is back to the keys this PR adds.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxStsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADQ8QACozGE3/SvudpPVMiWeWpwqb\nLVbOYnkA1YGsrXDZ69rsAJs5WxsHj/3A1SVnGRd7JtNapa57ml38vDot5gmNBAyq\n6BFX02LH1N52y3BMw9KN1ByYkN7LBIPoijktT5WfqM8el0FoRGf0f/yau8f0Gc+w\njFYI9O5NL9gyk/cyiZ2HJ+c4Cfztjn8ccbg7zAVaWicmpVqS6c1MpAX7ot4Spsl9\nAjWpsv3Td1a2eR0PPnVV17g8xJTpD9UMOlYsqiO/4K9pVPNxDryIGTaJKtc4MLJn\nBFzNou4i3MZm9MnYWqIibwTAPgKJK7vhzbCMhjSz5B1XkjkSEdPRMGeMRqUI9lSe\n08FwOjVrRHx0rUozOeVlJFUjRrJvZWCN4kkdvBuRoFnLgzSK2sUJJFK8CoCU2Um+\nvx8rxZ/O7t6yL57tuOe4gevneLnjHcOK25rJ40HsbqWi5tvLzret3FD6da6YbsM6\nHWsfGl9sAJpwkxLICEBhWnYcy0dXN5m+9V+OIUt4bca9KSc/ZuumqupV9MI3InT4\nhMIwstJVmDRQPKbMFETo8FVb8iu9AC5/290eZ7xCn8rhM5qao1SPjc1S4Ff/iOBB\nXANSEd/ZcB37AWfXszHGYadcC+l6VdBeK5X+2Ab6XU+/HQfcEX/4c1eU9dXeWLcu\nPflaEQIsDY4T/ZUSUJD7\n=KdI0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T17:10:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/e75b01088ec708c7e7a9eec177598b074210533f","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKGU3NWIwMTA4OGVjNzA4YzdlN2E5ZWVjMTc3NTk4YjA3NDIxMDUzM2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/38e56f79ea8c0afdb0362b30ba15e5f3e1e636d4","sha":"38e56f79ea8c0afdb0362b30ba15e5f3e1e636d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/38e56f79ea8c0afdb0362b30ba15e5f3e1e636d4"}],"sha":"e75b01088ec708c7e7a9eec177598b074210533f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/e75b01088ec708c7e7a9eec177598b074210533f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29783151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/38e56f79ea8c0afdb0362b30ba15e5f3e1e636d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T16:00:52Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T16:00:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(order): refer out one or every tube from Prepare Samples, with reason, step-save and fully referred completion (OGC-1423) (#4594)\n\n* feat(order): refer out one or every tube from Prepare Samples, with reason, step-save and fully referred completion (OGC-1423)\n\nThe v4 Refer Out section saved each referral on its own the moment the\nform was submitted, offered no reason and no bulk action, and a fully\nreferred order still went through the in-house Sample check and showed\nas any other order on the dashboard.\n\nPrepare Samples now stages a referral on its tube (Pending save) and\nsaves it with the step''s Save (FR-A5, FR-E5); the form asks for the\nreceiving laboratory and an optional reason from the referral reason\nlist; \"Refer out all in-house samples\" stages the same referral on every\ntube that has none. An order whose every test is referred finishes order\nentry at Prepare Samples (no Sample check) and the dashboard shows it as\nReferred out, with a referral line on split orders and a \"Has referred\ntests\" filter next to \"Referred Out\"; the worklists leave referred tests\nout. FHIR resources are created at dispatch, as before (FR-E3a).\n\n* fix(order): keep Prepare Samples label printing disabled until the order has loaded\n\nOpening Prepare Samples by lab number renders the sample cards before the\norder search answers. A Print Labels click in that window found no order id,\nsaved first, and posted an order without a lab number (400), so no PDF ever\nfollowed; the OGC-1422 spec hit it on CI shard 3. OrderContext.isLoading now\ndisables the card''s Print Labels and the labels section''s print actions, and\nthe print path refuses to save while the order is still loading.\n\n* fix(order): one open-referral rule for the dashboard, finished progress on referred orders, server-driven dashboard search\n\nReview follow-up on OGC-1423. OrderProgressService.isOpenReferral (exists, not\ncancelled, not rejected) now feeds the fully-referred check, the referral\ncounts and the Has referred tests filter, so a referral the reference lab\nrejected reads as in-house everywhere; the fully-referred check runs once per\ndashboard row; a complete order reports its remaining steps as done so a fully\nreferred order shows 3/3; the status and priority filter labels come from the\nmessage bundle.\n\nThe dashboard''s table search also ran Carbon''s client-side text filter over\ncells that are rendered elements, so typing a lab number hid every row the\nserver had matched. The server search alone drives the rows now.","tree":{"sha":"0b2093d4259149896b28c5e718ddeabad066c638","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/0b2093d4259149896b28c5e718ddeabad066c638"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/38e56f79ea8c0afdb0362b30ba15e5f3e1e636d4","verification":{"payload":"tree 0b2093d4259149896b28c5e718ddeabad066c638\nparent d468631395b5869bfc7da4a57245eeb6bb06ad49\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1791302452 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791302452 +0300\n\nfeat(order): refer out one or every tube from Prepare Samples, with reason, step-save and fully referred completion (OGC-1423) (#4594)\n\n* feat(order): refer out one or every tube from Prepare Samples, with reason, step-save and fully referred completion (OGC-1423)\n\nThe v4 Refer Out section saved each referral on its own the moment the\nform was submitted, offered no reason and no bulk action, and a fully\nreferred order still went through the in-house Sample check and showed\nas any other order on the dashboard.\n\nPrepare Samples now stages a referral on its tube (Pending save) and\nsaves it with the step''s Save (FR-A5, FR-E5); the form asks for the\nreceiving laboratory and an optional reason from the referral reason\nlist; \"Refer out all in-house samples\" stages the same referral on every\ntube that has none. An order whose every test is referred finishes order\nentry at Prepare Samples (no Sample check) and the dashboard shows it as\nReferred out, with a referral line on split orders and a \"Has referred\ntests\" filter next to \"Referred Out\"; the worklists leave referred tests\nout. FHIR resources are created at dispatch, as before (FR-E3a).\n\n* fix(order): keep Prepare Samples label printing disabled until the order has loaded\n\nOpening Prepare Samples by lab number renders the sample cards before the\norder search answers. A Print Labels click in that window found no order id,\nsaved first, and posted an order without a lab number (400), so no PDF ever\nfollowed; the OGC-1422 spec hit it on CI shard 3. OrderContext.isLoading now\ndisables the card''s Print Labels and the labels section''s print actions, and\nthe print path refuses to save while the order is still loading.\n\n* fix(order): one open-referral rule for the dashboard, finished progress on referred orders, server-driven dashboard search\n\nReview follow-up on OGC-1423. OrderProgressService.isOpenReferral (exists, not\ncancelled, not rejected) now feeds the fully-referred check, the referral\ncounts and the Has referred tests filter, so a referral the reference lab\nrejected reads as in-house everywhere; the fully-referred check runs once per\ndashboard row; a complete order reports its remaining steps as done so a fully\nreferred order shows 3/3; the status and priority filter labels come from the\nmessage bundle.\n\nThe dashboard''s table search also ran Carbon''s client-side text filter over\ncells that are rendered elements, so typing a lab number hid every row the\nserver had matched. The server search alone drives the rows now.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxRs0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEpYQAAjj8yDYVRD+oJR2UuOdraez\nwA6Q5E2uLWZdRtVJ7jyhJ9J09srWGcOxb/LtDr5i8d+9nQ0NwdTAJfSAida15mq8\nLqc1tA6QUIOpOyt/3Qu8tJoYRmY9LEY/aSr0pSs44uSnRzbcD9Hu14pZ7jFMaLkY\nNlabtdZkYOB1zMK1NocQI2w1heNJM7DY6T29Js3a/gM6+gFYdHI0mcJDK1mbsoy