:"38e56f79ea8c0afdb0362b30ba15e5f3e1e636d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/38e56f79ea8c0afdb0362b30ba15e5f3e1e636d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29783151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/d468631395b5869bfc7da4a57245eeb6bb06ad49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T11:07:24Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T11:07:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(order): print barcode labels from Prepare Samples (OGC-1422) (#4590)\n\n* feat(order): print barcode labels from Prepare Samples (OGC-1422)\n\nThe per-sample Print Labels button on Prepare Samples was a stub, so a\nlaboratory on order entry v4 could not print tube labels from order entry\nat all. Prepare Samples now carries the Labels section the v4 FRS calls\nfor (FR-I2 to FR-I7): the order''s label types from the active presets and\nthe test catalog, a quantity per tube and per label type with its source,\nand Print row, Print column and Print all. The quantities travel with the\nstep''s save; printing saves first when anything is pending, then opens the\nsaved labels as a PDF in a window opened inside the click. A failed print\nsays so and offers Retry, an empty selection says no labels are\nconfigured, an unreachable server is named as such, and a blocked window\nfalls back to a download with a notice. The card''s Print Labels prints\nthat tube''s row; the storage section''s legacy print button and the\n\"Print More Sample Labels\" stub are gone (one print control per row and\ncolumn, FR-I7).\n\nBackend: GET /api/orders/{id}/labels/pdf renders the order''s saved label\nrequests narrowed by preset, tube and scope; a save replaces the order''s\nlabel requests instead of adding to them; a client that holds the saved\ntubes may key a row by item-<sampleItemId>, accepted only for an item of\nthat order.\n\n* fix(order): seed Prepare Samples labels from the order''s saved rows, keep the test link on item-keyed rows\n\nReview of #4590: reopening Prepare Samples proposed the presets'' defaults\nagain and marked them pending, so the next save or print wrote them over\nthe quantities the order had saved. The section now reads the order''s\nsaved label rows once the order id is known, seeds every covered cell\nfrom them (shown as \"Saved\", not pending) and leaves only uncovered cells\non their proposal. The step''s save keyed by item id now carries the\ntube''s tests too, so the snapshot keeps its test link; the PDF and list\nendpoints answer 400 to a non-numeric id instead of 500; an unreachable\nserver is named as such in the print notice; the unused \"printed\" key is\ngone. The Playwright spec covers the reopen and the plain save.","tree":{"sha":"2eaf4f0d2e66334b29b97d323d6feb35c403b943","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/2eaf4f0d2e66334b29b97d323d6feb35c403b943"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/d468631395b5869bfc7da4a57245eeb6bb06ad49","verification":{"payload":"tree 2eaf4f0d2e66334b29b97d323d6feb35c403b943\nparent ed6e8eeebaa65c4350c630a23351f8ee70fe99f6\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1791284844 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791284844 +0300\n\nfeat(order): print barcode labels from Prepare Samples (OGC-1422) (#4590)\n\n* feat(order): print barcode labels from Prepare Samples (OGC-1422)\n\nThe per-sample Print Labels button on Prepare Samples was a stub, so a\nlaboratory on order entry v4 could not print tube labels from order entry\nat all. Prepare Samples now carries the Labels section the v4 FRS calls\nfor (FR-I2 to FR-I7): the order''s label types from the active presets and\nthe test catalog, a quantity per tube and per label type with its source,\nand Print row, Print column and Print all. The quantities travel with the\nstep''s save; printing saves first when anything is pending, then opens the\nsaved labels as a PDF in a window opened inside the click. A failed print\nsays so and offers Retry, an empty selection says no labels are\nconfigured, an unreachable server is named as such, and a blocked window\nfalls back to a download with a notice. The card''s Print Labels prints\nthat tube''s row; the storage section''s legacy print button and the\n\"Print More Sample Labels\" stub are gone (one print control per row and\ncolumn, FR-I7).\n\nBackend: GET /api/orders/{id}/labels/pdf renders the order''s saved label\nrequests narrowed by preset, tube and scope; a save replaces the order''s\nlabel requests instead of adding to them; a client that holds the saved\ntubes may key a row by item-<sampleItemId>, accepted only for an item of\nthat order.\n\n* fix(order): seed Prepare Samples labels from the order''s saved rows, keep the test link on item-keyed rows\n\nReview of #4590: reopening Prepare Samples proposed the presets'' defaults\nagain and marked them pending, so the next save or print wrote them over\nthe quantities the order had saved. The section now reads the order''s\nsaved label rows once the order id is known, seeds every covered cell\nfrom them (shown as \"Saved\", not pending) and leaves only uncovered cells\non their proposal. The step''s save keyed by item id now carries the\ntube''s tests too, so the snapshot keeps its test link; the PDF and list\nendpoints answer 400 to a non-numeric id instead of 500; an unreachable\nserver is named as such in the print notice; the unused \"printed\" key is\ngone. The Playwright spec covers the reopen and the plain save.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxNZsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAN/UQAKKyna5ekNMrAFyrDaIQzVcD\noCf4PpMlX2AVh0t0Caw1vTJQmI+CNoDv51+OLIGJtwrj48w8pD1T3cVocd0mT+vB\n1mNSld0eNWpS1fbhNIGBs5snAHBcUl2G9gu7r5neQE0Dw5zBRu9eMzXwu9nh+e5H\nkXVnLnUfvAE7f9X2D/pfYom9uwrwXs2vxu66kPoi8UUxY+Ywu2pftqcdjZiOin5S\n8M7lJNRrkCeEeZc09ry/23c0EnT4zm7NYDkUbU7vJwUvI/8O4ZGKrRy+4goL8H49\nsTLmldoxNXYVSRYRALElyo2OYaq7X9jsie0xiYOxKrRF49OtLXam5Zh4nQNFfor7\n0SVqKsYxjfGgKCPHXt9AwNEhrQ8Pxqm+5rS5vimPbPXYOr4fj4IY9+2t7pE0zXyK\njyrnQ/00IS3eoWOnjg9kC0B0FoCOAKzVTPmLfFhYTiLt3zaILik4xpSLLTI5W+ss\nl50d0HR6cOdgYrudY3c0FQ4kHvJ2UxgBTYYbcxX8EBwP1QLrqNGHtyRo9KeoT5hy\nYA4/oMGVZs1SonZ+Dzt5xci4eiQqJ0VRrNXqrIL0c1ys4pAuCTcTa6I0JFFet8MJ\nxYY8m9L114hftn7LrJx9TfW/ADCnrOgq3o3sFBxXzyiWshmrDz2m5nv/vqy0izAR\n2Hq+v1Z3OLsLmgbV5YjN\n=PlTN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T11:07:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/d468631395b5869bfc7da4a57245eeb6bb06ad49","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKGQ0Njg2MzEzOTViNTg2OWJmYzdkYTRhNTcyNDVlZWI2YmIwNmFkNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/ed6e8eeebaa65c4350c630a23351f8ee70fe99f6","sha":"ed6e8eeebaa65c4350c630a23351f8ee70fe99f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/ed6e8eeebaa65c4350c630a23351f8ee70fe99f6"}],"sha":"d468631395b5869bfc7da4a57245eeb6bb06ad49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/d468631395b5869bfc7da4a57245eeb6bb06ad49"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29783151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/ed6e8eeebaa65c4350c630a23351f8ee70fe99f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T05:56:33Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T05:56:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(label-presets): seed system presets from the real site_information keys and repair upgraded sites (OGC-1219) (#4589)\n\n* fix(label-presets): seed system presets from the real site_information keys and repair upgraded sites (OGC-1219)\n\nChangeset 030 read a barcode.<type>.<field> namespace that has never\nexisted in OpenELIS, so on every upgraded site all five system presets\ncame out of the hardcoded fallbacks (25 x 76 mm, default 1, max 10) while\nthe site''s real dimensions and quantities stayed untouched in\nsite_information. The test fixture invented the same wrong keys, so the\nsuite stayed green.\n\n030 now reads height{Type}Labels, width{Type}Labels,\nnumDefault{Type}Labels and numMax{Type}Labels, clamps out-of-range legacy\nvalues into the table''s constraints instead of failing the upgrade, and\nends with a guard that raises when v1 configuration exists and a preset\nstill carries the fallbacks (FRS MG-6). validCheckSum ANY keeps databases\nthat already ran the old text validating.\n\nA new changeset (3.6.x.x/008) repairs those databases: every system preset\nstill on the complete fallback set is re-read from the real keys, and a\npreset an administrator changed since is left alone. The seed tests run\nagainst the real key names, stash and restore the keys the test database\nalready carries, and cover the guard, AC-22a and the repair.\n\n* fix(order): persist the proposed label quantities when the labels section is left untouched\n\nAdd Order lifted labelPersistRequest only from the labels section''s\nonChange, so a save that kept the proposed quantities stored no label\nrequest at all and the post-save print panel fell back to one label: the\nsite''s configured quantities, restored by the seed repair, never reached\nthe order. The section now exposes the payload an untouched section would\npersist, and Add Order seeds it when the aggregation lands and clears it\nwhen no sample carries tests.\n\n* test(e2e): the seeded Order Label default is proposed and stored by Add Order (OGC-1219)\n\nEvery database carries numDefaultOrderLabels=2 from the 2.5.x.x seed, so\nthe Order Label preset must say 2 wherever the seed or its repair read the\nreal key; the spec then enters an order without touching the labels\nsection and reads the stored quantity back by accession number.\n\n* fix(label-presets): round decimal legacy sizes in the seed and repair, keep label requests out of Modify Order\n\nReview of #4589: the v1 Barcode Configuration page stored dimensions\nthrough Float.toString (\"40.0\", \"25.4\"), which both changesets and the\nMG-6 guard rejected as non-numeric, so such a site silently kept the\nfallbacks; the values are now accepted and rounded, the fixture carries\ndecimals, and 008 gains validCheckSum ANY for the database that already\nran its first text. Modify Order shares the Add Order component, and its\nsave (/rest/SampleEdit) rejects a labelPersistRequest it never declared,\nso the labels aggregation is no longer offered or lifted there.","tree":{"sha":"e9cd9cb72cc24a0a53d84e8e55e4a94e01584dd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/e9cd9cb72cc24a0a53d84e8e55e4a94e01584dd4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/ed6e8eeebaa65c4350c630a23351f8ee70fe99f6","verification":{"payload":"tree e9cd9cb72cc24a0a53d84e8e55e4a94e01584dd4\nparent 1c9ee7f9467ed79ff476ce368f2fde21d59c706d\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1791266193 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791266193 +0300\n\nfix(label-presets): seed system presets from the real site_information keys and repair upgraded sites (OGC-1219) (#4589)\n\n* fix(label-presets): seed system presets from the real site_information keys and repair upgraded sites (OGC-1219)\n\nChangeset 030 read a barcode.<type>.<field> namespace that has never\nexisted in OpenELIS, so on every upgraded site all five system presets\ncame out of the hardcoded fallbacks (25 x 76 mm, default 1, max 10) while\nthe site''s real dimensions and quantities stayed untouched in\nsite_information. The test fixture invented the same wrong keys, so the\nsuite stayed green.\n\n030 now reads height{Type}Labels, width{Type}Labels,\nnumDefault{Type}Labels and numMax{Type}Labels, clamps out-of-range legacy\nvalues into the table''s constraints instead of failing the upgrade, and\nends with a guard that raises when v1 configuration exists and a preset\nstill carries the fallbacks (FRS MG-6). validCheckSum ANY keeps databases\nthat already ran the old text validating.\n\nA new changeset (3.6.x.x/008) repairs those databases: every system preset\nstill on the complete fallback set is re-read from the real keys, and a\npreset an administrator changed since is left alone. The seed tests run\nagainst the real key names, stash and restore the keys the test database\nalready carries, and cover the guard, AC-22a and the repair.\n\n* fix(order): persist the proposed label quantities when the labels section is left untouched\n\nAdd Order lifted labelPersistRequest only from the labels section''s\nonChange, so a save that kept the proposed quantities stored no label\nrequest at all and the post-save print panel fell back to one label: the\nsite''s configured quantities, restored by the seed repair, never reached\nthe order. The section now exposes the payload an untouched section would\npersist, and Add Order seeds it when the aggregation lands and clears it\nwhen no sample carries tests.\n\n* test(e2e): the seeded Order Label default is proposed and stored by Add Order (OGC-1219)\n\nEvery database carries numDefaultOrderLabels=2 from the 2.5.x.x seed, so\nthe Order Label preset must say 2 wherever the seed or its repair read the\nreal key; the spec then enters an order without touching the labels\nsection and reads the stored quantity back by accession number.\n\n* fix(label-presets): round decimal legacy sizes in the seed and repair, keep label requests out of Modify Order\n\nReview of #4589: the v1 Barcode Configuration page stored dimensions\nthrough Float.toString (\"40.0\", \"25.4\"), which both changesets and the\nMG-6 guard rejected as non-numeric, so such a site silently kept the\nfallbacks; the values are now accepted and rounded, the fixture carries\ndecimals, and 008 gains validCheckSum ANY for the database that already\nran its first text. Modify Order shares the Add Order component, and its\nsave (/rest/SampleEdit) rejects a labelPersistRequest it never declared,\nso the labels aggregation is no longer offered or lifted there.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxI2RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbMIQAI4CPbJ8VM3LMDFdWKb25eZo\n8fw74AbRueXYUpHy2tm9LI6xSHhx/EDw23nF5IpRICPlV8Hd8nkUBTl8W9GvID7N\nlWc3LbX79abQzrbdI+SpLJ3TKerjdAx3ycekfHKjxtZzm7JB50ErMC7VIHL1WIt6\npHwSVOro9xx1xwslzHjsjx2HI03+2xVwXUjXIyiHZuFKiCmu0gpa9F61l8EV7hzq\nOT0eCpI2DE9voLkWeKkIi4zOIOkFLK/hdq9xD4v7VaM/WBELJDRievo3/7nPSxP1\nf3YvX41Xvd4FDz9jVZelWRYa2HpFFOlcNGxlkd9jPo4TOmY7ppMEL056qV8lzVB8\nrhDX4vAQuO8Lnf4IcShCqNMynbIR7Qcg/X4bxuOY6UOK3/thH6mxajZET7uKyu+n\nn6wVd/0nOc/9frvjA4Lvl5SW1hiM2yDq1HveLtjDQ6AEg+oZ2oXq2zyUELENaHfu\njxfO34sgy8BXc7xQILab+WO5EdOnKDUcHccFl6m/avpu0U8OTDsn1/4G/gy2y032\nVL175wTeBt2cwKyAMYl69DB/sGKFLVXC/tgEmvx8yJHpXMmJNYxu/y+8tiYzmQ4O\nAUPqiNcx7X4Qmo5L+CNnISY0rR+zC4qvdExDhwq+38w3wMvVice+NhcPDelmFDiH\nc3SlFbVMMOBExGJGJUPv\n=FML7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T05:56:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/ed6e8eeebaa65c4350c630a23351f8ee70fe99f6","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKGVkNmU4ZWVlYmFhNjVjNDM1MGM2MzBhMjMzNTFmOGVlNzBmZTk5ZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/1c9ee7f9467ed79ff476ce368f2fde21d59c706d","sha":"1c9ee7f9467ed79ff476ce368f2fde21d59c706d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/1c9ee7f9467ed79ff476ce368f2fde21d59c706d"}],"sha":"ed6e8eeebaa65c4350c630a23351f8ee70fe99f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/ed6e8eeebaa65c4350c630a23351f8ee70fe99f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29783151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/1c9ee7f9467ed79ff476ce368f2fde21d59c706d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T03:06:59Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T03:06:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(label-presets): make preset edits save, keep fields on partial updates, confirm saves (OGC-1227) (#4582)\n\n* fix(label-presets): make preset edits save, keep fields on partial updates, confirm saves (OGC-1227)\n\nThe editor''s PUT was rejected with 400 because it echoed the GET''s field rows\n(id, sourceType, lastupdated) into a DTO that refused unknown properties; a\nclean PUT then failed with 500 because the service cleared and re-added the\nfields in one flush and Hibernate inserts before it deletes orphans, colliding\non the unique (preset_id, display_order) index; and a PUT without a fields key\ncleared the preset''s fields.\n\nThe form now ignores read-only properties, treats a missing fields list as\n\"leave unchanged\" and refuses duplicate keys or positions with a 422. The\nservice reconciles fields by key, parking retained rows on temporary orders and\nflushing before the final orders are written, so row ids survive a save and\nreordering cannot collide. A System preset keeps its stored name whatever case\nthe client sends. The editor sends the declared field shape and the typed name\nand shows the server''s status and reason above the footer when a save is\nrefused; the list confirms a save with a toast and sends Activate/Deactivate as\nPATCH (it POSTed to a PATCH-only endpoint and got 405).\n\n* fix(users): keep what was typed when the user form''s payload is read again\n\nOpening Add from the user list now navigates in-app (#4578), so the form\nmounts with the cached GET /rest/UnifiedSystemUser?ID=0 payload and reads\nit again. That payload stamps systemUserLastupdated with the current time,\nso every read is a new object: handleUserData ran again and replaced the\nform state while the user was typing (the Cypress user-search test saved\n\"Willy Warren\" with the login name \"d\").\n\nThe payload now seeds the form once per user id and again only after a\nsave, where the fresh timestamp is wanted.\n\n* test(e2e): read the OGC-1186 dictionary row''s result cell only\n\nThe row-wide check tripped on the Reference Range column once #4578 began\nshowing a dictionary''s normal entry there.\n\n* fix(label-presets): refuse a null field entry with a 422, keep the HTTP reason out of translated notices\n\nReview of #4582: PUT {\"fields\":[null]} reached replaceFields and answered\n500; the form now names the rule (error.labelpreset.field.required). The\nsave-failure notice no longer appends \"Bad Request\" when the server''s\nmessageKey was translated, and the editor test mocks the uniqueness 422 in\nthe shape the server sends (a fieldError, not a globalError).\n\n* fix(users): seed the form from a fresh read and let a deactivated user be reactivated\n\nReopening a user from the list within the cache window mounted the form on\nthe cached payload; the seed then ran in the same effect flush as the\nuserDataShow effect, whose setValidation spread the initial all-false flags\nand won, so Save stayed disabled until every field was retyped. The form\nnow shows Loading until a read made after mount lands and seeds from that\nread (a user changed elsewhere in between shows the new values), every\nvalidation update is functional, and the flags come from the payload: a\ndeactivated user, whose login row is gone, keeps the names valid and only\nasks for the login name and password.","tree":{"sha":"e45aaf88572d684f2862f652ffb33801ad2c937a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/e45aaf88572d684f2862f652ffb33801ad2c937a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/1c9ee7f9467ed79ff476ce368f2fde21d59c706d","verification":{"payload":"tree e45aaf88572d684f2862f652ffb33801ad2c937a\nparent b931f0487f037e6bc681d9894a610425818d3ebc\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1791256019 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791256019 +0300\n\nfix(label-presets): make preset edits save, keep fields on partial updates, confirm saves (OGC-1227) (#4582)\n\n* fix(label-presets): make preset edits save, keep fields on partial updates, confirm saves (OGC-1227)\n\nThe editor''s PUT was rejected with 400 because it echoed the GET''s field rows\n(id, sourceType, lastupdated) into a DTO that refused unknown properties; a\nclean PUT then failed with 500 because the service cleared and re-added the\nfields in one flush and Hibernate inserts before it deletes orphans, colliding\non the unique (preset_id, display_order) index; and a PUT without a fields key\ncleared the preset''s fields.\n\nThe form now ignores read-only properties, treats a missing fields list as\n\"leave unchanged\" and refuses duplicate keys or positions with a 422. The\nservice reconciles fields by key, parking retained rows on temporary orders and\nflushing before the final orders are written, so row ids survive a save and\nreordering cannot collide. A System preset keeps its stored name whatever case\nthe client sends. The editor sends the declared field shape and the typed name\nand shows the server''s status and reason above the footer when a save is\nrefused; the list confirms a save with a toast and sends Activate/Deactivate as\nPATCH (it POSTed to a PATCH-only endpoint and got 405).\n\n* fix(users): keep what was typed when the user form''s payload is read again\n\nOpening Add from the user list now navigates in-app (#4578), so the form\nmounts with the cached GET /rest/UnifiedSystemUser?ID=0 payload and reads\nit again. That payload stamps systemUserLastupdated with the current time,\nso every read is a new object: handleUserData ran again and replaced the\nform state while the user was typing (the Cypress user-search test saved\n\"Willy Warren\" with the login name \"d\").\n\nThe payload now seeds the form once per user id and again only after a\nsave, where the fresh timestamp is wanted.\n\n* test(e2e): read the OGC-1186 dictionary row''s result cell only\n\nThe row-wide check tripped on the Reference Range column once #4578 began\nshowing a dictionary''s normal entry there.\n\n* fix(label-presets): refuse a null field entry with a 422, keep the HTTP reason out of translated notices\n\nReview of #4582: PUT {\"fields\":[null]} reached replaceFields and answered\n500; the form now names the rule (error.labelpreset.field.required). The\nsave-failure notice no longer appends \"Bad Request\" when the server''s\nmessageKey was translated, and the editor test mocks the uniqueness 422 in\nthe shape the server sends (a fieldError, not a globalError).\n\n* fix(users): seed the form from a fresh read and let a deactivated user be reactivated\n\nReopening a user from the list within the cache window mounted the form on\nthe cached payload; the seed then ran in the same effect flush as the\nuserDataShow effect, whose setValidation spread the initial all-false flags\nand won, so Save stayed disabled until every field was retyped. The form\nnow shows Loading until a read made after mount lands and seeds from that\nread (a user changed elsewhere in between shows the new values), every\nvalidation update is functional, and the flags come from the payload: a\ndeactivated user, whose login row is gone, keeps the names valid and only\nasks for the login name and password.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxGXTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmfQQADTfpO580kzQoGcc9uGnG6ug\n/vCg34pV0SX0Ibdc