owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelmale/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelmale","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/c55eb17a1eae9d14fe23936e2d84f98fd0adeb35/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:22:55Z","email":"samuelsmalek@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Male"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:22:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(order): name a resample''s counterpart by lab number and lock the original on commit (OGC-1269, OGC-1268) (#4575)\n\n* test(order): read back only the panels an order was placed under (OGC-1268)\n\nA panel-member test ordered on its own reads back with no panel, and an\norder placed through a panel reads back with exactly that panel. #4447\nfixed the read-back; these tests drive the real save path and pin it.\n\n* fix(order): name a resample''s counterpart by lab number and lock the original on commit (OGC-1269)\n\nThe acceptance evaluation returns the linked order''s accession in both\ndirections, so both banners show a lab number after a reload instead of\nan internal sample id. A committed resample now marks the original\nrejected at once, so its checklist goes read-only without a reload.\n\n* fix(i18n): restore the comma the develop merge dropped from en.json","tree":{"sha":"66fb302f92766d48d6a1d772a11fa7b76c47fa97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/66fb302f92766d48d6a1d772a11fa7b76c47fa97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/c55eb17a1eae9d14fe23936e2d84f98fd0adeb35","verification":{"payload":"tree 66fb302f92766d48d6a1d772a11fa7b76c47fa97\nparent ed6fbeaf7c655bf49dc03c50a5eae378260ff184\nauthor Samuel Male <samuelsmalek@gmail.com> 1791210175 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791210175 +0300\n\nfix(order): name a resample''s counterpart by lab number and lock the original on commit (OGC-1269, OGC-1268) (#4575)\n\n* test(order): read back only the panels an order was placed under (OGC-1268)\n\nA panel-member test ordered on its own reads back with no panel, and an\norder placed through a panel reads back with exactly that panel. #4447\nfixed the read-back; these tests drive the real save path and pin it.\n\n* fix(order): name a resample''s counterpart by lab number and lock the original on commit (OGC-1269)\n\nThe acceptance evaluation returns the linked order''s accession in both\ndirections, so both banners show a lab number after a reload instead of\nan internal sample id. A committed resample now marks the original\nrejected at once, so its checklist goes read-only without a reload.\n\n* fix(i18n): restore the comma the develop merge dropped from en.json","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw7K/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnjoQAIpUCgAgudYkEaVGlvHtQgKx\nlI9JdjXddMEpQzpZ1Uo4VJYrRCQrKrwD1bOiNis+FAW4Jv+RTRy5C7g9lIxPtS9B\nF5zCyOzvWBkhwgQ5AtUFYsqLHBFaP1CE9/EIOMsTNHomzvL0aRjVpN1kJZGhIYUe\ns8CZkdHF8Y5d9TVvS1lKs0X+itKFHwOfs5r3N45svUWsXX6omCxfBwmxsuMSvyGZ\n8v1TrShxq8DjfhFcFmhUvOTO5LipAhsJj/VZ5lTDX/OptBKLn5HoZgTrfUQBVgjr\n4vEMe3sCruT2sLGpOQKAAn9rE3jcUHlKyO/TXNKJhB3gPEE0G/hOdFYH4gzCGdJL\nW+F97HXecdmqK3mk6WTA6rgvycVchDehli+jS3A+SGviw5OR87aWTSBKcx0vOTYi\n6YezfSqscWDhmvPOou/e+2FuLOogCUo5q7phdqNM9tK/YQ4f6UNjHQBdftHYk9OH\nTPLrmSnwoWcsQA44aNyEO2hF+1Ob07BDcE+y+AZjb0qtv88UWrxg4iratwCo5rr8\n4gto0iPjxrecwdz/Ufm1zvTbzimVoC/jTZEyDXfqmxJ5r/RZdGj2Aa7hr/AJ5QkW\nGlCTD9kKjD6ElSW+cprXHt/eBsntt4berMMHdlrc4S+PUBjwq+ezXpXa7JlJv39z\n7gMIPM49T9BECLVza3lC\n=YXQH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T14:22:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flo