E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/30ce9604a0fc3f035330b5d3b41cee48b283096d","sha":"30ce9604a0fc3f035330b5d3b41cee48b283096d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/30ce9604a0fc3f035330b5d3b41cee48b283096d"}],"sha":"03efbcd940164533ec2cc13c0e3ba4101af9c761","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/03efbcd940164533ec2cc13c0e3ba4101af9c761"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/30ce9604a0fc3f035330b5d3b41cee48b283096d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T02:45:56Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T02:45:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(security): patch log4j, jsoup and qs advisories (#4564)\n\n* chore(security): patch log4j, jsoup and qs advisories\n\nBumps the fixes from the individual Dependabot PRs closed in favor of\ngrouped updates (#4562) that develop did not already have:\n\n- log4j 2.17.1 -> 2.25.5 (log4j-core, -api and -1.2-api advisories).\n  log4j-liquibase is dropped: it was built for Liquibase 3.5, its last\n  release is 2.19.0, and nothing loads it under Liquibase 4.8.\n  The 1.2 bridge now has trace() on Logger only, as log4j 1.2 did, so\n  LogEvent gets a Logger instead of a Category.\n- jsoup 1.15.3 -> 1.23.1\n- qs 6.14.2 -> 6.16.0 (frontend dependency and override)\n\n* fix(test): drop the inactive rolling appender log4j 2.25 rejects\n\nWith log4j 2.25.5 the test log4j2.properties failed to load (\"No type\nattribute provided for component appender\"), so SpringRunner failed to\ninitialize and every Spring test errored: 863 in CI. The config\ndeclared a RollingFile appender that `appenders = console` kept out of\nuse; 2.17.1 ignored it, 2.25.5 rejects it. It was never active, and\nits file name was commented out, so removing it leaves the effective\nconfig unchanged: one console appender, under both versions.","tree":{"sha":"051ad46ec86188f831773e28b7986c6cada483c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/051ad46ec86188f831773e28b7986c6cada483c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/30ce9604a0fc3f035330b5d3b41cee48b283096d","verification":{"payload":"tree 051ad46ec86188f831773e28b7986c6cada483c6\nparent 6bd6da3eff05200e4dd207ed4d30163b1dc35466\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1791168356 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791168356 -0700\n\nchore(security): patch log4j, jsoup and qs advisories (#4564)\n\n* chore(security): patch log4j, jsoup and qs advisories\n\nBumps the fixes from the individual Dependabot PRs closed in favor of\ngrouped updates (#4562) that develop did not already have:\n\n- log4j 2.17.1 -> 2.25.5 (log4j-core, -api and -1.2-api advisories).\n  log4j-liquibase is dropped: it was built for Liquibase 3.5, its last\n  release is 2.19.0, and nothing loads it under Liquibase 4.8.\n  The 1.2 bridge now has trace() on Logger only, as log4j 1.2 did, so\n  LogEvent gets a Logger instead of a Category.\n- jsoup 1.15.3 -> 1.23.1\n- qs 6.14.2 -> 6.16.0 (frontend dependency and override)\n\n* fix(test): drop the inactive rolling appender log4j 2.25 rejects\n\nWith log4j 2.25.5 the test log4j2.properties failed to load (\"No type\nattribute provided for component appender\"), so SpringRunner failed to\ninitialize and every Spring test errored: 863 in CI. The config\ndeclared a RollingFile appender that `appenders = console` kept out of\nuse; 2.17.1 ignored it, 2.25.5 rejects it. It was never active, and\nits file name was commented out, so removing it leaves the effective\nconfig unchanged: one console appender, under both versions.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqww9lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmlcQAFpSWCow3axBnUA0kFDv8JSC\n3WjX6jFM87pVEAlwt9t2QmGlwowda+WlD6KsvQA9jsOB8QVJLyNtvtlgMBq/OMZ4\ncANxN+63OZvvddwPauiuXzUSccgA7xarv62MAqs1N7jyjSIGKHn2VFIEXKLDRt+/\nKNNN7fzMml2l1A0prwclBSxh6ndtVLtK+FgR9zMygesZg3dA/4eUN4ozSAPEJJVX\nCNF0mINVV/z1uKi3YTHqzwHo+haySe+8Zpf786u6SCLF4f7dKHaEPjPdaDefM02A\noZ6y0QQFlV7ZgNc/7PpZ0ZxoI9qd/vukF4vmwkf+WNhuH8txgaRKKAzHQp1fDozQ\nzxaD0V31OHxfJ7WHpMe6DA1f5flWtM8CtoHCWxLtuv3Cdd8uvDPsgrxCo3ksCdfM\n8lcLmd2tOKj2HpDEcrnHwGVpjCmtmI5/VIpu1Yn3jQGHT80gFW72SGskB/bMQIXF\nwCiFDtOgkeQsvAdE1YKw1fPa7+qVHkdEpHxBdnghivBtFh7dnLYtYykfwGP7hxXH\nbdOhnTN5OUcQChytHeuFDIz85YtGAchi8Gj4IMb1DwkiFFOPcleX9/SxBDL8KVpM\n7US786G5coye27wAG1T2gNIZJEJV6Jkl3feDi22KNzBa2fw+T2faXEzpr+n0xUxb\nFn+/iCq/Yq1EbDRhponx\n=nwGy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T02:45:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/30ce9604a0fc3f035330b5d3b41cee48b283096d","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDMwY2U5NjA0YTBmYzNmMDM1MzMwYjVkM2I0MWNlZTQ4YjI4MzA5NmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/6bd6da3eff05200e4dd207ed4d30163b1dc35466","sha":"6bd6da3eff05200e4dd207ed4d30163b1dc35466","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/6bd6da3eff05200e4dd207ed4d30163b1dc35466"}],"sha":"30ce9604a0fc3f035330b5d3b41cee48b283096d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/30ce9604a0fc3f035330b5d3b41cee48b283096d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/6bd6da3eff05200e4dd207ed4d30163b1dc35466/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T02:24:46Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T02:24:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): one monthly Dependabot PR per ecosystem, security fixes grouped (#4562)\n\n* chore(deps): one monthly Dependabot PR per ecosystem, security fixes grouped\n\nWeekly runs with only minor and patch grouped left every major version and\nevery security fix as its own pull request. Version updates now run\nmonthly with a 7-day cooldown, major versions are not proposed (they are\nplanned upgrades), and security fixes for maven, npm and GitHub Actions\narrive as one grouped pull request per ecosystem. Submodule bumps are\ngrouped too.\n\n* chore(deps): drop target-branch so the security groups apply\n\nGitHub''s Dependabot options reference: options defined for a\npackage-ecosystem block that names a target-branch no longer apply to\nsecurity updates, which always use the default branch. develop is the\ndefault branch, so target-branch: develop added nothing and switched\nthe new security groups off.\n\n* chore(deps): state the major-version policy per ecosystem\n\nMaven, npm and Docker majors are migrations we plan and stay ignored; GitHub Actions majors stay in, since they mostly follow runner Node retirements. The header said no majors at all, which the Actions block never matched.\n\n* chore(deps): give submodule bumps the same seven-day cooldown\n\nThe gitsubmodule entry was the only one without it, so submodule bumps could be proposed immediately while every other ecosystem waits seven days. Cooldown is documented as supported for gitsubmodule.\n\n* Potential fix for pull request finding ''Clarify the run-on comment about removing target-branch''\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(deps): rewrite the policy header, including major security fixes\n\nThe autofix left the header broken mid-sentence. It now states the major-version policy per ecosystem; that GitHub documents update-types as a version-update filter while also documenting ignore rules as applying to security updates, so a security fix needing a new major is not guaranteed to open, with the Security tab alert as the backstop; and why target-branch is omitted.","tree":{"sha":"d8be6cc9c1c03bb7b9dedc51a714c0d203b9be9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/d8be6cc9c1c03bb7b9dedc51a714c0d203b9be9b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/6bd6da3eff05200e4dd207ed4d30163b1dc35466","verification":{"payload":"tree d8be6cc9c1c03bb7b9dedc51a714c0d203b9be9b\nparent 8549ea01def0229e3b326c5d57f92368e9bc1bce\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1791167086 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791167086 -0700\n\nchore(deps): one monthly Dependabot PR per ecosystem, security fixes grouped (#4562)\n\n* chore(deps): one monthly Dependabot PR per ecosystem, security fixes grouped\n\nWeekly runs with only minor and patch grouped left every major version and\nevery security fix as its own pull request. Version updates now run\nmonthly with a 7-day cooldown, major versions are not proposed (they are\nplanned upgrades), and security fixes for maven, npm and GitHub Actions\narrive as one grouped pull request per ecosystem. Submodule bumps are\ngrouped too.\n\n* chore(deps): drop target-branch so the security groups apply\n\nGitHub''s Dependabot options reference: options defined for a\npackage-ecosystem block that names a target-branch no longer apply to\nsecurity updates, which always use the default branch. develop is the\ndefault branch, so target-branch: develop added nothing and switched\nthe new security groups off.\n\n* chore(deps): state the major-version policy per ecosystem\n\nMaven, npm and Docker majors are migrations we plan and stay ignored; GitHub Actions majors stay in, since they mostly follow runner Node retirements. The header said no majors at all, which the Actions block never matched.\n\n* chore(deps): give submodule bumps the same seven-day cooldown\n\nThe gitsubmodule entry was the only one without it, so submodule bumps could be proposed immediately while every other ecosystem waits seven days. Cooldown is documented as supported for gitsubmodule.\n\n* Potential fix for pull request finding ''Clarify the run-on comment about removing target-branch''\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(deps): rewrite the policy header, including major security fixes\n\nThe autofix left the header broken mid-sentence. It now states the major-version policy per ecosystem; that GitHub documents update-types as a version-update filter while also documenting ignore rules as applying to security updates, so a security fix needing a new major is not guaranteed to open, with the Security tab alert as the backstop; and why target-branch is omitted.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwwpuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1mQQAHL/K9jovNF6wAtUSSEYyL9M\nkQ+XUos4DgDXcszsdlfWdkL9RZXy9igI5ESNUSePiMG8cM4VTGF8rWh0AGesAf+R\nA9KFsShgMOMw92TbEm+zkZ5qEFsRZfPLAOR90rQZPCQQtVha9CUgSPM3c4CDiFGc\njd+sVRyQrEhOiNNkhOwu9xX+JD8qGWazmb84Bbx3pnxKrrqSvnkbXLs+D++a/CA0\nJ8j9sCOz/HHsemNTIfYpr/nbKFmP0pAOKexYKO9JAlh/oJCbfrwIQK0HAy7n3b2j\n0BiIME6HE5a98gGvVmy/8ZzgiS6Uu5H3mCqbZ7iM02hfL3B4xfbnN/tF0LM07SNY\ngw2IOsehFGKi5U8VrOz1ikm6ETPrEuZpQf0D7FZed0dgV+ztfPfQJVUODKa2xrHC\n9bXcMoMKL3SqWeF24GSoL/KUxt9SFX8HnqDEieoFJ1c4pk1zdJwXOvXmF+4hkih6\n9mnWEoKd2yXyI+RrZ1OjbJUNfSjF4EC98Y3kHIRmqfuEukccLcNHrIyTDiI3mwmo\n0vNtBDQSCo01geeFBTAmX/4NsOZ2o32XcOWZv6W7qOG6RUWUOi/+qlmTOUseFy1o\nP/TamvKEZBM10BMp9Rl+ldamaepaL4/WOXFuwhPiOGy7+kyEch2MNxgMsHXgadIs\n+UMhIe6NF/138ok0zq8a\n=mt25\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T02:24:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/6bd6da3eff05200e4dd207ed4d30163b1dc35466","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDZiZDZkYTNlZmYwNTIwMGU0ZGQyMDdlZDRkMzAxNjNiMWRjMzU0NjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/8549ea01def0229e3b326c5d57f92368e9bc1bce","sha":"8549ea01def0229e3b326c5d57f92368e9bc1bce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/8549ea01def0229e3b326c5d57f92368e9bc1bce"}],"sha":"6bd6da3eff05200e4dd207ed4d30163b1dc35466","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/6bd6da3eff05200e4dd207ed4d30163b1dc35466"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/8549ea01def0229e3b326c5d57f92368e9bc1bce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T00:49:01Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T00:49:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: stop taking runners for publish and merge-conflict runs that do nothing (#4568)\n\n* ci: stop taking runners for publish and merge-conflict runs that do nothing\n\nPublish images / Deploy testing follows every 03 - E2E completion, pull\nrequest builds included, and only found out inside its setup job that a\npull request build has nothing to publish; the always() summary job ran\nafter it. Two runner slots per pull request build, and per cancelled\nbuild, on an org pool of 20. The setup job now skips pull request builds\nin its condition, and the summary skips with it.\n\nAutomation / Merge Conflicts has no concurrency group, and every run\nre-checks all open pull requests, so only the newest matters. A stack\npush queued 24 of them. One group with cancel-in-progress keeps one.\n\n* ci(publish): do not wait for the checkpoints of a cancelled build\n\nA develop push cancels the previous push''s 03 - E2E build, and E2E /\nTests skips a cancelled build, so its checkpoint is never posted. The\npublish workflow still started its poller for that build and held a\nrunner for the full two-hour timeout: four merges in a row this evening\nleft three pollers waiting on checkpoints that could not come.\n\nThe poller now skips a cancelled build; the summary still explains why\nnothing was published.\n\n* test(ci): pin the publish workflow''s admission conditions\n\nThe publication contract tests covered the reporter and the request\nbuilder, not the conditions that keep a runner from being taken for a\npull request build or a cancelled build. A regression there would queue\ntwo jobs per pull request build again without failing anything. The\nnew case asserts the three conditions; it fails against the previous\nworkflow.","tree":{"sha":"0ba53270471edeacb08ce98d52f033d649665b63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/0ba53270471edeacb08ce98d52f033d649665b63"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/8549ea01def0229e3b326c5d57f92368e9bc1bce","verification":{"payload":"tree 0ba53270471edeacb08ce98d52f033d649665b63\nparent 6ff980ab393b9b16c31fd7cfd50599253b8a2cab\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1791161341 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791161341 +0000\n\nci: stop taking runners for publish and merge-conflict runs that do nothing (#4568)\n\n* ci: stop taking runners for publish and merge-conflict runs that do nothing\n\nPublish images / Deploy testing follows every 03 - E2E completion, pull\nrequest builds included, and only found out inside its setup job that a\npull request build has nothing to publish; the always() summary job ran\nafter it. Two runner slots per pull request build, and per cancelled\nbuild, on an org pool of 20. The setup job now skips pull request builds\nin its condition, and the summary skips with it.\n\nAutomation / Merge Conflicts has no concurrency group, and every run\nre-checks all open pull requests, so only the newest matters. A stack\npush queued 24 of them. One group with cancel-in-progress keeps one.\n\n* ci(publish): do not wait for the checkpoints of a cancelled build\n\nA develop push cancels the previous push''s 03 - E2E build, and E2E /\nTests skips a cancelled build, so its checkpoint is never posted. The\npublish workflow still started its poller for that build and held a\nrunner for the full two-hour timeout: four merges in a row this evening\nleft three pollers waiting on checkpoints that could not come.\n\nThe poller now skips a cancelled build; the summary still explains why\nnothing was published.\n\n* test(ci): pin the publish workflow''s admission conditions\n\nThe publication contract tests covered the reporter and the request\nbuilder, not the conditions that keep a runner from being taken for a\npull request build or a cancelled build. A regression there would queue\ntwo jobs per pull request build again without failing anything. The\nnew case asserts the three conditions; it fails against the previous\nworkflow.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwvP9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAG4AQACCVFelKWIr6WDD8DwKzRJbO\nB+zugh/uJFraNUE7gUTXNOF4jLk1DVJhUw2Pzotlwbr6RgprvZkzZp3JdVK/U9Sj\nNFG75awiDNrZqEEx8YVXcY6EZCdWa9OO1aHrQoThI7H2G5mMWQmy+iLp7Hgb2EMG\nDB7yT2x+V6JyCI3uQULdzZodxzMCtfuOiiSptoeSpOJ4G5fjMaWvR6t0hIjsz32r\nsLKmeV1xrHbSpcIYoz6LPv3s4JiJj0QzR921Df+HRa7Curwv8aiMe78Z6FWdhHl4\n+zqVVKtYVN3y8fe8VG/ob1jx597Gt3nHdXpMveP7tddAzNvkm+9PZXZF4BmUdYOy\nJnO7s57VnDjkLo+lpY/hfBlcnDIVELMhhzkk3ekQti3kemeMS2eF0kKiakgyBuPH\nFKrtt7Ag96v6Q0bNyN79D+l1daV6nszHDWbrWT3QdDFC1iuWScbgUNW2GK2Dtj4j\njNAHGWtbWRQyARoJ/smNJw86E4AWtnL5GgAnH0IWOGp8q9tPchKYq4g2xa6YReFX\nplrEgnnw7sm8Ly66nHm1hmZcmtn/4vXz4UQnP7kI0hq1vxMFIp/kYFcVtbR0dRiC\nNtiFNYgHuvr4Z0HRRvMPbsOLA1q/EqVGpDT8F5LUXtK9JpH4p6Bx5U08OWrLrw15\nczx37x+TipI0yUG4Cpjj\n=SucB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T00:49:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/8549ea01def0229e3b326c5d57f92368e9bc1bce","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDg1NDllYTAxZGVmMDIyOWUzYjMyNmM1ZDU3ZjkyMzY4ZTliYzFiY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/6ff980ab393b9b16c31fd7cfd50599253b8a2cab","sha":"6ff980ab393b9b16c31fd7cfd50599253b8a2cab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/6ff980ab393b9b16c31fd7cfd50599253b8a2cab"}],"sha":"8549ea01def0229e3b326c5d57f92368e9bc1bce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/8549ea01def0229e3b326c5d57f92368e9bc1bce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/6ff980ab393b9b16c31fd7cfd50599253b8a2cab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:59:07Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:59:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: cancel a PR''s superseded backend and frontend runs (#4565)\n\nThe org''s runners are shared by every repository on the Free plan, which\nallows 20 concurrent jobs. 01 - Backend and 02 - Frontend had no\nconcurrency group, so every push to a pull request queued a full new\nrun while the previous one kept running or waiting, and a PR with\nseveral pushes held several hour-long backend suites in the queue.\n\nPull request runs now share a group per PR and a new push cancels the\nolder run. Pushes to develop, releases and manual runs each get a group\nof their own and are never cancelled. 03 - E2E already did this.","tree":{"sha":"c8b9c327b889ea6fa2b48472a556732b072aa8ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/c8b9c327b889ea6fa2b48472a556732b072aa8ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/6ff980ab393b9b16c31fd7cfd50599253b8a2cab","verification":{"payload":"tree c8b9c327b889ea6fa2b48472a556732b072aa8ee\nparent 51969e77e6afed0abaf733ab7e5f6009bd3ba1fb\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1791154747 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791154747 -0700\n\nci: cancel a PR''s superseded backend and frontend runs (#4565)\n\nThe org''s runners are shared by every repository on the Free plan, which\nallows 20 concurrent jobs. 01 - Backend and 02 - Frontend had no\nconcurrency group, so every push to a pull request queued a full new\nrun while the previous one kept running or waiting, and a PR with\nseveral pushes held several hour-long backend suites in the queue.\n\nPull request runs now share a group per PR and a new push cancels the\nolder run. Pushes to develop, releases and manual runs each get a group\nof their own and are never cancelled. 03 - E2E already did this.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwto7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8JgQAHoC5AKieI9x3dEP3jG9sATz\nkDktXEfI2wQsTf+hD5LH8mGId7GXsf3SKQ0UoOn8xUH4dBgL8VURF+1dJlNf+LlJ\nlNU5C4K+NLuzpoVoh53T7QhS76yH1XKUGfk1dBsc7+NESuPqyGPm+3s7Igdwb9e8\nBb7yiysHAKSsAIFxCuwsfYgwzzi3IVSCF6OO9kpnzSduy8LJOPfCZUvQchBXWW+o\nagD082j4pHx2bzeSULaLdcRx4zjDUMp6vNcq4FldZTUKfPoUki6SIMozg4pUdOno\nNzHei81JDJxTXWt6hcqfWvQyVA5VdO15f447ucqRkBCweRZQ49WnPI2hJBZZMch3\nqqqQcuxF2wR1M2oBzE1jGy4BYHRe5FDkXVfd4w6oiTZG4UcCXUx4QSZlIQNWBRD1\nqIO/d3/ky7DLJN0sn0gJU7NMl6MXFFeAYLLUR0m481BG7gwhNTMil736mTQjmCVI\nPSSdRae0o+p0jOZ6EYmKX3yAVgBseRbv32oOCsrpO2reqZiUk0nhIHhX9QmQPeTz\nxUaJGNyCvYHvL+UhrMcvXqHNPC+ludbN4zLWClrWPIIW0BHziHmKZLzkPv/Mlons\nLfJOGfIcDsY+R90zrK7cGehcb7LGOmBWpxQKm0uOX2mXaGTGpJ4hec4PQfLvdmY9\nYPnjR4cTYfEzKmmYkm6h\n=/zmc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T22:59:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.co