e5f6009bd3ba1fb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:58:26Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:58:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci-docs): read CI state only from the checks GitHub shows (#4563)\n\n* fix(ci-docs): read CI state only from the checks GitHub shows\n\nRuns started by workflow_run (E2E / Tests) and Dependabot execute on the\ndefault branch, so GitHub files them under develop''s newest commit\nwhichever PR they test. fix-ci and download-ci-logs fell back to\ngh run list --branch when no PR was in scope, and the log downloader\npicked runs the same way: on develop it pulled in other PRs'' E2E\nfailures, and on a PR branch it found no E2E run at all.\n\nThe downloader now takes its runs from the commit''s statusCheckRollup,\nkeeping only the newest run of each check as GitHub does. fix-ci,\ndownload-ci-logs and AGENTS.md name that as the only source for a PR or\nbranch tip, list the queries that disagree with it, and say to open the\nE2E / Tests run while 03 Checkpoint - E2E is pending, since a shard can\nfail long before the checkpoint does. --limit goes with the run listing.\n\n* fix(ci-docs): page through the status rollup and keep the no-PR check\n\nReview findings on the first version:\n\n- The downloader read the first 100 rollup contexts only. A commit\n  re-run many times carries more, and the newest checks would have been\n  cut off silently. Every page is read now.\n- STALE, a check GitHub no longer trusts, fell through as success. It\n  is pending, as gh pr checks reports it.\n- The post-push check in fix-ci had lost the no-PR path that the\n  preflight check keeps. Both now use gh pr checks for a pull request\n  and the downloader''s --list view for a branch tip.","tree":{"sha":"ddc466d8360cf5b15a3723d2672a4203df4468a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/ddc466d8360cf5b15a3723d2672a4203df4468a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/51969e77e6afed0abaf733ab7e5f6009bd3ba1fb","verification":{"payload":"tree ddc466d8360cf5b15a3723d2672a4203df4468a8\nparent 8d8a35537923bfe17c8a46f910e178a04c24548a\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1791154706 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791154706 -0700\n\nfix(ci-docs): read CI state only from the checks GitHub shows (#4563)\n\n* fix(ci-docs): read CI state only from the checks GitHub shows\n\nRuns started by workflow_run (E2E / Tests) and Dependabot execute on the\ndefault branch, so GitHub files them under develop''s newest commit\nwhichever PR they test. fix-ci and download-ci-logs fell back to\ngh run list --branch when no PR was in scope, and the log downloader\npicked runs the same way: on develop it pulled in other PRs'' E2E\nfailures, and on a PR branch it found no E2E run at all.\n\nThe downloader now takes its runs from the commit''s statusCheckRollup,\nkeeping only the newest run of each check as GitHub does. fix-ci,\ndownload-ci-logs and AGENTS.md name that as the only source for a PR or\nbranch tip, list the queries that disagree with it, and say to open the\nE2E / Tests run while 03 Checkpoint - E2E is pending, since a shard can\nfail long before the checkpoint does. --limit goes with the run listing.\n\n* fix(ci-docs): page through the status rollup and keep the no-PR check\n\nReview findings on the first version:\n\n- The downloader read the first 100 rollup contexts only. A commit\n  re-run many times carries more, and the newest checks would have been\n  cut off silently. Every page is read now.\n- STALE, a check GitHub no longer trusts, fell through as success. It\n  is pending, as gh pr checks reports it.\n- The post-push check in fix-ci had lost the no-PR path that the\n  preflight check keeps. Both now use gh pr checks for a pull request\n  and the downloader''s --list view for a branch tip.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwtoSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPrcQABKz8fw+gCYJ9c/0m/zg1KHd\noYlx9TSHNJvEX6ZJjkKDdgFePRwGVU7gXK0ZK7Cx0DV4tZjl7rioQdBy5bGZJZGb\nNM9ZV4l7VhiDu10OxzkFsk/kuST2qq8emto5CAy1FXoA25jzU82GlddXtIAqHwRn\nswU9uUANFzrCHBP3qsGXeokKjBvjQaUcopchzfczvuyQUdvyCBdVbsg46Voc2Tvg\nx7KGbEgq7LlbsUKjF8G4yOgewoPa7GPOgQK3mZmcVojftmXrjpR1P7UoE4nIsiHF\nqTGRzEcBgWJsxKL1fjW6ft1cUiTIh0UJG2E0Gs/unt+UDMePl/PhM5BoVRqfICvZ\ndWuX/TbpxV1IKqEe4LnErjKr+UYjcNYG5ITenbBBT9NknXX3GNLbjH8YOPmnxy+7\nRhF6SOtQIViwL+u2MgunYiCeI/DAN9vJeZnAtJBJt2Mmm/akQfmeJygxYnUQgb94\ndxYm3674tkVsTA0QbaG+zHHMQQUpGnJqHbBWQs7Zo1NhHf5w9muvEaDvj8GE2OaN\n7SgjB/l3zJ5VdQaQnV/sQyRgXT0yYUWBI1hhBIaYw5zwFhtvl4G07euOsmIU9T15\nlN6jBErTSlD1LZoI0F5JhArrFkJcdFbAH/OBcawBCs+Ngvn+S/olDDUuDyXVH10O\nsIl0lTlyj3BJhfNElyv/\n=Wmdi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T22:58:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/51969e77e6afed0abaf733ab7e5f6009bd3ba1fb","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDUxOTY5ZTc3ZTZhZmVkMGFiYWY3MzNhYjdlNWY2MDA5YmQzYmExZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/8d8a35537923bfe17c8a46f910e178a04c24548a","sha":"8d8a35537923bfe17c8a46f910e178a04c24548a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/8d8a35537923bfe17c8a46f910e178a04c24548a"}],"sha":"51969e77e6afed0abaf733ab7e5f6009bd3ba1fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/51969e77e6afed0abaf733ab7e5f6009bd3ba1fb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/8d8a35537923bfe17c8a46f910e178a04c24548a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:57:37Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:57:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: run Build + Test and the frontend checks only on the top of a stack (#4567)\n\n* ci: run Build + Test and the frontend checks only on the top of a stack\n\nGitHub runs every pull request in a stack as if it targeted the stack''s\nbase, so one push of a 20-PR stack starts 20 hour-long backend suites\nand 20 frontend check runs on an org pool of 20 concurrent jobs. The\ntop pull request contains every commit of the stack, so its runs cover\nthem all.\n\nDetect Changes in 01 - Backend and 02 - Frontend now reads the stack\nposition from the pull_request payload. A pull request below the top\nreports its area as unchanged, which skips Build + Test, Static and\nImage the way a change outside the watched paths does, and the\ncheckpoints pass as they already do for a skipped job. Formatting and\nthe deployment contract still run on every pull request. Missing or\nmalformed stack metadata runs everything.\n\n* ci: filter the top of a stack against the stack''s base\n\nReview finding on the first version, verified: dorny/paths-filter reads\na pull request''s own files when it has a token, and the top of a stack\nis one layer (17 files for the top of today''s stack, against 252 on its\nbranch). A backend change in a lower layer under a frontend-only top\nwould have skipped Build + Test for the whole stack with green\ncheckpoints.\n\nFor the top of a stack the filter now runs with no token and base set\nto the stack''s base branch, so it diffs the checkout against develop\nwith git and the lower layers'' changes count. Every other pull request\nkeeps the ordinary filter.","tree":{"sha":"d4f17f9599b80dfcc5459bf254368bd1680b68d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/d4f17f9599b80dfcc5459bf254368bd1680b68d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/8d8a35537923bfe17c8a46f910e178a04c24548a","verification":{"payload":"tree d4f17f9599b80dfcc5459bf254368bd1680b68d2\nparent 13cad83aecc2e6d6b63e48ca25d51fcbcb599d13\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1791154657 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791154657 -0700\n\nci: run Build + Test and the frontend checks only on the top of a stack (#4567)\n\n* ci: run Build + Test and the frontend checks only on the top of a stack\n\nGitHub runs every pull request in a stack as if it targeted the stack''s\nbase, so one push of a 20-PR stack starts 20 hour-long backend suites\nand 20 frontend check runs on an org pool of 20 concurrent jobs. The\ntop pull request contains every commit of the stack, so its runs cover\nthem all.\n\nDetect Changes in 01 - Backend and 02 - Frontend now reads the stack\nposition from the pull_request payload. A pull request below the top\nreports its area as unchanged, which skips Build + Test, Static and\nImage the way a change outside the watched paths does, and the\ncheckpoints pass as they already do for a skipped job. Formatting and\nthe deployment contract still run on every pull request. Missing or\nmalformed stack metadata runs everything.\n\n* ci: filter the top of a stack against the stack''s base\n\nReview finding on the first version, verified: dorny/paths-filter reads\na pull request''s own files when it has a token, and the top of a stack\nis one layer (17 files for the top of today''s stack, against 252 on its\nbranch). A backend change in a lower layer under a frontend-only top\nwould have skipped Build + Test for the whole stack with green\ncheckpoints.\n\nFor the top of a stack the filter now runs with no token and base set\nto the stack''s base branch, so it diffs the checkout against develop\nwith git and the lower layers'' changes count. Every other pull request\nkeeps the ordinary filter.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwtnhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+18QAAasI1iLNgbA7qDS7rkKanQK\n/n+qwG4pU2uxItS4Wj+HNL0J/KCkbvS4V/NmnIfzmrfUWBIzKFxFrni1uMGOj9+5\nMJVi8q2WG2HobBsnKYC/w/1Lr0sdAwP/nGp/jUXvma0wICWHsnkN7AIcb+gjnvqh\nwWxVuE3EfwkNQwzs1BwZqOx0o/eyef5P2jv0zKEWEVoXy+mhosCIvFbojthsIuzR\n0PoVsHNZAq+5tgvBNoe1VimW0uUga8nZAWs8wMS61Q5b6H/fhj9H+eZbRrcvSDrq\nrYzea8kyB+YKOttLY/byWHe6HgglzC7qpLAXXxnwkoCmQj9H/r0WzcWDXGYHZZW+\nD6V9q8pOiuIkT6TMvT3Nmxm6h6DN3YO7Jl4hCPmbR51jN0GHKbPncqxWLNLgKehj\n0aIdNg2jKkzB1uUAmpd3xMo5VQToabPHLrszvPDpUBeaXjQSScH84RJV+fT5uvW9\no1rd+z