ers/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/13cad83aecc2e6d6b63e48ca25d51fcbcb599d13/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:56:58Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:56:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(e2e): run E2E on the top of a stack and report its result to the stack (#4566)\n\n* ci(e2e): run E2E only on the top pull request of a stack\n\nGitHub runs every pull request in a stack as if it targeted the stack''s\nbase, so the branch filter on 03 - E2E never applies to a stack and a\n20-PR stack runs the full E2E pipeline 20 times per push: 20 Shared\nBuilds and about 400 test jobs on an org pool of 20 concurrent jobs.\nTwo pushes of such a stack filled the queue for most of 2026-10-04.\n\nThe top pull request of a stack contains every commit of the stack, so\nits run covers them all. A pull request below the top now skips E2E the\nsame way a documentation-only change does: its own 03 - E2E skips the\nShared Build, and E2E / Tests re-decides from the default branch''s copy\nof e2e-scope.cjs, reading the stack position from the REST pull request\nobject, then posts the checkpoint as success with the reason in its\ndescription. Missing or malformed stack metadata runs E2E.\n\n* ci(e2e): hold lower stack members pending until the top reports to them\n\nReview findings on the first version, each verified:\n\n- The reporter''s new toJSON(...) expression was not substituted by\n  test_publication_workflow.py, which runs in deployment-contract on\n  every pull request, so merging would have failed 01 Checkpoint -\n  Backend repo-wide. The harness now substitutes every expression and\n  asserts none is left.\n- The top of a stack was judged on its own layer: the pull request\n  files API lists one layer (17 files for the top of today''s stack,\n  against 252 on its branch), so a docs-only top layer above code\n  changes would have skipped E2E for the whole stack. The top is now\n  judged on the comparison from the stack''s base; GitHub cuts that list\n  at 300 files, and a list that long runs E2E.\n- A lower pull request got a green checkpoint before, and regardless\n  of, the top''s result. It now gets pending, and the top''s run posts\n  its own result on every lower pull request whose head it contains. A\n  lower pull request pushed after the stack was built stays pending\n  until the stack is rebuilt.\n- stack.number is validated like position and size.","tree":{"sha":"5838fdf5f19a72fc1cd92aba015e2ba04de9da2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/5838fdf5f19a72fc1cd92aba015e2ba04de9da2d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/13cad83aecc2e6d6b63e48ca25d51fcbcb599d13","verification":{"payload":"tree 5838fdf5f19a72fc1cd92aba015e2ba04de9da2d\nparent cc9e332df202142fc2861ebde1e1e055eee2a4f1\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1791154618 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791154618 -0700\n\nci(e2e): run E2E on the top of a stack and report its result to the stack (#4566)\n\n* ci(e2e): run E2E only on the top pull request of a stack\n\nGitHub runs every pull request in a stack as if it targeted the stack''s\nbase, so the branch filter on 03 - E2E never applies to a stack and a\n20-PR stack runs the full E2E pipeline 20 times per push: 20 Shared\nBuilds and about 400 test jobs on an org pool of 20 concurrent jobs.\nTwo pushes of such a stack filled the queue for most of 2026-10-04.\n\nThe top pull request of a stack contains every commit of the stack, so\nits run covers them all. A pull request below the top now skips E2E the\nsame way a documentation-only change does: its own 03 - E2E skips the\nShared Build, and E2E / Tests re-decides from the default branch''s copy\nof e2e-scope.cjs, reading the stack position from the REST pull request\nobject, then posts the checkpoint as success with the reason in its\ndescription. Missing or malformed stack metadata runs E2E.\n\n* ci(e2e): hold lower stack members pending until the top reports to them\n\nReview findings on the first version, each verified:\n\n- The reporter''s new toJSON(...) expression was not substituted by\n  test_publication_workflow.py, which runs in deployment-contract on\n  every pull request, so merging would have failed 01 Checkpoint -\n  Backend repo-wide. The harness now substitutes every expression and\n  asserts none is left.\n- The top of a stack was judged on its own layer: the pull request\n  files API lists one layer (17 files for the top of today''s stack,\n  against 252 on its branch), so a docs-only top layer above code\n  changes would have skipped E2E for the whole stack. The top is now\n  judged on the comparison from the stack''s base; GitHub cuts that list\n  at 300 files, and a list that long runs E2E.\n- A lower pull request got a green checkpoint before, and regardless\n  of, the top''s result. It now gets pending, and the top''s run posts\n  its own result on every lower pull request whose head it contains. A\n  lower pull request pushed after the stack was built stays pending\n  until the stack is rebuilt.\n- stack.number is validated like position and size.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwtm6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW2gQAHE4+dGJ//obz2Vw6ESRKeKT\nY1KqDa3nLLgatrfSbC56GamDHufhY71bqRwJP4cfo57iARWfh/OChOPV433/ExwC\nyzvAjV7bWogJdR+gAn1SQuhnLLCWyOg9smt7P34ZrBWOVclanTOOViCCEQC9wLSy\nO2GkHBtqBphaWLmiDd5DG2qXQUfaoumMPahxVCseoEfGAAjbKEYBBrD5amTD1Ul0\nPXyZsJjbsIk6Fse7xS5XX8SCNl1kocBzB3f3RQe633qVhjCAZkmgjeDnXSGrphHv\nrTNBnEYMHQwqzpoDte3Gy4xgwiZX19Sqx4OX2f1Vu3wyxYPhfdtjJKO43mE/z0Y9\nhNFjo5KQPNtZC0C8O3b1SNKaI5NxwY60s+vTzNHgofVeff6FImjHz/YAFjtiBDaR\nR0wZnnWqffExoOdQZqGG4Lk9C/xHgzdZuJtjU9LDAdLOkFocPFkW4A2QjfJAmYZq\nZ1pow9vnr2MF+SqfubHUvwYZP+tR60/CmmVuFvxov6YQFn/uSXr+Bn1aqQ3+Etky\nFngrLkYmCe4lXxNayZR14dMWrgzgccUVEpoV45H0zf3RkDwBKcDVLf0WLCTjIqeS\nYTQzDyelGHEbB9Ws/wNSd9NwutlV54KiJa9eUd81EjwuWQgT3+7adOe+pGeryvmH\nk4EcnGvo5qN5Z3pT4wZQ\n=6vwy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T22:56:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/13cad83aecc2e6d6b63e