/api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/ca6d6fd19b286ded643dd27d452669dfd51ecdb3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:03:23Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:03:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(security): upgrade Spring Security 6.2.8 -> 6.5.11 (#4524)\n\nCVE-2026-22732 (critical): under some conditions Spring Security does\nnot write the configured HTTP response headers, which here are the\nContent-Security-Policy and X-Frame-Options set in SecurityConfig. The\n6.2 line has no fixed release; 6.5.11 is the 6.x release that has it.\nIt also clears CVE-2025-22228 (BCrypt password length) in\nspring-security-crypto.\n\n6.5.11 is built against Spring Framework 6.2.17 and keeps OpenSAML\n4.3.2, so it runs on the Spring 6.2.19 and OpenSAML already in the WAR.\nMain and test sources compile with no deprecation warnings from the\nsecurity configuration.","tree":{"sha":"edafc160aa628306837e09ac3b1d44e5cf486f5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/edafc160aa628306837e09ac3b1d44e5cf486f5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/ca6d6fd19b286ded643dd27d452669dfd51ecdb3","verification":{"payload":"tree edafc160aa628306837e09ac3b1d44e5cf486f5a\nparent f77840b163cead7eef80ce4f084e4629c8feb218\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1791126203 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791126203 -0700\n\nchore(security): upgrade Spring Security 6.2.8 -> 6.5.11 (#4524)\n\nCVE-2026-22732 (critical): under some conditions Spring Security does\nnot write the configured HTTP response headers, which here are the\nContent-Security-Policy and X-Frame-Options set in SecurityConfig. The\n6.2 line has no fixed release; 6.5.11 is the 6.x release that has it.\nIt also clears CVE-2025-22228 (BCrypt password length) in\nspring-security-crypto.\n\n6.5.11 is built against Spring Framework 6.2.17 and keeps OpenSAML\n4.3.2, so it runs on the Spring 6.2.19 and OpenSAML already in the WAR.\nMain and test sources compile with no deprecation warnings from the\nsecurity configuration.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwmq7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7RoQAKlApJdoe9PMGyqwjfSa/9LO\nxgRvuQBxwauDtFUr6Dosds98rFHdR9my5RW6bBqW/p6SB7ML70wDF05P5H85zX3l\nSdnXzIbx2uiAW+SKiw9R+YSdTSN3ca29abNMF9bdZCd/+sKLaGGBFofj3zcvHzkZ\nSXp3ISedHkqtiwQECF7TOft93FXWwJzFpFKrb/wHtqH11RlfXIfoI1nRhvRL3Z9O\nxDzZp61LGZJgImVZHljG+Wa5gF6jx0YQJ0NT3o3vSb4GfCHzuo9J4kLiqWaWPT7R\nEgVEccmTlU2NANIW3qgPP6YSqDBG+PuFt5TDGsY1AStctE9hyjeMQNqPrZPKHFLo\ns0k7naqz19xfBxnxqq2z5qAzCgrVqQe+MLkDR0mxJhxoGsmWqKoYEP37bdgDu6VG\nUmSS5MAcQysYJPC0cethpIvxDGpmgTYAX+/1vUFE0YXTZCtQJDJUjihZ8TKLK04u\npA2zTWLHOzD2hA1tDrUI+xc9rFyxLeVDJAZW4Ys+DEUgHbFEfgyJPg2knrNUNyuK\nXIo6dBdv8dAGQSwBiPffypoio8FIbL2uYvoidQu2m1SVyLhgG4B8zMaZbGLiD1OG\nJYyvoEkTJGZDJXm5pogDkvg3Ok4q5ek0y6NjqGeaozqosglL1XQqj8APYf6SZiF7\nmBPmWpH1Yh4BUEBavYyp\n=Vfer\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T15:03:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/ca6d6fd19b286ded643dd27d452669dfd51ecdb3","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKGNhNmQ2ZmQxOWIyODZkZWQ2NDNkZDI3ZDQ1MjY2OWRmZDUxZWNkYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/f77840b163cead7eef80ce4f084e4629c8feb218","sha":"f77840b163cead7eef80ce4f084e4629c8feb218","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/f77840b163cead7eef80ce4f084e4629c8feb218"}],"sha":"ca6d6fd19b286ded643dd27d452669dfd51ecdb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/ca6d6fd19b286ded643dd27d452669dfd51ecdb3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/f77840b163cead7eef80ce4f084e4629c8feb218/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:03:22Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:03:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(security): drop async-http-client, align Netty, remove unused c3p0 (#4523)\n\nweb-push 5.1.1 brings async-http-client 2.10.4, which brings Netty\n4.1.42 and pins jose4j 0.7.0. Only web-push''s PushAsyncService uses\nasync-http-client; NotificationRestController sends through the\nsynchronous PushService, which runs on Apache HttpClient 4. The client\nis excluded and jose4j is managed at 0.9.7. WebPushRequestTest builds a\nVAPID-signed, aes128gcm-encrypted request the way the controller does,\nwithout async-http-client on the classpath.\n\nThe remaining Netty modules came from modbus-tcp 2.1.5 at 4.1.131. The\nNetty BOM is imported at 4.1.138.Final and modbus moves to 2.1.6, so the\nWAR carries one Netty version.\n\nc3p0 0.9.5.4 was declared directly and also arrived through Quartz.\nThe DataSource is a JNDI lookup and quartz.properties uses RAMJobStore,\nso neither pool is used: the direct dependency is removed and c3p0 and\nmchange-commons-java are excluded from Quartz. In Quartz only\nC3p0PoolingConnectionProvider and a JDBC job store delegate reference\nmchange.","tree":{"sha":"aaedb1a16778c72f873e1f89c3601fde49b46528","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/aaedb1a16778c72f873e1f89c3601fde49b46528"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/f77840b163cead7eef80ce4f084e4629c8feb218","verification":{"payload":"tree aaedb1a16778c72f873e1f89c3601fde49b46528\nparent 64d7c86b5dc57d005d77c7d88f3ed68319f7c24f\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1791126202 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791126202 -0700\n\nchore(security): drop async-http-client, align Netty, remove unused c3p0 (#4523)\n\nweb-push 5.1.1 brings async-http-client 2.10.4, which brings Netty\n4.1.42 and pins jose4j 0.7.0. Only web-push''s PushAsyncService uses\nasync-http-client; NotificationRestController sends through the\nsynchronous PushService, which runs on Apache HttpClient 4. The client\nis excluded and jose4j is managed at 0.9.7. WebPushRequestTest builds a\nVAPID-signed, aes128gcm-encrypted request the way the controller does,\nwithout async-http-client on the classpath.\n\nThe remaining Netty modules came from modbus-tcp 2.1.5 at 4.1.131. The\nNetty BOM is imported at 4.1.138.Final and modbus moves to 2.1.6, so the\nWAR carries one Netty version.\n\nc3p0 0.9.5.4 was declared directly and also arrived through Quartz.\nThe DataSource is a JNDI lookup and quartz.properties uses RAMJobStore,\nso neither pool is used: the direct dependency is removed and c3p0 and\nmchange-commons-java are excluded from Quartz. In Quartz only\nC3p0PoolingConnectionProvider and a JDBC job store delegate reference\nmchange.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwmq7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyZoQAGokHYCca4xBDqmyww/xavib\nwFyHyvuzRUnXhnkzvwwWZ8DNeTWL2PKWGfUToF3fW0Cr59C4O3J80CWTDGhqQZfo\nbC7R+3ei26Z9q/8urrK9A0PUsEDRhBo67IhYRsHcqiWWtDaOE/+omeSd6kbxq8jK\nP2XbWNIrzqbWQaM8fyjxZexy+KfBsr/0eXLq9Z4ZNEOZHO08sa2BcG3mfgWlCFQt\n5i53QDGoEDNTUW4C81jYiCdu8kMrbeCke/RFXUFT6QB62r4W6fJDRQg/+OOytD8w\nvTSyDXXdGMxhtVims/LAQYSH9yPp24iqgoXwauruTRwTT1Wlc1Rb9/VFup5BsEHf\n3Dy0USdMY/rRMYlwYWFGO8JAKUSbpEP+DW9/cXZO+Fpb5qnb0kN+bcB5tme1o84f\nErfR/Lym/WZYPvUeVAe5Fb6q1q7AqUUaDtqwIx2YMWiCIXRvdtGooZAWctEcthQ+\nSIp7yKkoWbk1X/B5hjbwqJmT0FokJCUPV/UXSPF07tYpNu/8xI8LLqcceysRrnlL\n53OUIww1/Ungggx1PyGX5CaHIoPSUW7dPwQq5YiGKgnqRN1JvkpC4IPbk+CWtbpW\nvug3bI8R/c/2p9wc4Jr2TGr53VzPkKbSIkFc9Q23QK7ZsVo8RXfyjf9xJXEzVfn2\nrZJaHXnCbNqXrzzJ0UDh\n=+UN/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T15:03:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/pri