starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/5352403cd560bbc6c422af2624840c1944c2d8b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:03:21Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:03:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(security): scan only the shipped WAR and remove the catalyst submodule (#4519)\n\nThe backend dependency snapshot scanned the whole workspace after the\nbuild, so it reported submodule lockfiles (catalyst uv.lock files and the\nbridge package-lock.json) and every jar twice, once from the exploded\ntarget/OpenELIS-Global directory and once from the war. Most open\nDependabot alerts came from those entries rather than from anything\nOpenELIS ships.\n\nThe snapshot now comes from target/OpenELIS-Global.war. The workflow,\njob and artifact-name are unchanged, so the action''s correlator is the\nsame and this snapshot replaces the previous one instead of adding a\nsecond.\n\nprojects/catalyst was pinned to its May extraction commit and nothing in\nCI or the application consumed it. The submodule and the OGC-070 spec\nfolder are removed; the project lives in DIGI-UW/openelis-catalyst.\nThe pre-commit hook README no longer describes the Catalyst Python lint\nthe hook stopped running, and the worktree docs no longer state a\nsubmodule count.","tree":{"sha":"23e8f9272a4dde989c376f2e582b54825c2230f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/23e8f9272a4dde989c376f2e582b54825c2230f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/5352403cd560bbc6c422af2624840c1944c2d8b7","verification":{"payload":"tree 23e8f9272a4dde989c376f2e582b54825c2230f5\nparent 18a36abf5a25de889aa63b51d0ce52ba53330f5b\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1791126201 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791126201 -0700\n\nchore(security): scan only the shipped WAR and remove the catalyst submodule (#4519)\n\nThe backend dependency snapshot scanned the whole workspace after the\nbuild, so it reported submodule lockfiles (catalyst uv.lock files and the\nbridge package-lock.json) and every jar twice, once from the exploded\ntarget/OpenELIS-Global directory and once from the war. Most open\nDependabot alerts came from those entries rather than from anything\nOpenELIS ships.\n\nThe snapshot now comes from target/OpenELIS-Global.war. The workflow,\njob and artifact-name are unchanged, so the action''s correlator is the\nsame and this snapshot replaces the previous one instead of adding a\nsecond.\n\nprojects/catalyst was pinned to its May extraction commit and nothing in\nCI or the application consumed it. The submodule and the OGC-070 spec\nfolder are removed; the project lives in DIGI-UW/openelis-catalyst.\nThe pre-commit hook README no longer describes the Catalyst Python lint\nthe hook stopped running, and the worktree docs no longer state a\nsubmodule count.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwmq5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd2QQAJ3WN6vHjYqvpUc+uTp11f31\nDo3mlULwJNqm9IIpMtd17XOli1yHbpAGvdxLwRJSr+QUZmDaXk9bkGRLK7OPZb6i\nKYH3PBSmW8YNV2YtsNByroZc3NffNjNq1gv74IJrrvuYXuA6vMGD782JKM5sctsz\nAQ93UnbzhgHZGR0IcPQku3lYUGxwWwwhemCJaWraGWF4C43SSY+Ilc8WjeE++Tn8\n5BCIuxIoQWiZeuMP1EyNouAZ9G9YF4KXn1smM621Ecqvow7gFW33A/HDo54o3voj\n4uCYItS8E365su4xeIG7lz8KUMtl/vu3E93VYtFG887NRAl4kCvxoBF1HPw4ZPEK\nKWgeddPi5J6F/wH1eoqiHnoz5c3I7GLCh0FaGlk7wiw6Noy1dSt3NnfrQ2F4IpjF\nMxg31dajLOHc8iL87N3Roys4Y7Lox2aMQr4Wb1BtaE0UB7FX7VpDAJ7YCQv0vPcJ\nXzlCC7qazLnkd1gS3Rf30exSkSkMil7QjJsz81cR1u6cBeSmdM9tZx3ZEsyIkTW6\nsKy6ncSSvRtcqBvy6iI56olwkRdIqfsqZw49lPzyIvLGf6jXuiieNQH5B+FEhpTJ\nXbh6+qYILl62I/Rbe8pn3739ZZYF/BupxOnPWqpvQT5kzbjzUdIFeJIJLmF130h3\neJJqsKkXq4BTLkfYl4eT\n=R3Pl\n-----END PGP 