:"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/404a995184d268148cd9436eb6fa459547245f8b","sha":"404a995184d268148cd9436eb6fa459547245f8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/404a995184d268148cd9436eb6fa459547245f8b"}],"sha":"18a36abf5a25de889aa63b51d0ce52ba53330f5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/18a36abf5a25de889aa63b51d0ce52ba53330f5b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/404a995184d268148cd9436eb6fa459547245f8b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T20:24:05Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T20:24:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(testing): make test isolation a MUST (constitution V.7) (#4473)\n\n* docs(testing): make test isolation a MUST (constitution V.7)\n\nThe guidance defined isolation only as not reusing another test''s browser\nstate. Specs share one database per stack, and nothing told authors to write\nand read only their own data, so aggregate assertions over a date window\ndepended on which specs happened to share a shard.\n\nAdds V.7 with one invariant for every test level, replaces the ''prefer\nisolated tests'' bullet, and carries the rules into the testing roadmap\n(U4, E5, E6), the Playwright guide, and the playwright skill.\nConstitution 1.11.2 -> 1.12.0.\n\n* docs(testing): address isolation rule review feedback\n\nCarry mandatory isolation into generated feature plans and restrict shared baseline fixtures to read-only reference data. Require explicit dates and controlled clocks for current-time behavior across the constitution, guides, and Playwright skill. Addresses both review comments on PR #4473.","tree":{"sha":"dd6636b9d8d36890a52c1cd82f620cd30bc3849d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/dd6636b9d8d36890a52c1cd82f620cd30bc3849d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/404a995184d268148cd9436eb6fa459547245f8b","verification":{"payload":"tree dd6636b9d8d36890a52c1cd82f620cd30bc3849d\nparent 46539d7d619011b71c1330eb308839434f0e0aa4\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1791059045 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791059045 -0700\n\ndocs(testing): make test isolation a MUST (constitution V.7) (#4473)\n\n* docs(testing): make test isolation a MUST (constitution V.7)\n\nThe guidance defined isolation only as not reusing another test''s browser\nstate. Specs share one database per stack, and nothing told authors to write\nand read only their own data, so aggregate assertions over a date window\ndepended on which specs happened to share a shard.\n\nAdds V.7 with one invariant for every test level, replaces the ''prefer\nisolated tests'' bullet, and carries the rules into the testing roadmap\n(U4, E5, E6), the Playwright guide, and the playwright skill.\nConstitution 1.11.2 -> 1.12.0.\n\n* docs(testing): address isolation rule review feedback\n\nCarry mandatory isolation into generated feature plans and restrict shared baseline fixtures to read-only reference data. Require explicit dates and controlled clocks for current-time behavior across the constitution, guides, and Playwright skill. Addresses both review comments on PR #4473.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwWRlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzi4QACs7VsJxk866GEsGgEi/kGPP\nnItgRRY0aXWNBVHNeZBiNkSh4jnurm0MVFY96UHJhWSnE4Y32f1xKAOI2kd4IL7v\nEbhuUKe6EegItLj+anTZ1+MEWCvvVu70cMGcLrG0UZkVZp2EX9IfpDLlHL2bqIce\nvdq3SeXXdINqloOmhnENNlKq9daquDANG5fYJjrffBq1EV1j8Q1fV1E5BLJRNabm\nuXkpi3dBL9C+MyZzxFNi+Y3yDABBgzc+Vpi/TQSvZtAa+5jbpnWWAZeVUpe7jzDh\nNiAz6uk59R8BNEG40BeW62aKhxxYmIDoWXbwhONl+zKKNMwr4rGgsWzlKAlwSfE7\n4FE+HGXMWMRMNcRdm3X1DjQa0JqhtbvsumJ0EUyL7ZlE4VTOY6OXY8vA4WcATZ7U\nju8dLgmsiml+IjAss0N/S1eXoCljyLvWBPeEUNsXVPbiE5dbMtSGc2sjSmuVeK+D\nKbAcS7Qk2SZRbFJP4HZla9Ai/RsAqYG8ETyi8enuMUtYMOXKl/mK0VR7q5KGOh3o\n/3m+oiUB0/5wtvZY5XLhLyJLmNzEf/MXztG80u5mxvYqZCFgzDl1xS7oJCtA8MNX\nHogIAJ/5o08+lMus9OAoDiKb8QofrJxi4HipfWqmOGX98TW+5qDih2vM2vt7RIRt\n/JGY4I+HNSiiqM3c+An7\n=TfnZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T20:24:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/404a995184d268148cd9436eb6fa459547245f8b","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDQwNGE5OTUxODRkMjY4MTQ4Y2Q5NDM2ZWI2ZmE0NTk1NDcyNDVmOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/46539d7d619011b71c1330eb308839434f0e0aa4","sha":"46539d7d619011b71c1330eb308839434f0e0aa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/46539d7d619011b71c1330eb308839434f0e0aa4"}],"sha":"404a995184d268148cd9436eb6fa459547245f8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/404a995184d268148cd9436eb6fa459547245f8b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29783151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/46539d7d619011b71c1330eb308839434f0e0aa4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:56:28Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:56:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: retire the legacy Test Management and Results Entry pages (#4528)\n\n* refactor: retire the legacy Test Management and Results Entry pages\n\nTest Management now links only to the domain- and component-aware editors\n(Test Catalogue, Panels, Sample Types, Lab Units, Methods, Catalogue import)\nplus the rule pages. The legacy add/modify/rename/manage/view pages are\nremoved; their addresses redirect to the editor that replaced each one.\n\nThe legacy Results Entry pages and the resultsEntryUnifiedRoute switch are\nremoved: /Results is the only results page. Old addresses redirect to it\nwith the accession or patient carried over, Liquibase 117 retires the\nswitch and the legacy menu rows, and the Notebook results modal and the\nImmunohistochemistry case view embed the unified table instead of the\nlegacy one.\n\nFixes found while testing the new pages:\n- a lab number typed with a Lab Unit selected was ignored; both now apply\n- result flag chips rendered gray; Critical/Abnormal colours now show\n- Manage Methods did not list a new method until reload, and a taken name\n  returned 200 with nothing saved; it is now a 409 the page explains\n- the notebook audit trail and sample locations never loaded (an error\n  callback was passed where getFromOpenElisServer takes an AbortSignal)\n- prop warnings on the Reflex and Calculated Value forms\n\n* fix: IHC and Cytology results stored a raw message key; review follow-ups\n\n- Finalizing an Immunohistochemistry or Cytology case stored the raw\n  \"see report\" message key as the result (the IHC key was missing, the\n  Cytology one misspelled). Both keys now exist; Liquibase 118 repairs\n  rows already stored.\n- Results Entry is on the menu allow-list, so sites with menu autocreate\n  keep it.\n- The referral critical-result alert links to /Results?accessionNumber=.\n- A date + lab number test pins the other keepAccession branches.\n- Stale mentions of the retired results switch removed.\n\n* test(e2e): the merge-screen paging test seeds its own two patients\n\nIt searched both merge panels for \"a\" and expected the second panel to list\nsomeone besides the patient chosen in the first. On CI''s database that\nsearch matches one patient, which the screen correctly hides from the\nsecond panel, so the test failed on develop in most recent runs. It now\nseeds two patients sharing a unique last name and checks each by name.\n\n* test: method-create refusal test seeds the roles it grants\n\nA method create grants the Results and Validation roles by name. Other\nfixtures truncate the shared role seed, so in the full suite the lookup\nreturned a stub (id -1) and the insert failed on the role foreign key.\nThe test now seeds both roles when absent, as its sibling tests do.","tree":{"sha":"462e8879fbe654f7ff0828f5e5d685a43829c9c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/462e8879fbe654f7ff0828f5e5d685a43829c9c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/46539d7d619011b71c1330eb308839434f0e0aa4","verification":{"payload":"tree 462e8879fbe654f7ff0828f5e5d685a43829c9c5\nparent 420f1a48a86b8b78111c65af416f5288136256cb\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1791024988 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791024988 +0300\n\nrefactor: retire the legacy Test Management and Results Entry pages (#4528)\n\n* refactor: retire the legacy Test Management and Results Entry pages\n\nTest Management now links only to the domain- and component-aware editors\n(Test Catalogue, Panels, Sample Types, Lab Units, Methods, Catalogue import)\nplus the rule pages. The legacy add/modify/rename/manage/view pages are\nremoved; their addresses redirect to the editor that replaced each one.\n\nThe legacy Results Entry pages and the resultsEntryUnifiedRoute switch are\nremoved: /Results is the only results page. Old addresses redirect to it\nwith the accession or patient carried over, Liquibase 117 retires the\nswitch and the legacy menu rows, and the Notebook results modal and the\nImmunohistochemistry case view embed the unified table instead of the\nlegacy one.\n\nFixes found while testing the new pages:\n- a lab number typed with a Lab Unit selected was ignored; both now apply\n- result flag chips rendered gray; Critical/Abnormal colours now show\n- Manage Methods did not list a new method until reload, and a taken name\n  returned 200 with nothing saved; it is now a 409 the page explains\n- the notebook audit trail and sample locations never loaded (an error\n  callback was passed where getFromOpenElisServer takes an AbortSignal)\n- prop warnings on the Reflex and Calculated Value forms\n\n* fix: IHC and Cytology results stored a raw message key; review follow-ups\n\n- Finalizing an Immunohistochemistry or Cytology case stored the raw\n  \"see report\" message key as the result (the IHC key was missing, the\n  Cytology one misspelled). Both keys now exist; Liquibase 118 repairs\n  rows already stored.\n- Results Entry is on the menu allow-list, so sites with menu autocreate\n  keep it.\n- The referral critical-result alert links to /Results?accessionNumber=.\n- A date + lab number test pins the other keepAccession branches.\n- Stale mentions of the retired results switch removed.\n\n* test(e2e): the merge-screen paging test seeds its own two patients\n\nIt searched both merge panels for \"a\" and expected the second panel to list\nsomeone besides the patient chosen in the first. On CI''s database that\nsearch matches one patient, which the screen correctly hides from the\nsecond panel, so the test failed on develop in most recent runs. It now\nseeds two patients sharing a unique last name and checks each by name.\n\n* test: method-create refusal test seeds the roles it grants\n\nA method create grants the Results and Validation roles by name. Other\nfixtures truncate the shared role seed, so in the full suite the lookup\nreturned a stub (id -1) and the insert failed on the role foreign key.\nThe test now seeds both roles when absent, as its sibling tests do.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwN9cCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXYEQAEvTmbkiNPVwz6j37ce+zSY+\nnquYdSbkPvQLDnSAjddu1f2iyVY3tbf6UkSsSkN1n2kW4Cn3L0UeQqp6oPpXOzCv\naIh7IhGizlK9H+3ibNx4ymTOLoFibOPgqNUjaxrOZlgLxg4Cuh8FXVAlE6OqCfYF\nqhGxVpxOiIrVkijDbA307vHkpw1hr6NYba6mSVkq8rg4shG4q0rKk/m+uJPGCWPG\n7oRF227PLSUkAyZeA1aXe7FNuH33r4T3uWIyfsSm0sxVTL/yGKcJW267uySmRyE7\ncS5v9evtuv0Ah5IMvuWYmVl6CLhtwy2MDowRU0rXKLxzsiQmjTMEiYKgppdp0M02\n5ZprIDqnk401ipAlOwoHemtTfrah9iJQ8XSf2iwgHtT4DI8/H8vdrXSxZROB/vXS\nzNVVjESoccTokt0IqTu+KW5cei5jvrLwDEpVcCdvquzUtOojrwMy7FpheZOBjePg\nYe/sg3rpKfcxSR2Pwr0InTUCAHA5hHIoOPcbodqZakrhnfRen3ZeaeVDqLg2uRFp\nbLKKdoEfu8LdjrWIUCZHTLmLnC/NoQ38u0Q5Or0ZMhGepFSFo5nOMfCcn4cOEVpO\nsqd1xYquaWLKC7zFXB9HI1ooU4MKnj4NiCr3MvlMHHxCgOkXeJCG4YEHMmWPA8t/\ngrK82HtyTgkanfkonHRd\n=9m86\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T10:56:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/46539d7d619011b71c1330eb308839434f0e0aa4","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDQ2NTM5ZDdkNjE5MDExYjcxYzEzMzBlYjMwODgzOTQzNGYwZTBhYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/420f1a48a86b8b78111c65af416f5288136256cb","sha":"420f1a48a86b8b78111c65af416f5288136256cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/420f1a48a86b8b78111c65af416f5288136256cb"}],"sha":"46539d7d619011b71c1330eb308839434f0e0aa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/46539d7d619011b71c1330eb308839434f0e0aa4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/420f1a48a86b8b78111c65af416f5288136256cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T01:00:36Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T01:00:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(e2e): run every Cypress spec a shard lists, port the valid ones to Playwright, fix the bugs they found (#4479)\n\n* fix(ci): run every spec each Cypress shard lists\n\nThe core and admin shards list their specs in YAML folded scalars, which\njoin the lines with \", \". Cypress splits --spec on commas without\ntrimming, so every entry after the first began with a space, matched no\nfile and was skipped without an error: core ran only login.cy.js and\nadmin only userManagement.cy.js, while the independent catch-all trims\nthe lists and excluded the same specs as assigned. Since #3096 those 22\nspecs ran nowhere in CI.\n\nThe step now strips whitespace from the list and fails the job when a\nlisted spec file does not exist, so a list that runs less than it names\ncannot pass again.\n\n* fix(program): release a case against its own analysis, not the sample id\n\nPathology, IHC and Cytology release looked up the analysis with the\nsample id, which failed with a 500 and would have written results onto\nanother order''s analysis once the ids overlapped. Resolve each result\nitem''s own analysis id instead.\n\n* fix(nav): leave new-window menu items to the browser\n\nThe side nav rendered every internal URL as a router Link, so items\nconfigured to open in a new window navigated the current tab.\n\n* fix(reports): route the HIV Test Summary to its own report\n\nIt opened the All Tests report.\n\n* fix(programs): show stage labels on the IHC and Cytology dashboards\n\nThe dashboards printed raw stage constants.\n\n* fix(workplan): give the top and bottom print buttons distinct ids\n\n* fix(nce): show the saved severity, category and type in View NCE\n\n* fix(batch-order): save once per order, save EID with its specimen and test\n\n- Pre-Printed saved an order on every keystroke of the lab number; it\n  now saves once, on Generate or Save.\n- EID posted no sample XML, so the order had no specimen; the server\n  builds it from the ticked specimens and DNA PCR.\n- Validation failures were recorded but the order was persisted anyway;\n  they now return 400 and persist nothing.\n- The EID and Viral Load checkboxes set the wrong test flag and mutated\n  shared state.\n- Notifications showed twice because embedded patient forms rendered\n  their own alert dialog.\n\n* test(e2e): port the valid Cypress specs to Playwright\n\nAdds 18 specs under foundational/core plus shared helpers. Each spec\nseeds its own data through the API and asserts only on its own records.\n\n* chore(cypress): remove the specs ported to Playwright and their dead support code\n\nDrops the 17 ported or retired specs, the page objects, fixtures, merge\nSQL hook and cypress.config.js tasks only they used. The shard lists in\ne2e-cypress-deprecated.yml now name the 16 specs that remain.\n\n* fix(batch-order): look up EID specimens in the CLINICAL domain\n\nThe catalog stores specimen domains as CLINICAL; the lookup used a\nlegacy code, so the sample XML came back empty and every EID save was\nrefused. The fixture now mirrors the real catalog.\n\n* fix(nce): default the date of event to the lab server''s today\n\nThe NCE forms took today, and the latest allowed date, from the browser\nclock, so a browser in another zone could pre-fill or accept the wrong\nday. They now use the server clock, keeping a date the user picked.\n\n* fix(dates): read today from the lab''s clock everywhere, not the browser''s\n\nCalendar values (today, this year, a range ending today, a latest\nallowed date) came from the browser clock, so a browser in another zone,\nor with a wrong clock, pre-filled, accepted or filtered by a day that is\nnot the lab''s. labClock reads the lab server''s zone and clock once at\nlogin; labNow() gives the lab''s wall clock and labTimeToInstant() turns a\nlab day bound back into an instant. This replaces the per-screen\nserver-time fetches on the order and NCE screens.\n\nA guard test fails on any new browser-clock calendar value; real\ninstants are pinned to their exact lines.\n\n* fix(cypress): restore page-object methods the remaining specs reach by name\n\nThe earlier prune kept only methods called literally, so it dropped ones\nthe menu and general configuration specs reach through computed names\n(adminPage[`goTo${name}Config`], selectors[key]) and those specs\nfailed. The surviving page objects are back to develop''s, minus only the\nmethods that build page objects whose specs were retired.\n\n* test(e2e): measure the program menu once the order page has settled\n\nThe picker was scrolled to the middle once, then measured; sections and\nfonts still laying out above it could push the open menu below the\nviewport, failing about one run in four. The measurement now scrolls the\nwindow back to the picker and polls, so only a container clipping the\nmenu fails it.\n\n* fix: address lab clock and calendar date review comments\n\n* ci: rebalance Playwright and Cypress E2E shards\n\n* fix: preserve lab calendar boundaries at midnight and unblinding\n\n* Align local CI runner with rebalanced E2E shards\n\n* Fix CI parity cleanup after frontend test execution","tree":{"sha":"511649beda797c271f634e59b3c2c68c1bcffcc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/511649beda797c271f634e59b3c2c68c1bcffcc8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/420f1a48a86b8b78111c65af416f5288136256cb","verification":{"payload":"tree 511649beda797c271f634e59b3c2c68c1bcffcc8\nparent 3711c6f91117765953eee24d4844509333c3a9d4\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1790989236 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790989236 -0700\n\nfix(e2e): run every Cypress spec a shard lists, port the valid ones to Playwright, fix the bugs they found (#4479)\n\n* fix(ci): run every spec each Cypress shard lists\n\nThe core and admin shards list their specs in YAML folded scalars, which\njoin the lines with \", \". Cypress splits --spec on commas without\ntrimming, so every entry after the first began with a space, matched no\nfile and was skipped without an error: core ran only login.cy.js and\nadmin only userManagement.cy.js, while the independent catch-all trims\nthe lists and excluded the same specs as assigned. Since #3096 those 22\nspecs ran nowhere in CI.\n\nThe step now strips whitespace from the list and fails the job when a\nlisted spec file does not exist, so a list that runs less than it names\ncannot pass again.\n\n* fix(program): release a case against its own analysis, not the sample id\n\nPathology, IHC and Cytology release looked up the analysis with the\nsample id, which failed with a 500 and would have written results onto\nanother order''s analysis once the ids overlapped. Resolve each result\nitem''s own analysis id instead.\n\n* fix(nav): leave new-window menu items to the browser\n\nThe side nav rendered every internal URL as a router Link, so items\nconfigured to open in a new window navigated the current tab.\n\n* fix(reports): route the HIV Test Summary to its own report\n\nIt opened the All Tests report.\n\n* fix(programs): show stage labels on the IHC and Cytology dashboards\n\nThe dashboards printed raw stage constants.\n\n* fix(workplan): give the top and bottom print buttons distinct ids\n\n* fix(nce): show the saved severity, category and type in View NCE\n\n* fix(batch-order): save once per order, save EID with its specimen and test\n\n- Pre-Printed saved an order on every keystroke of the lab number; it\n  now saves once, on Generate or Save.\n- EID posted no sample XML, so the order had no specimen; the server\n  builds it from the ticked specimens and DNA PCR.\n- Validation failures were recorded but the order was persisted anyway;\n  they now return 400 and persist nothing.\n- The EID and Viral Load checkboxes set the wrong test flag and mutated\n  shared state.\n- Notifications showed twice because embedded patient forms rendered\n  their own alert dialog.\n\n* test(e2e): port the valid Cypress specs to Playwright\n\nAdds 18 specs under foundational/core plus shared helpers. Each spec\nseeds its own data through the API and asserts only on its own records.\n\n* chore(cypress): remove the specs ported to Playwright and their dead support code\n\nDrops the 17 ported or retired specs, the page objects, fixtures, merge\nSQL hook and cypress.config.js tasks only they used. The shard lists in\ne2e-cypress-deprecated.yml now name the 16 specs that remain.\n\n* fix(batch-order): look up EID specimens in the CLINICAL domain\n\nThe catalog stores specimen domains as CLINICAL; the lookup used a\nlegacy code, so the sample XML came back empty and every EID save was\nrefused. The fixture now mirrors the real catalog.\n\n* fix(nce): default the date of event to the lab server''s today\n\nThe NCE forms took today, and the latest allowed date, from the browser\nclock, so a browser in another zone could pre-fill or accept the wrong\nday. They now use the server clock, keeping a date the user picked.\n\n* fix(dates): read today from the lab''s clock everywhere, not the browser''s\n\nCalendar values (today, this year, a range ending today, a latest\nallowed date) came from the browser clock, so a browser in another zone,\nor with a wrong clock, pre-filled, accepted or filtered by a day that is\nnot the lab''s. labClock reads the lab server''s zone and clock once at\nlogin; labNow() gives the lab''s wall clock and labTimeToInstant() turns a\nlab day bound back into an instant. This replaces the per-screen\nserver-time fetches on the order and NCE screens.\n\nA guard test fails on any new browser-clock calendar value; real\ninstants are pinned to their exact lines.\n\n* fix(cypress): restore page-object methods the remaining specs reach by name\n\nThe earlier prune kept only methods called literally, so it dropped ones\nthe menu and general configuration specs reach through computed names\n(adminPage[`goTo${name}Config`], selectors[key]) and those specs\nfailed. The surviving page objects are back to develop''s, minus only the\nmethods that build page objects whose specs were retired.\n\n* test(e2e): measure the program menu once the order page has settled\n\nThe picker was scrolled to the middle once, then measured; sections and\nfonts still laying out above it could push the open menu below the\nviewport, failing about one run in four. The measurement now scrolls the\nwindow back to the picker and polls, so only a container clipping the\nmenu fails it.\n\n* fix: address lab clock and calendar date review comments\n\n* ci: rebalance Playwright and Cypress E2E shards\n\n* fix: preserve lab calendar boundaries at midnight and unblinding\n\n* Align local CI runner with rebalanced E2E shards\n\n* Fix CI parity cleanup after frontend test execution","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwFO0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkDIQALBBIdMyzEQhogAMxNM5aPxi\nihTjaYEykbmf1kurC/BcAQLaU4k9t5nHLp3fvZx2EsXDFKpgZhY6CWL56Ck01MiH\nfMyjFItu3w78OuA5Zh03qWjGbsh9Ibd99pdjR6BHCgn/C3k8/pXGegn7/+Pu6HHv\nAWKln/MApFRhUUHT/49bycd0lh7doMvQqQk39eZb0WEgxDhWtu78rbnS3Q3wGTfx\nVXpV9oeC2AvZirBZe0Uwv2lTd4JILw3jGJNBrsj8r1mg1O1Z2LQwujOIS1hP7gNj\nRxO4YrIi9w2mZM/5Vj8ez9IOQQRLbq2/GjVIu7TMSfG4xBMo52ZBlYL6T84YMAHm\n5CzJWCS9qfG8Y1Eb0RZccAHXH1oYqOu25l7XvgrdumvKT4+nv/qU2cIG6y+CznXo\nxyUdymkT3DtN9bRU8E3LoJnvTcmPtGumZzwCQ5wrFyEYnHq9YarybiK3p86fOYKU\nIzq7RvwI2mnEnzXjhVjk8MDx/v1XN6774YvSnBJjY0lqawpj96yXNMp+PVi4yE07\nb0Y2t+2jjJK+BW4LF9Pkp6SxaWsFQJ5frqiivfgZFk4hq2B/S1iKiX+8hoZiE8uG\n1Fy7zBb/83ZkJGAgwLl9lXz5Gbep8j1E+WGRZrdEjVRTFvewy/vT+Zlb9P6ZPfAQ\nBaxQBwNKqMz3qd/EwrWz\n=tIrR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T01:00:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/420f1a48a86b8b78111c65af416f5288136256cb","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDQyMGYxYTQ4YTg2YjhiNzgxMTFjNjVhZjQxNmY1Mjg4MTM2MjU2Y2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/3711c6f91117765953eee24d4844509333c3a9d4","sha":"3711c6f91117765953eee24d4844509333c3a9d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/3711c6f91117765953eee24d4844509333c3a9d4"}],"sha":"420f1a48a86b8b78111c65af416f5288136256cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/420f1a48a86b8b78111c65af416f5288136256cb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/3711c6f91117765953eee24d4844509333c3a9d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T00:59:24Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T00:59:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(analyzers): export pre-Bridge analyzer settings and remove their storage (#4511)\n\n* fix(analyzers): report nothing to upgrade when the retained analyzer schema is gone\n\nDatabases that ran develop between 8 and 24 September 2026 applied the\nsince-removed changeset 098-remove-superseded-analyzer-schema, which dropped\nthe analyzer_type, analyzer_test_map and analyzer_plugin_config tables and\neight analyzer columns while 011-002-02 stayed EXECUTED. The AnalyzerUpgrade*\nentities still map that storage, so AnalyzerUpgradeDAO.pendingIds() failed\nwith \"column analyzerup0_.analyzer_type_id does not exist\" at every start\n(AnalyzerUpgradeStartup) and on every Admin > Analyzers load and retry\n(/rest/analyzer/upgrade).\n\nThe DAO now checks information_schema for the retained columns and tables\nbefore the entity query, reports no pending analyzers when they are gone,\nand logs that once at INFO. Fresh installs and released databases are\nunaffected; no release shipped the drop.\n\nThe integration fixture also stubbed fhirContext.newJsonParser() on a real\nFhirContext bean; Mockito''s when() consumed whichever mock call came last,\nso a failing earlier test broke the next one''s setup. The stub is removed.\n\nOGC-1416\n\n* fix(analyzers): re-create the analyzer upgrade storage where removed changesets dropped it\n\nDatabases that ran develop between 8 and 24 September 2026 applied the\nsince-removed changesets OGC-1054-remove-openelis-analyzer-connection-runtime\n(094) and 098-remove-superseded-analyzer-schema. Between them they dropped\nanalyzer.analyzer_type_id, the analyzer connection and file columns, and the\nanalyzer_type, analyzer_test_map, analyzer_plugin_config and\nserial_port_configuration tables. The read-only AnalyzerUpgrade* entities map\nthat storage, so the upgrade check failed with \"column\nanalyzerup0_.analyzer_type_id does not exist\" at every start and on every\nAdmin > Analyzers load and retry.\n\nChangeset file 113-restore-retained-analyzer-storage re-creates that storage,\nempty and with the definitions a database built from the full changelog has.\nEach of its six changesets is MARK_RAN where its object exists, so fresh and\nreleased databases are unchanged. On an affected database the upgrade check\nthen finds nothing to transfer. The other objects those changesets dropped\nare read by no code and are not re-created.\n\nThis replaces the information_schema probe in AnalyzerUpgradeDAO from the\nprevious commit, which was native SQL in a DAO.\n\nThe analyzer-window-schema upgrade scenario applies those drops to a full\nschema, runs the changelog, and compares the result with the fresh\ndefinitions.\n\nOGC-1416\n\n* test(analyzers): check retained analyzer storage against the fresh schema too\n\nThe expected column, constraint and index definitions moved into\nanalyzer-retained-storage-assertions.xml, which both the analyzer-unmigrated\nscenario (storage created by the full changelog) and the\nanalyzer-window-schema scenario (storage re-created by changeset 113)\ninclude. Both now check the same values, so the restored storage is shown\nequal to the fresh one rather than to definitions copied from a database.\n\nOGC-1416\n\n* docs(liquibase): say why the analyzer storage restore has empty rollbacks\n\nLiquibase 4.8 runs a changeset''s rollback for MARK_RAN rows as well\n(RollbackVisitor.visit calls ChangeSet.rollback without checking the exec\ntype), so a dropping rollback, or an omitted one that generates the inverse,\nwould delete the populated retained storage on every database where these\nobjects already existed.\n\nOGC-1416\n\n* chore: restore develop''s ExpandedPanel.tsx\n\nThe merge commit''s pre-commit hook reformatted this develop file with an\nnpx-fetched Prettier, because this worktree has no frontend/node_modules.\nDevelop''s version already passes the pinned Prettier 3.8.3.\n\n* fix(analyzers): number the analyzer storage restore 114\n\n#4512 added 113-result-entry-acknowledgement.xml to 3.5.x.x. The restore\nfile and its changeset ids move to 114; they have run only on disposable\ntest databases, so no applied changeset changes.\n\nOGC-1416\n\n* fix(analyzers): end the analyzer upgrade where its retained storage no longer exists\n\nThe analyzer upgrade job (AnalyzerUpgradeService, from #4433) reads the\nretained pre-Bridge analyzer settings through the AnalyzerUpgrade* entities\nand assumed that storage exists. Databases that ran develop between 8 and 24\nSeptember 2026 applied two since-removed cleanup changesets (094 and 098)\nthat dropped it, so the job failed with \"column analyzerup0_.analyzer_type_id\ndoes not exist\" at every start and on every Admin > Analyzers load and retry.\n\nThe job now has a terminal state. Changeset 114-analyzer-upgrade-not-applicable\nrecords a NOT_APPLICABLE run in the upgrade''s own history\n(configuration_import_run) where any of the tables or columns the entities\nmap is missing, and is MARK_RAN everywhere else. migrate() and pending()\nreturn nothing when that run exists, before reading the retained storage.\nReleased and fresh databases keep their storage and behave as before.\n\nThis replaces the previous commits'' approach of re-creating the dropped\ntables empty: the storage is scheduled for removal, so restoring it pointed\nthe wrong way.\n\nOGC-1416\n\n* fix(analyzers): export pre-Bridge analyzer settings and remove their storage\n\nBefore the Analyzer Bridge, OpenELIS kept each analyzer''s own connection,\nfile-import and plugin settings, analyzer types, test mappings and serial\nports in the analyzer table and a dozen side tables. #4433 added a transfer\njob that read that storage at every start to move it into Bridge connections;\non databases where two since-removed cleanup changesets had already dropped\nthe storage (develop, 8 to 24 September 2026) it failed with \"column\nanalyzerup0_.analyzer_type_id does not exist\" at every start and on every\nAdmin > Analyzers load and retry.\n\nThe storage was scheduled for removal, so this removes it, and the job with\nit. Changeset 114-remove-pre-bridge-analyzer-storage writes every analyzer\nthat still holds such settings and has no Bridge connection as one JSON\ndocument into a configuration_import_run row (source ANALYZER_LEGACY,\nstatus EXPORTED), then drops the tables and columns in the same transaction,\nso nothing configured is lost. Databases that already lost the storage have\nnothing to do. The export is read with one query; the doc explains how to set\nthe instrument up again through the Bridge-backed pages.\n\nRemoved: the AnalyzerUpgrade* entities, DAO, services, startup scheduler and\nREST controller; their persistence registrations; the Admin > Analyzers\ntransfer banner, its service calls and i18n keys; the integration test and\ntwo fixtures that only populated the dropped tables; and two harness scripts\nthat asserted analyzer_type links.\n\nReplaces this branch''s earlier approaches (an information_schema probe in the\nDAO, re-creating the tables empty, a recorded NOT_APPLICABLE run).\n\nOGC-1416\n\n* fix(analyzers): export and drop whatever pre-Bridge storage exists\n\nThe removal changeset no longer works from a fixed picture of the schema.\nIt reads which legacy analyzer columns and tables the database still has,\nkeeps every non-default value (not only active serial rows or analyzers\nwithout a Bridge connection), dumps every row of every removed table\nincluding analyzer_file_upload and file_import_configuration, and runs\nwithout a precondition: where nothing is left it writes nothing and the\ndrops are no-ops.\n\nThe window fixture now replays all six cleanup changesets the 8 to 24\nSeptember builds ran, not just two of them.","tree":{"sha":"b9f2c5a18d2aa140a201d2632880016a21a976ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/b9f2c5a18d2aa140a201d2632880016a21a976ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/3711c6f91117765953eee24d4844509333c3a9d4","verification":{"payload":"tree b9f2c5a18d2aa140a201d2632880016a21a976ae\nparent 181c28c99abf7083782a0bb3a060182a9a8344a6\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1790989164 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790989164 -0700\n\nfix(analyzers): export pre-Bridge analyzer settings and remove their storage (#4511)\n\n* fix(analyzers): report nothing to upgrade when the retained analyzer schema is gone\n\nDatabases that ran develop between 8 and 24 September 2026 applied the\nsince-removed changeset 098-remove-superseded-analyzer-schema, which dropped\nthe analyzer_type, analyzer_test_map and analyzer_plugin_config tables and\neight analyzer columns while 011-002-02 stayed EXECUTED. The AnalyzerUpgrade*\nentities still map that storage, so AnalyzerUpgradeDAO.pendingIds() failed\nwith \"column analyzerup0_.analyzer_type_id does not exist\" at every start\n(AnalyzerUpgradeStartup) and on every Admin > Analyzers load and retry\n(/rest/analyzer/upgrade).\n\nThe DAO now checks information_schema for the retained columns and tables\nbefore the entity query, reports no pending analyzers when they are gone,\nand logs that once at INFO. Fresh installs and released databases are\nunaffected; no release shipped the drop.\n\nThe integration fixture also stubbed fhirContext.newJsonParser() on a real\nFhirContext bean; Mockito''s when() consumed whichever mock call came last,\nso a failing earlier test broke the next one''s setup. The stub is removed.\n\nOGC-1416\n\n* fix(analyzers): re-create the analyzer upgrade storage where removed changesets dropped it\n\nDatabases that ran develop between 8 and 24 September 2026 applied the\nsince-removed changesets OGC-1054-remove-openelis-analyzer-connection-runtime\n(094) and 098-remove-superseded-analyzer-schema. Between them they dropped\nanalyzer.analyzer_type_id, the analyzer connection and file columns, and the\nanalyzer_type, analyzer_test_map, analyzer_plugin_config and\nserial_port_configuration tables. The read-only AnalyzerUpgrade* entities map\nthat storage, so the upgrade check failed with \"column\nanalyzerup0_.analyzer_type_id does not exist\" at every start and on every\nAdmin > Analyzers load and retry.\n\nChangeset file 113-restore-retained-analyzer-storage re-creates that storage,\nempty and with the definitions a database built from the full changelog has.\nEach of its six changesets is MARK_RAN where its object exists, so fresh and\nreleased databases are unchanged. On an affected database the upgrade check\nthen finds nothing to transfer. The other objects those changesets dropped\nare read by no code and are not re-created.\n\nThis replaces the information_schema probe in AnalyzerUpgradeDAO from the\nprevious commit, which was native SQL in a DAO.\n\nThe analyzer-window-schema upgrade scenario applies those drops to a full\nschema, runs the changelog, and compares the result with the fresh\ndefinitions.\n\nOGC-1416\n\n* test(analyzers): check retained analyzer storage against the fresh schema too\n\nThe expected column, constraint and index definitions moved into\nanalyzer-retained-storage-assertions.xml, which both the analyzer-unmigrated\nscenario (storage created by the full changelog) and the\nanalyzer-window-schema scenario (storage re-created by changeset 113)\ninclude. Both now check the same values, so the restored storage is shown\nequal to the fresh one rather than to definitions copied from a database.\n\nOGC-1416\n\n* docs(liquibase): say why the analyzer storage restore has empty rollbacks\n\nLiquibase 4.8 runs a changeset''s rollback for MARK_RAN rows as well\n(RollbackVisitor.visit calls ChangeSet.rollback without checking the exec\ntype), so a dropping rollback, or an omitted one that generates the inverse,\nwould delete the populated retained storage on every database where these\nobjects already existed.\n\nOGC-1416\n\n* chore: restore develop''s ExpandedPanel.tsx\n\nThe merge commit''s pre-commit hook reformatted this develop file with an\nnpx-fetched Prettier, because this worktree has no frontend/node_modules.\nDevelop''s version already passes the pinned Prettier 3.8.3.\n\n* fix(analyzers): number the analyzer storage restore 114\n\n#4512 added 113-result-entry-acknowledgement.xml to 3.5.x.x. The restore\nfile and its changeset ids move to 114; they have run only on disposable\ntest databases, so no applied changeset changes.\n\nOGC-1416\n\n* fix(analyzers): end the analyzer upgrade where its retained storage no longer exists\n\nThe analyzer upgrade job (AnalyzerUpgradeService, from #4433) reads the\nretained pre-Bridge analyzer settings through the AnalyzerUpgrade* entities\nand assumed that storage exists. Databases that ran develop between 8 and 24\nSeptember 2026 applied two since-removed cleanup changesets (094 and 098)\nthat dropped it, so the job failed with \"column analyzerup0_.analyzer_type_id\ndoes not exist\" at every start and on every Admin > Analyzers load and retry.\n\nThe job now has a terminal state. Changeset 114-analyzer-upgrade-not-applicable\nrecords a NOT_APPLICABLE run in the upgrade''s own history\n(configuration_import_run) where any of the tables or columns the entities\nmap is missing, and is MARK_RAN everywhere else. migrate() and pending()\nreturn nothing when that run exists, before reading the retained storage.\nReleased and fresh databases keep their storage and behave as before.\n\nThis replaces the previous commits'' approach of re-creating the dropped\ntables empty: the storage is scheduled for removal, so restoring it pointed\nthe wrong way.\n\nOGC-1416\n\n* fix(analyzers): export pre-Bridge analyzer settings and remove their storage\n\nBefore the Analyzer Bridge, OpenELIS kept each analyzer''s own connection,\nfile-import and plugin settings, analyzer types, test mappings and serial\nports in the analyzer table and a dozen side tables. #4433 added a transfer\njob that read that storage at every start to move it into Bridge connections;\non databases where two since-removed cleanup changesets had already dropped\nthe storage (develop, 8 to 24 September 2026) it failed with \"column\nanalyzerup0_.analyzer_type_id does not exist\" at every start and on every\nAdmin > Analyzers load and retry.\n\nThe storage was scheduled for removal, so this removes it, and the job with\nit. Changeset 114-remove-pre-bridge-analyzer-storage writes every analyzer\nthat still holds such settings and has no Bridge connection as one JSON\ndocument into a configuration_import_run row (source ANALYZER_LEGACY,\nstatus EXPORTED), then drops the tables and columns in the same transaction,\nso nothing configured is lost. Databases that already lost the storage have\nnothing to do. The export is read with one query; the doc explains how to set\nthe instrument up again through the Bridge-backed pages.\n\nRemoved: the AnalyzerUpgrade* entities, DAO, services, startup scheduler and\nREST controller; their persistence registrations; the Admin > Analyzers\ntransfer banner, its service calls and i18n keys; the integration test and\ntwo fixtures that only populated the dropped tables; and two harness scripts\nthat asserted analyzer_type links.\n\nReplaces this branch''s earlier approaches (an information_schema probe in the\nDAO, re-creating the tables empty, a recorded NOT_APPLICABLE run).\n\nOGC-1416\n\n* fix(analyzers): export and drop whatever pre-Bridge storage exists\n\nThe removal changeset no longer works from a fixed picture of the schema.\nIt reads which legacy analyzer columns and tables the database still has,\nkeeps every non-default value (not only active serial rows or analyzers\nwithout a Bridge connection), dumps every row of every removed table\nincluding analyzer_file_upload and file_import_configuration, and runs\nwithout a precondition: where nothing is left it writes nothing and the\ndrops are no-ops.\n\nThe window fixture now replays all six cleanup changesets the 8 to 24\nSeptember builds ran, not just two of them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwFNsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlXkQAGcKNbAb6L74aXgDs4VWVg5F\njA/DPMrG14iNux8y3/Hl7RMRhVnS9X1xycL3tkD67xR12/IITi3p/4FlddyQzhTU\nHn2KLZMTKASIOYGWRsEflrtgwf58uebRFtJ3v5ElVCr/jHxELgi7yqbZhxLwpLrM\nYatSzWudPmrHwf3vHO6qhX1gKO6T5V5mwcEv46/+3X9p7orUTuFB8iftg2BGMEBm\nr2ueGJvo+T1B2h+fZdXXsrw+YcoRVMtEJMcgNQ3xMwr9U10eJFSz7R+6UQ1ABEGt\nq7wx4ddt655EQJuyiyY+pfSeQM2B69nbLOEa0grEQDvy/ZwOj1PTIGs/2AZaY0PA\n6W9TGjoheWpfJpGmmoJffUUmYRxo37cXcEJe4IxBr4HSzOOrffcA4ir26gaD1me7\nnaKCwo7wsVlCCvPI4yzeCInzVS4gNF9+Bnjz8od9CRZVJ2u9AdS/tMhNeAPSJI3F\np6BVi7hXxC0aqJbZHXWhy0YQZs97lu8LpVEl7lj6L2jFYEE9N6kqH9HgQnQIvlVp\nV7394+tElxPsJAhEbBK5NXrmhIoJAHmjGGr39qX5QfxPN8pKM4A+jXvqOn247qdI\ndQikdfGxW1Tjl73rMIVUe5EXA6Kvf6hjQH63N21ZzJcWXSrCzAMDPnNtDFZ59Qyc\nVJsUpE2vDrQmiK56GyJ4\n=Ia0N\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T00:59:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/re