r":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/181c28c99abf7083782a0bb3a060182a9a8344a6","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDE4MWMyOGM5OWFiZjcwODM3ODJhMGJiM2EwNjAxODJhOWE4MzQ0YTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/022ca225394867d83ed5620556d0b5ca0a495c00","sha":"022ca225394867d83ed5620556d0b5ca0a495c00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/022ca225394867d83ed5620556d0b5ca0a495c00"}],"sha":"181c28c99abf7083782a0bb3a060182a9a8344a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/181c28c99abf7083782a0bb3a060182a9a8344a6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29783151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/022ca225394867d83ed5620556d0b5ca0a495c00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T21:54:00Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T21:54:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(locations): OGC-1420 import, Replace, area entry, save feedback and upgrade defects (#4515)\n\n* fix(locations): OGC-1420 import, Replace, field lengths, upgrade codes and FHIR identifiers\n\nCSV import (1, 2, 9b):\n- Excel files import as typed: a UTF-8 byte order mark is dropped and a\n  file that is not UTF-8 is read as Windows-1252 (shared CSV reader, used\n  by the catalog loaders and the area files).\n- A possible rename needs the same distinctive words or a near-identical\n  spelling; sharing \"Health Centre\" no longer pairs two centres, and the\n  best candidate wins.\n- An identifier repeated inside a file rejects the later row; columns the\n  importer does not know are listed on the plan as ignored.\n- Replace is scoped to the fewest types that cover the file''s rows, so a\n  referral-lab export no longer takes every referring clinic in scope; its\n  preview counts open orders as the list does, sampling sites included.\n- Recent imports name each run''s files and say whether it was applied.\n\nSaving (6, 7b, 8):\n- A value longer than its column is refused with a message naming the\n  field instead of being cut or answering 500; identifiers up to 100.\n- State / Province holds a name (Liquibase 115, varchar(100)).\n- The default list is one name order, coded or not.\n- An identifier the record already carries is not re-checked for clashes,\n  so records that shared a code before the upgrade can still be edited;\n  GET /rest/locations/identifier-collisions lists those shared codes.\n\nFHIR (9a): the Organization carries every identifier with its label as\ntype.text, the reporting code as official, and always its UUID.\n\n* fix(locations): OGC-1420 keep renames and same-record rows, plain failure text\n\n- A name whose distinctive words are all in the other''s (\"Tokarara\n  Clinic\" to \"Tokarara Urban Clinic\") is still offered as a rename.\n- The repeated-identifier check runs after matching: two rows that name\n  the same existing record by its identifier both match it; only rows\n  that would land on different records are rejected.\n- Recent imports say \"preview\" or \"apply\" for each run.\n- An unexpected failure is logged and answered without the exception''s\n  text, so a parser or database message never reaches the page.\n\n* fix(locations): OGC-1420 areas, messages, form saves, list links and import page\n\n- Areas (3): the add row is rendered by a call, not declared as a\n  component inside AreasView, so it no longer remounts on every key; a\n  new child reloads its grandparent''s list so the parent shows its\n  expander.\n- Messages (4): pinned in view and stacked, newest first; success closes\n  by itself, errors and warnings stay until dismissed; a request with no\n  usable answer shows a translated message instead of parser or browser\n  text.\n- Form (5): a blocked save names the fields and focuses the first; the\n  untouched pre-filled Code row is not sent; Close, Add and a search ask\n  before discarding changes; a 409 keeps what the user typed and fills in\n  the other admin''s changes; typed wards hold the save, and new wards are\n  saved one at a time so a retry never repeats one that saved.\n- Fields (6): maxLength on every free-text field, server field errors\n  shown on their inputs; State / Province takes 100 characters.\n- List (7): a record named in the address opens even off the current\n  page; a ward-name search opens its organization; chosen types are\n  listed as tags under the type picker.\n- Upgrade codes (8): identifiers two records share are listed above the\n  list, each record a link.\n- Import (1d, 9): file errors and ignored columns are shown; Recent\n  imports name the files and say preview or apply; the page fits 1280 px;\n  match counts use plurals.\n\n* test(fhir): OGC-1420 a province name fits Organization.address.state\n\nState / Province now holds 100 characters, so the over-long case uses a\n101-character value and the message names the new limit.\n\n* fix(locations): OGC-1420 apply any file name, ward refusal reasons, per-form messages\n\n- Apply stores each upload under a name its loader picks up\n  (organizations-*.csv, *-levels.csv), so a freely named Excel file is\n  written; a file the reload did not process is reported, and the last\n  plan is cleared first so a preview''s plan is never reported as done.\n- A refused ward says why (the first field error), on add and on edit;\n  saved wards are reported.\n- Each message names the form it is about; a later success from that\n  form clears its earlier errors and warnings.\n- A rename by the subset rule also needs the same generic words, so a\n  shared place name alone (\"Kila Aid Post\", \"Walk-in Clinic Kila\") is not\n  offered; name words are cached per catalogue name and Levenshtein is\n  skipped when the lengths rule out a match.\n- Shared identifiers are fetched once per view and after a save.","tree":{"sha":"ef2199a90527e3b17c9995bd4be6b406cf15106b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/ef2199a90527e3b17c9995bd4be6b406cf15106b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/022ca225394867d83ed5620556d0b5ca0a495c00","verification":{"payload":"tree ef2199a90527e3b17c9995bd4be6b406cf15106b\nparent af759dc3f1def475d6e65163e6d433c7451f9ab0\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1790978040 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790978040 +0300\n\nfix(locations): OGC-1420 import, Replace, area entry, save feedback and upgrade defects (#4515)\n\n* fix(locations): OGC-1420 import, Replace, field lengths, upgrade codes and FHIR identifiers\n\nCSV import (1, 2, 9b):\n- Excel files import as typed: a UTF-8 byte order mark is dropped and a\n  file that is not UTF-8 is read as Windows-1252 (shared CSV reader, used\n  by the catalog loaders and the area files).\n- A possible rename needs the same distinctive words or a near-identical\n  spelling; sharing \"Health Centre\" no longer pairs two centres, and the\n  best candidate wins.\n- An identifier repeated inside a file rejects the later row; columns the\n  importer does not know are listed on the plan as ignored.\n- Replace is scoped to the fewest types that cover the file''s rows, so a\n  referral-lab export no longer takes every referring clinic in scope; its\n  preview counts open orders as the list does, sampling sites included.\n- Recent imports name each run''s files and say whether it was applied.\n\nSaving (6, 7b, 8):\n- A value longer than its column is refused with a message naming the\n  field instead of being cut or answering 500; identifiers up to 100.\n- State / Province holds a name (Liquibase 115, varchar(100)).\n- The default list is one name order, coded or not.\n- An identifier the record already carries is not re-checked for clashes,\n  so records that shared a code before the upgrade can still be edited;\n  GET /rest/locations/identifier-collisions lists those shared codes.\n\nFHIR (9a): the Organization carries every identifier with its label as\ntype.text, the reporting code as official, and always its UUID.\n\n* fix(locations): OGC-1420 keep renames and same-record rows, plain failure text\n\n- A name whose distinctive words are all in the other''s (\"Tokarara\n  Clinic\" to \"Tokarara Urban Clinic\") is still offered as a rename.\n- The repeated-identifier check runs after matching: two rows that name\n  the same existing record by its identifier both match it; only rows\n  that would land on different records are rejected.\n- Recent imports say \"preview\" or \"apply\" for each run.\n- An unexpected failure is logged and answered without the exception''s\n  text, so a parser or database message never reaches the page.\n\n* fix(locations): OGC-1420 areas, messages, form saves, list links and import page\n\n- Areas (3): the add row is rendered by a call, not declared as a\n  component inside AreasView, so it no longer remounts on every key; a\n  new child reloads its grandparent''s list so the parent shows its\n  expander.\n- Messages (4): pinned in view and stacked, newest first; success closes\n  by itself, errors and warnings stay until dismissed; a request with no\n  usable answer shows a translated message instead of parser or browser\n  text.\n- Form (5): a blocked save names the fields and focuses the first; the\n  untouched pre-filled Code row is not sent; Close, Add and a search ask\n  before discarding changes; a 409 keeps what the user typed and fills in\n  the other admin''s changes; typed wards hold the save, and new wards are\n  saved one at a time so a retry never repeats one that saved.\n- Fields (6): maxLength on every free-text field, server field errors\n  shown on their inputs; State / Province takes 100 characters.\n- List (7): a record named in the address opens even off the current\n  page; a ward-name search opens its organization; chosen types are\n  listed as tags under the type picker.\n- Upgrade codes (8): identifiers two records share are listed above the\n  list, each record a link.\n- Import (1d, 9): file errors and ignored columns are shown; Recent\n  imports name the files and say preview or apply; the page fits 1280 px;\n  match counts use plurals.\n\n* test(fhir): OGC-1420 a province name fits Organization.address.state\n\nState / Province now holds 100 characters, so the over-long case uses a\n101-character value and the message names the new limit.\n\n* fix(locations): OGC-1420 apply any file name, ward refusal reasons, per-form messages\n\n- Apply stores each upload under a name its loader picks up\n  (organizations-*.csv, *-levels.csv), so a freely named Excel file is\n  written; a file the reload did not process is reported, and the last\n  plan is cleared first so a preview''s plan is never reported as done.\n- A refused ward says why (the first field error), on add and on edit;\n  saved wards are reported.\n- Each message names the form it is about; a later success from that\n  form clears its earlier errors and warnings.\n- A rename by the subset rule also needs the same generic words, so a\n  shared place name alone (\"Kila Aid Post\", \"Walk-in Clinic Kila\") is not\n  offered; name words are cached per catalogue name and Levenshtein is\n  skipped when the lengths rule out a match.\n- Shared identifiers are fetched once per view and after a save.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwCf4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVpsQAHqFgBvbdC7hzLTO0kbuzgeJ\nyjjO0zghNNuyTy8e2uOlZ93t7lfHagYTlvfU+0ARCRPxYCBW4lwGGYtR1FMdnTU3\nUicHgjCetyhtjJOizpYrTj8f5D+F3x1YncyIGH6pjf82B/UD4EBnHrEJPAC7sFlD\nbrfp1hGcvKuhbH1sgKsz9HVwqxRz78tVgqBYkatgMS4KeK91Diy2ggpAn46RYl7P\n49FrPJeqmhfNAMY0yIRzxchRfxRYeWoOTuwDBARUdndv5EVvyGQgm2Ywlyg+EOZl\n0bZroVGq5p+MPHrRF07X8BfIrEAK/CfSU548+CxjDUjkC7CHhf3C1OEVzPENLltP\n8spfBIK+etcbYnpR7XTtqhOtEwu6phv/Ai9qz1xfZ8sl7makhEc/1LkSv4P9loud\nqJbkyU7MATHAbc28VswH6sV9WJmLlJ2OP77dcLbD3wv5MMrUDfLNvFkie4NMvYrJ\nXvLlfIBGhxMEMbqwpT6fflqwDY6Rzmiqf1fctf9aSaq4UO4fFIkvYVoIX2xYl5uG\nRUJvBOuW16SJpqp5oUNi7sFaomRWmKpLBZ1I1B6DCWKMyjndr71tcFkbM2PYegor\npDGkzi0vz0xO0+Kqx7GNUqGksLY7fU2tIKBWavdCmKbyKQWpGdZhucBnNIJ8HZSF\n1Iir0nxJbU+GtgqvjgnR\n=Q6qK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T21:54:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/022ca225394867d83ed5620556d0b5ca0a495c00","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDAyMmNhMjI1Mzk0ODY3ZDgzZWQ1NjIwNTU2ZDBiNWNhMGE0OTVjMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/af759dc3f1def475d6e65163e6d433c7451f9ab0","sha":"af759dc3f1def475d6e65163e6d433c7451f9ab0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/af759dc3f1def475d6e65163e6d433c7451f9ab0"}],"sha":"022ca225394867d83ed5620556d0b5ca0a495c00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/022ca225394867d83ed5620556d0b5ca0a495c00"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29783151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/af759dc3f1def475d6e65163e6d433c7451f9ab0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T16:53:26Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T16:53:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(order): OGC-1419 collector is optional on Prepare Samples (#4514)\n\n* fix(order): OGC-1419 collector is optional on Prepare Samples\n\nMany labs never learn who collected a tube, so the collector no longer\nholds Save and next: a sample with a type and a collection date and time\ncontinues, and the \"Collector for\" checklist item and its string are\ngone. The complete-level checklist moves into prepareSamplesToContinue\nso it can be tested on its own; the other rules are unchanged.\n\nAlso: the patient form on Enter Order crashed the page when one of its\nlists (education, marital status, regions, districts) failed to load;\na failed list is now empty.\n\n* fix(order): OGC-1419 an emptied collector saves as empty\n\nThe sample XML fell back to the loaded collector whenever the field was\nempty, so a wrong name could not be removed. It now falls back only when\nthe field was never loaded. The fix-now spec clears the collection time\nto save Prepare Samples incomplete, since the defaults now complete it.","tree":{"sha":"d0170811c96e1e0cc3d8897e3f4c989879851cf8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/d0170811c96e1e0cc3d8897e3f4c989879851cf8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/af759dc3f1def475d6e65163e6d433c7451f9ab0","verification":{"payload":"tree d0170811c96e1e0cc3d8897e3f4c989879851cf8\nparent 85001620351eae1092c1f17921c4f780b019b18d\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1790960006 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790960006 +0300\n\nfix(order): OGC-1419 collector is optional on Prepare Samples (#4514)\n\n* fix(order): OGC-1419 collector is optional on Prepare Samples\n\nMany labs never learn who collected a tube, so the collector no longer\nholds Save and next: a sample with a type and a collection date and time\ncontinues, and the \"Collector for\" checklist item and its string are\ngone. The complete-level checklist moves into prepareSamplesToContinue\nso it can be tested on its own; the other rules are unchanged.\n\nAlso: the patient form on Enter Order crashed the page when one of its\nlists (education, marital status, regions, districts) failed to load;\na failed list is now empty.\n\n* fix(order): OGC-1419 an emptied collector saves as empty\n\nThe sample XML fell back to the loaded collector whenever the field was\nempty, so a wrong name could not be removed. It now falls back only when\nthe field was never loaded. The fix-now spec clears the collection time\nto save Prepare Samples incomplete, since the defaults now complete it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv+GGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXMEQABW99htAna9mXozuv+qPsLTc\nGxznNcWHPKoDxdW64xpzj5JGKR/9LB66nEU+xS7m4KFrfzL9BsjMRcsZiRBJyM7y\nDtJ/Q46lHfwwRQdILCb4VQQfCeWw889HQveNIrA3lx138LiCJ4KzVWJB68OIYmEY\nywxE9VLUO9DczIFxnCBCfPxHODf8k79IPCB/NB6QRckn1bJUuQRTjnM1issB8Str\nptoJmgjP7/D/QHMrcviR4tjPleLalma9ssK77HrBufTbuHscrm8Tyu+OJum4G4Up\n+I0A/hSZ0OTXCj6IEPSqC36kuFx1O1kJfLiiKDM0T5kN