2fd83c2232"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/864a63ad584106736ea356e87536e53d84094ffa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T13:13:38Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T13:13:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(analyzers): remove the legacy analyzer plugin API and its CI build (OGC-1412) (#4506)\n\n* chore(analyzers): remove the legacy analyzer plugin API and its CI build\n\nAnalyzer results arrive through the Bridge. Nothing in OpenELIS loads a\nplugin jar or calls PluginAnalyzerService, so the five classes of the\nold plugin API (PluginAnalyzerService, APlugin, AnalyzerImporterPlugin,\nAnalyzerLineInserter, AnalyzerResponder) only referenced each other.\n\nCI still built the Generic* plugins against them and uploaded the jars\nas e2e-plugin-jars, an artifact nothing downloads. That build and the\nplugins submodule go, along with the classes jar and test-jar packaging\nthat existed only to feed it and the 3.2.1.3 revision pin the root\nbuild was installed under for the same reason. The root E2E build now\nskips tests like every other sub-build.\n\nopenelisglobal-plugins compiles against its own pinned OpenELIS\n3.2.1.3 and is unaffected.\n\n* chore(analyzers): drop the plugins submodule from dev-stack and the plugin-only CI build\n\nscripts/dev-stack still listed \"plugins\" in required_submodules(), so\n`dev-stack up` on a clean checkout ran `git submodule update --init plugins`\nagainst a submodule this branch removes and exited. It also passed\n--skip-plugins to the analyzer harness bootstrap.sh, which parsed the flag\nand never read it; both are removed and the dev-stack tests use dataexport\nas their sample submodule.\n\nShared Build kept a host-side Maven build of dataexport and the root\nproject that only the plugin compilation consumed: .dockerignore excludes\nevery target/ directory and the Docker build compiles from source. That\nstep and its Java setup are removed. The local runner''s shared-build lane\nkeeps its host builds, because ci-parity-test.sh --build compiles the root\nproject against the dataexport artifacts that lane installs.\n\nThe CI architecture spec now describes Shared Build without plugins or\ne2e-plugin-jars, alongside the workflow change.\n\n* chore(analyzers): remove the last references to the plugin system\n\n- AppConfig scanned \"oe.plugin\", the package plugin jars loaded into; no\n  source or jar provides it now.\n- AppTestConfig listed \"org.openelisglobal.plugin\" a second time; that\n  package no longer exists.\n- The ListPluginsPageDefinition tile pointed at pages/plugin/listPlugin.jsp,\n  which does not exist and which no controller maps; its four plugin.*\n  message keys had no other use.\n- docs/dev.md listed a plugin resources folder that does not exist, and\n  careful-rebase.md used the plugins submodule as its example.\n\n* chore(analyzers): remove the compile-only shims the plugins needed\n\nThese existed only so the GenericASTM, GenericHL7 and GenericFile plugins\ncompiled against OpenELIS; none has a caller left:\n\n- AnalyzerType, AnalyzerTypeService, AnalyzerPluginConfig,\n  AnalyzerPluginConfigService, AnalyzerTestMapping, AnalyzerTestMappingPK\n  and AnalyzerTestMappingService. The three service interfaces had no\n  implementation, so no bean ever existed for them.\n- AnalyzerTestNameCache and MappedTestName. Nothing called the cache;\n  constructing it would have thrown, because it looked up the missing\n  AnalyzerTestMappingService bean.\n- Analyzer.getAnalyzerType(), which always returned null, and the\n  DeviceProvider branch that checked it.\n- AnalyzerService.findByIdentifierPatternMatch, two defaults that always\n  returned empty.","tree":{"sha":"6390c38c22331a979a78942f6ccfcd17bfdfc768","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/6390c38c22331a979a78942f6ccfcd17bfdfc768"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/864a63ad584106736ea356e87536e53d84094ffa","verification":{"payload":"tree 6390c38c22331a979a78942f6ccfcd17bfdfc768\nparent c0a925a5a3d497616b635b4f44b572932243fc5f\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1790946818 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790946818 -0700\n\nchore(analyzers): remove the legacy analyzer plugin API and its CI build (OGC-1412) (#4506)\n\n* chore(analyzers): remove the legacy analyzer plugin API and its CI build\n\nAnalyzer results arrive through the Bridge. Nothing in OpenELIS loads a\nplugin jar or calls PluginAnalyzerService, so the five classes of the\nold plugin API (PluginAnalyzerService, APlugin, AnalyzerImporterPlugin,\nAnalyzerLineInserter, AnalyzerResponder) only referenced each other.\n\nCI still built the Generic* plugins against them and uploaded the jars\nas e2e-plugin-jars, an artifact nothing downloads. That build and the\nplugins submodule go, along with the classes jar and test-jar packaging\nthat existed only to feed it and the 3.2.1.3 revision pin the root\nbuild was installed under for the same reason. The root E2E build now\nskips tests like every other sub-build.\n\nopenelisglobal-plugins compiles against its own pinned OpenELIS\n3.2.1.3 and is unaffected.\n\n* chore(analyzers): drop the plugins submodule from dev-stack and the plugin-only CI build\n\nscripts/dev-stack still listed \"plugins\" in required_submodules(), so\n`dev-stack up` on a clean checkout ran `git submodule update --init plugins`\nagainst a submodule this branch removes and exited. It also passed\n--skip-plugins to the analyzer harness bootstrap.sh, which parsed the flag\nand never read it; both are removed and the dev-stack tests use dataexport\nas their sample submodule.\n\nShared Build kept a host-side Maven build of dataexport and the root\nproject that only the plugin compilation consumed: .dockerignore excludes\nevery target/ directory and the Docker build compiles from source. That\nstep and its Java setup are removed. The local runner''s shared-build lane\nkeeps its host builds, because ci-parity-test.sh --build compiles the root\nproject against the dataexport artifacts that lane installs.\n\nThe CI architecture spec now describes Shared Build without plugins or\ne2e-plugin-jars, alongside the workflow change.\n\n* chore(analyzers): remove the last references to the plugin system\n\n- AppConfig scanned \"oe.plugin\", the package plugin jars loaded into; no\n  source or jar provides it now.\n- AppTestConfig listed \"org.openelisglobal.plugin\" a second time; that\n  package no longer exists.\n- The ListPluginsPageDefinition tile pointed at pages/plugin/listPlugin.jsp,\n  which does not exist and which no controller maps; its four plugin.*\n  message keys had no other use.\n- docs/dev.md listed a plugin resources folder that does not exist, and\n  careful-rebase.md used the plugins submodule as its example.\n\n* chore(analyzers): remove the compile-only shims the plugins needed\n\nThese existed only so the GenericASTM, GenericHL7 and GenericFile plugins\ncompiled against OpenELIS; none has a caller left:\n\n- AnalyzerType, AnalyzerTypeService, AnalyzerPluginConfig,\n  AnalyzerPluginConfigService, AnalyzerTestMapping, AnalyzerTestMappingPK\n  and AnalyzerTestMappingService. The three service interfaces had no\n  implementation, so no bean ever existed for them.\n- AnalyzerTestNameCache and MappedTestName. Nothing called the cache;\n  constructing it would have thrown, because it looked up the missing\n  AnalyzerTestMappingService bean.\n- Analyzer.getAnalyzerType(), which always returned null, and the\n  DeviceProvider branch that checked it.\n- AnalyzerService.findByIdentifierPatternMatch, two defaults that always\n  returned empty.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv64CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAUsQAAxj2zLaGEvufp9njh1aCiKH\n0BPBM284Lc/f/dtj8YQxBZ9V4TnoF9Ddg8xMbmBFeNWlvyYM1H+bt7dBhigH9rCs\nhPc4CHLBitD0oZ0eTnqn1w0SDTwukK1a3Kd7dNBbpsri0yhzttFz4HEtg1j4Sc9n\nKeEHcVfziQ+WyfUKf+MUqCPkpCZuAOu3ejc0XVOmtKlpk2j1kbW8dvEhPNZHNF7P\naZwrbmfJke8+sB1wTxAvKNUZ6LImZ+Z7H0N/gaZaRYI0+vsHmhmTiky+R6/JmSQu\nGXs6IsI8HCRIPiOGQdOJ0GkE3cSM8a1gZQVXhpeSGxpK31qTHt3CVVtfBHTzyJeA\nAxHhgYLj5uL5K1ZlxaE1EnvcqyL42+Yklj3JgKzi/ocHyZQEN91Rw0p7j7o0Gog+\npPPw3gmGT3cXzA63VguXZFzwN/m31xA6MVzg2xYCiW3dR0ngOPNa7SxTWzqnzy4Z\nj+3gBaZALZ04H1DGT8XUL17lEUQ7X343P+w4HaPxzbAbUU9ubQ19l0zUGzksV9GW\n1wy2rIpOQl2uGjl7/Jjy3OKAg22UPr5oyamPrt3P4IqhB+GccU8G6BdbG/V5hrAl\n5nLjB/w93c8kWrSY4PnvnjlJ0OCluK0GB9wm9Z7Q/gKJb1pdvuu+G2kfPTkc3eIr\ne533OjDuvpnrAWwtFaHf\n=BuhY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T13:13:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","htm