thub.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/c0a925a5a3d497616b635b4f44b572932243fc5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T11:28:51Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T11:28:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(results): OGC-1417 acknowledge critical values and confirm invalid ones before saving (#4512)\n\nA critical result is now acknowledged by the person entering it, before the save is signed, with the custom message from Result Configuration (or a translated default). A value outside the valid range is questioned on leaving the field when alertWhenInvalidResult is on, and keeping it is recorded. The server refuses an unacknowledged save on unified and legacy Results, Validation Modify, the batch validation save and analyzer review, so a REST call cannot skip it. Acknowledgements are stored with user, time, value and message, and appear in the result history. Admin changes apply without a restart, and the OGC-714 callback log is on the unified page. Tested with the full backend and frontend suites, Playwright specs, and a live walk with e-signatures on and off; the independent review was addressed.","tree":{"sha":"c31fa6f7b711b05f3de6a763fa8be9a974fd9cb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/c31fa6f7b711b05f3de6a763fa8be9a974fd9cb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/c0a925a5a3d497616b635b4f44b572932243fc5f","verification":{"payload":"tree c31fa6f7b711b05f3de6a763fa8be9a974fd9cb0\nparent a3b6d23b8da920e0817ff353f93f920d90f7a9af\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1790940531 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790940531 +0300\n\nfeat(results): OGC-1417 acknowledge critical values and confirm invalid ones before saving (#4512)\n\nA critical result is now acknowledged by the person entering it, before the save is signed, with the custom message from Result Configuration (or a translated default). A value outside the valid range is questioned on leaving the field when alertWhenInvalidResult is on, and keeping it is recorded. The server refuses an unacknowledged save on unified and legacy Results, Validation Modify, the batch validation save and analyzer review, so a REST call cannot skip it. Acknowledgements are stored with user, time, value and message, and appear in the result history. Admin changes apply without a restart, and the OGC-714 callback log is on the unified page. Tested with the full backend and frontend suites, Playwright specs, and a live walk with e-signatures on and off; the independent review was addressed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv5VzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjcYQAKMa0ONkbOe2Ei6fFH5ZlN+6\nDOKRGMOewy93zlvufo7XdvrQPbMKn2GxXgWUEctf+iPwlqNI+Ye1Dib18VQ15Uv7\n7ETaP2TSwKUaUX47jmg0DptXXYt3GYS5NVNjAQQwlUNHFq/Oh1lK932RU/6rLhSE\ngvr24IdXd30RnLYSTiTY2EwE3j+EESl/J2rgVjFsuQ2p+v8nwscVWjSxbglA8dzO\nJDFFUkAdKPVTrGpfbjDjXG7Ix+8JHCfK5/pmya/+LWEs5PdB/cguw14fyoN6qjc+\nTxVMWMPc4JiEUcJ4y+gZYofp2hTV5xYKqpQxk/RxnvlwUInpLO/3JI5u0VRO/XGk\nkyKXIOciSDWFXLDnyXIJBxACeWG38mcAL/GTerVPgOfLUmgB1WOJamfDbTzeuJN9\nVldsR+L69OU2hxju3Z9U6Mv+5bWlRnuCULFOc04eVrK2QrgSVhgNCcQ19mbtcxJo\nXP/XWqmrJXqFVasz+hZi1HqG69bjTyY51y27EzuSrZUquFwuo92j7skqBRqsuRxq\nu1euad7koMSJptKBuA7CUIyGYvAFz7ZBB/tr0p+y+w7iWP1Wxzi0qa4jiUfzMi6b\n6tEkQUPn8t/DCXH1ccYGcaUKb4B0S5qQ+DY0wn0R3VaPoicSRLXr8K8FQ75vihed\nqCusEX/x3EfRrpoJJVin\n=nQci\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T11:28:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github