"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/2125fc864b11d0e501b2dae407b8b12a7b95f17d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:35:50Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:35:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(analyzers): keep only analyzer docs that match the code (#4495)\n\n* docs(analyzers): remove specs, plans and docs that no longer match the code\n\nAnalyzer runtime moved to the Bridge in September (#4118, #4125, #4138) and\nthe remediation stack has landed, but the repository still carried the\nearlier designs: plugin-jar setup guides, the 011 research and templates,\npointer stubs for 004 and 012-014, the 015 migration contract, dated demo and\nbranch plans, and the retired plan archive. Anyone following them would set\nup analyzers a way the code no longer supports.\n\nRemove them outright; git history keeps the old versions. Also remove\ntools/analyzer-connection-migration: it calls /rest/analyzer/migration\nendpoints deleted in #4138, nothing builds it, and its test loads the 015\nschema. The upgrade now runs inside the WAR (AnalyzerUpgradeService, #4433).\n\nRepoint the links that pointed at removed files: the Playwright skill and\nAGENTS.md now name scripts/dev-stack instead of the broken\n/restart-analyzer-harness command (it called reset-env.sh, deleted in #4332),\nCONTRIBUTING.md states the keep-current rule instead of the archive, and the\nmkdocs nav, microbiology spec and React 18 plan drop dead references.\n\n* docs(analyzers): make the remaining analyzer docs match the code\n\nThe feature roadmap becomes the single analyzer roadmap. It keeps its\nworkflow, ownership and acceptance rules, drops the merge-train status that\nwent stale when the stack landed, and takes over the live parts of the\nremediation plan: current state and pins, the ordered remaining work, the\nF-REV deferred items and the open related PRs. The plan itself is removed.\n\nCorrections checked against the code:\n- OGC-1054 spec: adopting a corrected mapping re-maps held originals in\n  place (recoverHeldMappingResults), and the upgrade runs inside the WAR\n  after startup, matching an exact old type name; the MVP-0xx and AN-MVP IDs\n  it cited exist nowhere.\n- OGC-41 spec: QC export and manual bench QC entry exist; only the\n  dedicated manual QC page is still a placeholder.\n- default-catalog-evidence: the RIF test comes from the harness catalog,\n  Bridge #69 and profile revision 7 have shipped, and the harness keeps its\n  outbox on the data volume.\n- partial-mapping-setup: held rows link from the analyzer''s results\n  (\"Review Analyzer Type mapping\"), not Import issues; the UI calls the\n  exclude state \"Do not receive\".\n- Harness README and LANE-IDENTIFIERS: four seeded analyzers, mock 0.1.3\n  substitutes FluoroCycler sample IDs, and no HL7 push-based Test Connection.\n- AGENTS.md and README.md: real Playwright project and CI job names,\n  harness fixture profile, and no cy:analyzer (its Cypress folder is gone;\n  the npm script is removed with it).\n\n* docs(analyzers): say which harness workflows read results back\n\nOnly the result workflows do independent clinical readback; the default,\ndismissal and guided-setup checks are UI and API checks.\n\n* docs(analyzers): list the Bridge authentication PR and the 3.2.5 repin in the roadmap\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the Bridge 3.2.6 release and the #4497 repin in the roadmap\n\n* docs(analyzers): name the Bridge repository in the roadmap''s #73 reference","tree":{"sha":"a6f3ac574fa78f693a7c6cb260bf5e56da7d9be7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/a6f3ac574fa78f693a7c6cb260bf5e56da7d9be7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/2125fc864b11d0e501b2dae407b8b12a7b95f17d","verification":{"payload":"tree a6f3ac574fa78f693a7c6cb260bf5e56da7d9be7\nparent e8e8552a73ef2bb50cd72de1c7aa1b11479fcb54\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1790865350 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790865350 -0700\n\ndocs(analyzers): keep only analyzer docs that match the code (#4495)\n\n* docs(analyzers): remove specs, plans and docs that no longer match the code\n\nAnalyzer runtime moved to the Bridge in September (#4118, #4125, #4138) and\nthe remediation stack has landed, but the repository still carried the\nearlier designs: plugin-jar setup guides, the 011 research and templates,\npointer stubs for 004 and 012-014, the 015 migration contract, dated demo and\nbranch plans, and the retired plan archive. Anyone following them would set\nup analyzers a way the code no longer supports.\n\nRemove them outright; git history keeps the old versions. Also remove\ntools/analyzer-connection-migration: it calls /rest/analyzer/migration\nendpoints deleted in #4138, nothing builds it, and its test loads the 015\nschema. The upgrade now runs inside the WAR (AnalyzerUpgradeService, #4433).\n\nRepoint the links that pointed at removed files: the Playwright skill and\nAGENTS.md now name scripts/dev-stack instead of the broken\n/restart-analyzer-harness command (it called reset-env.sh, deleted in #4332),\nCONTRIBUTING.md states the keep-current rule instead of the archive, and the\nmkdocs nav, microbiology spec and React 18 plan drop dead references.\n\n* docs(analyzers): make the remaining analyzer docs match the code\n\nThe feature roadmap becomes the single analyzer roadmap. It keeps its\nworkflow, ownership and acceptance rules, drops the merge-train status that\nwent stale when the stack landed, and takes over the live parts of the\nremediation plan: current state and pins, the ordered remaining work, the\nF-REV deferred items and the open related PRs. The plan itself is removed.\n\nCorrections checked against the code:\n- OGC-1054 spec: adopting a corrected mapping re-maps held originals in\n  place (recoverHeldMappingResults), and the upgrade runs inside the WAR\n  after startup, matching an exact old type name; the MVP-0xx and AN-MVP IDs\n  it cited exist nowhere.\n- OGC-41 spec: QC export and manual bench QC entry exist; only the\n  dedicated manual QC page is still a placeholder.\n- default-catalog-evidence: the RIF test comes from the harness catalog,\n  Bridge #69 and profile revision 7 have shipped, and the harness keeps its\n  outbox on the data volume.\n- partial-mapping-setup: held rows link from the analyzer''s results\n  (\"Review Analyzer Type mapping\"), not Import issues; the UI calls the\n  exclude state \"Do not receive\".\n- Harness README and LANE-IDENTIFIERS: four seeded analyzers, mock 0.1.3\n  substitutes FluoroCycler sample IDs, and no HL7 push-based Test Connection.\n- AGENTS.md and README.md: real Playwright project and CI job names,\n  harness fixture profile, and no cy:analyzer (its Cypress folder is gone;\n  the npm script is removed with it).\n\n* docs(analyzers): say which harness workflows read results back\n\nOnly the result workflows do independent clinical readback; the default,\ndismissal and guided-setup checks are UI and API checks.\n\n* docs(analyzers): list the Bridge authentication PR and the 3.2.5 repin in the roadmap\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the Bridge 3.2.6 release and the #4497 repin in the roadmap\n\n* docs(analyzers): name the Bridge repository in the roadmap''s #73 reference","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvm/GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2cQQAA4NaSmYu/m45rDVlqJX4a4t\nlSel0xFG5OqiHbHcZM8gFs98r0tgq4zRPKEtryt8JzHU/7CYHs046xkKkRlfWWju\npNpEbkuXIE0530PoL/v4GYMjcsEE6GIlDZnUkTgpTQsAuRx6gaD//kfwCHn/acQM\n2Gq8yLcm0lSlid8H0FeTJjXm0Wl5Aa84ZIu7mCnlKVWgT8l4IOQSySRACEmcdzJZ\n5LQhDhwrmUrAaPpONhx762CiA0N/vB8ZjK5Aw/iHL8JUfOg+2BeUlK8kgOkPgfwA\n9Vbhn7hB+N+MR72xcs3qz5nhSSuzireCgQYDeNqEndQzGm7rXaXsvB23d/mgJMAG\nD2JoaIDElXAwN1JVFWLmcE7fY46aVGJdH6CLcFqS4xMvr2j/5SpwWOD7li6yofja\nGaWzv++FlvmOGoNvn9rrKNsSGzyZnLt7PmIpGTDMspAWYe7JWTDrBT6xY3E09xaU\nwEnXIzDlmE8+6rpoDfPWduJWvC/aWtQnZ3wcyzAY8rNvc/2qqqhvwdAUQo59kDQr\nFSUllQXxvNryr1Y1e9KnjysMvGjgtDN11H5sblq8c9gZIPG+P4APC1zFARNITQ9L\nl/PPSKgMD+JwUQ00ftXQ/QrqhOMA9+h92qjroTRpxo2gJ4fUB2OPXfnnAnQ09wVX\nciQowYOfzwwBngEz+uH+\n=cp5x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T14:35:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","s