mozzy11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/8e3a7068451232ec3c6d20d6e03634b137615936/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T03:50:56Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T03:50:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(order): OGC-1266 clinical order entry v4: three steps, whole-step saves, order progress and cancel (#4490)\n\n* feat(order): OGC-1266 record order progress, gate release and cancel orders\n\nThe order carries an explicit progress status (Entered, Samples prepared,\nReady for testing, Cancelled) with the time each step completed, instead of\ninferring completion from a QA checklist row. The step''s save advances it:\nthe entry save records Entered, a Prepare Samples save made with the step\ncomplete records Samples prepared, and the Sample check''s release records\nReady for testing after a server-side gate (Mandatory acceptance unanswered\nis refused, Optional unanswered needs a reason, which is stored).\n\nPOST /rest/order/cancel records a reason from a new dictionary category,\ncancels the open tests and marks the sample cancelled; cancelled orders\nleave the open lists and show under the Cancelled filter.\n\nStorage travels with the order save: the sample XML carries condition\nnotes and the order carries the skip-storage decision, and the assignment\nlistener assigns, moves or updates notes from what the save says. An item\nnever stored reads back with a quantity snapshot but no location id, so\nthe id decides whether the item is already assigned.\n\nThe FHIR ServiceRequest create hands the save a detached shell of an\nexisting sample, so the progress is read from and written to the stored\nrow and the shell is brought up to date. The numeric who-cancelled column\nmaps through the project''s number user type like sys_user_id does.\n\nThe clinical side menu names Prepare Samples and Sample check and drops\nLabel & Store, which Prepare Samples absorbs.\n\n* feat(order): OGC-1266 clinical steps, footer, checklist and dashboard status\n\nClinical order entry is three steps: Enter Order, Prepare Samples (the\nCollect step, absorbing Label & Store) and Sample check, which exists\nonly while the clinical sample acceptance setting is not Off. The retired\n/order/clinical/label address opens Prepare Samples; an unknown step opens\nthe dashboard.\n\nEvery clinical step ends in the same footer: Discard (confirms, names what\nis lost, discards a never-saved order), Save and exit (back to the\ndashboard with the order highlighted) and Save and next or Save and finish\n(disabled with the count of items still needed). A save the server refuses\nkeeps the user on the step. Two levels of required feed a To continue\nchecklist whose items focus their fields: the save level (lab number,\npatient or the no-patient decision, sample type) and the complete level\n(provider where required; collection date, time and collector or lab\nsampling per sample; consent where required). The site setting only marks\nits field, as OGC-1201 decided.\n\nPrepare Samples holds the storage location, notes and skip decision and\nthe refer-out section, and saves them with the step. The Sample check\nreleases the order for testing, asks for a reason when Optional acceptance\nhas unanswered items, and finishes with \"Order X complete\". The dashboard\nshows the recorded status, Continue or Open, Cancel order with a reason\ndialog, the highlight of the order Save and exit came from and the finish\nnotice. The stepper and context card read the recorded progress.\n\nDefaults a step sets for itself (workflow type, generated lab number, EQA\npre-set) no longer mark an untouched order dirty, so it does not say\n\"Unsaved changes\" or prompt on leave. A reopened order''s patient card\noffers Edit details, which opens the locked patient form. The\nenvironmental and vector lanes keep their footer and steps.\n\n* test(e2e): OGC-1266 clinical order entry v4 specs\n\nA new spec walks the clinical lane end to end: the entry checklist and\nits two required levels, Save and exit with the dashboard highlight,\nPrepare Samples with lab sampling and skipped storage saved with the step,\nthe release with a reason (or Save and finish when the Sample check is\noff), the finish notice and status, Cancel order with a reason and the\nCancelled filter, and Discard on a never-saved order.\n\nThe specs that clicked the old footer or the Label & Store step follow\nthe new labels and steps; the storage picker spec deep-links into Prepare\nSamples and checks the retired address redirects there.\n\n* fix(order): OGC-1266 review: env release, skip storage, cancel guards, XML escaping\n\nThe Prepare Samples gate applies to the clinical lane only: the\nenvironmental and vector Sample check releases from Entered again, on the\nserver and on the step.\n\nThe skip-storage decision is written to the stored row by the progress\nservice, so a reopened order (saved through a detached copy) keeps it.\n\nCancel refuses an order once any test has moved past Not started, cancels\nthe sample items the way Edit Order does, and leaves the order''s own status\nalone. A cancelled order opens read-only with no Edit.\n\nThe collector and the other free-text sample attributes are escaped in\nthe sample XML, so a name with an apostrophe saves.\n\nOptional acceptance asks for a release reason only while a specimen''s\nchecklist is still pending. Orders saved before the status existed are\nbackfilled from the QA checklist row and the collection dates. Prepare\nSamples no longer opens as \"Unsaved changes\", the checklist targets exist,\nthe Discard dialog names the counts plainly, and the cancel and release\nerror codes have labels.\n\n* test(e2e): OGC-1266 release step tolerates an empty acceptance checklist\n\nThe CI database configures no clinical acceptance items, so Optional\nacceptance has nothing to answer and the first release succeeds. The spec\nnow asks for a reason only when the server refused the first release.","tree":{"sha":"9e9b418c7368fa6bac721bc038652b6dbb92f42f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/9e9b418c7368fa6bac721bc038652b6dbb92f42f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/8e3a7068451232ec3c6d20d6e03634b137615936","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e9b418c7368fa6bac721bc038652b6dbb92f42f\nparent bbdf344a42e7acc6ca2f6f670420ba9f7affc572\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1790826656 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790826656 +0300\n\nfeat(order): OGC-1266 clinical order entry v4: three steps, whole-step saves, order progress and cancel (#4490)\n\n* feat(order): OGC-1266 record order progress, gate release and cancel orders\n\nThe order carries an explicit progress status (Entered, Samples prepared,\nReady for testing, Cancelled) with the time each step completed, instead of\ninferring completion from a QA checklist row. The step''s save advances it:\nthe entry save records Entered, a Prepare Samples save made with the step\ncomplete records Samples prepared, and the Sample check''s release records\nReady for testing after a server-side gate (Mandatory acceptance unanswered\nis refused, Optional unanswered needs a reason, which is stored).\n\nPOST /rest/order/cancel records a reason from a new dictionary category,\ncancels the open tests and marks the sample cancelled; cancelled orders\nleave the open lists and show under the Cancelled filter.\n\nStorage travels with the order save: the sample XML carries condition\nnotes and the order carries the skip-storage decision, and the assignment\nlistener assigns, moves or updates notes from what the save says. An item\nnever stored reads back with a quantity snapshot but no location id, so\nthe id decides whether the item is already assigned.\n\nThe FHIR ServiceRequest create hands the save a detached shell of an\nexisting sample, so the progress is read from and written to the stored\nrow and the shell is brought up to date. The numeric who-cancelled column\nmaps through the project''s number user type like sys_user_id does.\n\nThe clinical side menu names Prepare Samples and Sample check and drops\nLabel & Store, which Prepare Samples absorbs.\n\n* feat(order): OGC-1266 clinical steps, footer, checklist and dashboard status\n\nClinical order entry is three steps: Enter Order, Prepare Samples (the\nCollect step, absorbing Label & Store) and Sample check, which exists\nonly while the clinical sample acceptance setting is not Off. The retired\n/order/clinical/label address opens Prepare Samples; an unknown step opens\nthe dashboard.\n\nEvery clinical step ends in the same footer: Discard (confirms, names what\nis lost, discards a never-saved order), Save and exit (back to the\ndashboard with the order highlighted) and Save and next or Save and finish\n(disabled with the count of items still needed). A save the server refuses\nkeeps the user on the step. Two levels of required feed a To continue\nchecklist whose items focus their fields: the save level (lab number,\npatient or the no-patient decision, sample type) and the complete level\n(provider where required; collection date, time and collector or lab\nsampling per sample; consent where required). The site setting only marks\nits field, as OGC-1201 decided.\n\nPrepare Samples holds the storage location, notes and skip decision and\nthe refer-out section, and saves them with the step. The Sample check\nreleases the order for testing, asks for a reason when Optional acceptance\nhas unanswered items, and finishes with \"Order X complete\". The dashboard\nshows the recorded status, Continue or Open, Cancel order with a reason\ndialog, the highlight of the order Save and exit came from and the finish\nnotice. The stepper and context card read the recorded progress.\n\nDefaults a step sets for itself (workflow type, generated lab number, EQA\npre-set) no longer mark an untouched order dirty, so it does not say\n\"Unsaved changes\" or prompt on leave. A reopened order''s patient card\noffers Edit details, which opens the locked patient form. The\nenvironmental and vector lanes keep their footer and steps.\n\n* test(e2e): OGC-1266 clinical order entry v4 specs\n\nA new spec walks the clinical lane end to end: the entry checklist and\nits two required levels, Save and exit with the dashboard highlight,\nPrepare Samples with lab sampling and skipped storage saved with the step,\nthe release with a reason (or Save and finish when the Sample check is\noff), the finish notice and status, Cancel order with a reason and the\nCancelled filter, and Discard on a never-saved order.\n\nThe specs that clicked the old footer or the Label & Store step follow\nthe new labels and steps; the storage picker spec deep-links into Prepare\nSamples and checks the retired address redirects there.\n\n* fix(order): OGC-1266 review: env release, skip storage, cancel guards, XML escaping\n\nThe Prepare Samples gate applies to the clinical lane only: the\nenvironmental and vector Sample check releases from Entered again, on the\nserver and on the step.\n\nThe skip-storage decision is written to the stored row by the progress\nservice, so a reopened order (saved through a detached copy) keeps it.\n\nCancel refuses an order once any test has moved past Not started, cancels\nthe sample items the way Edit Order does, and leaves the order''s own status\nalone. A cancelled order opens read-only with no Edit.\n\nThe collector and the other free-text sample attributes are escaped in\nthe sample XML, so a name with an apostrophe saves.\n\nOptional acceptance asks for a release reason only while a specimen''s\nchecklist is still pending. Orders saved before the status existed are\nbackfilled from the QA checklist row and the collection dates. Prepare\nSamples no longer opens as \"Unsaved changes\", the checklist targets exist,\nthe Discard dialog names the counts plainly, and the cancel and release\nerror codes have labels.\n\n* test(e2e): OGC-1266 release step tolerates an empty acceptance checklist\n\nThe CI database configures no clinical acceptance items, so Optional\nacceptance has nothing to answer and the first release succeeds. The spec\nnow asks for a reason only when the server refused the first release.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvdigCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABLsQACZXDkaP1Q4k882n+0OGRtn6\nnWKrJ8YGMnDPXIcHCqCv1yq87YZSQ3kdhdAhQ6ag5eNvYIPBf0zpQryTikA49FZW\nxwAWroM6KZFhvCR7xjIJ6Brpi4G/G1JriUs8lFbpsxXCmRJbF7ClXia+nGCFfMev\nFHvOYFiQSWNXb/Cc/M9qHne5PWNZ3TETXVhCQd7tJSJgOqZ16TAwZPUaQxATBj9I\nysL1npUVpNxtAcsDxldWg4M9Sbz8dAomq3XtqBWX8nt90UHi5rmuQwDiEXOQsW5x\nIedy8EVJhuEq7IF0ta0FUMTD8LWlEjRqqAgTnEgjd/3+jMnFpvzaEPeuhFeQBYUX\n0xPEnYHQloISt0rNj6fuGxFnmYOzJIFsWSEFhLmTPoB4sbZBdufbstz3xLr0CYJc\n/s/jm8BxofJYrrz/iNl7gq0ZOHlj16WGv9M4VE1b/dRI+M0lVb9rbv35bhSi/qNA\nR6nHUZiRMF6lOYO/oz02QtxpQgfoH3WSZK3E7fvkQKKIZf4ZSbjSUd6YwRVKBf1u\nEGJo8ixD68iUq2PjCBPei2fL+8Mb+euvC6bD1ZdlCpgsm9mpOX3nw93qClu/H9Mx\nnHk3Ky692zDVh2yg6NfD4ci0mOqR17r2IOIJldebg0xcrMxmICR+rVC5fPJD6Ugu\nVro1hE4lnqmZUFliqIJf\n=X6i9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026