FA1DvVDw++v3o1\nXFmVOU9trpJQI1AxrzbKSNhK+u6j7ahDzdgo0G88rTXpqL+U/eB+Yj9ZI+TFNCJI\nQGqdvIxgbdrOp/F6gzp8gypcpzcnQwSmtaXox98AAqv+uQGBpwnO5x9w/ghnOFpt\ns7zSv0W4WC0Km0LAGiTMnzmnz7d/RQefCt9hNJbMNjPcnhOHYSAI3j+peTxyo0VE\nkGV+3sxCFzPxb3LE4HElMfUx1a3IueUDMOOtvF/676q+YSWcBofOSKX1IDFqgTRI\n0AQOFNrXwLM41D6UrmE3dyZC4guRG7241W/IiDPuL76j0nZXgK+qzGN97leOwUXF\n6ZmlhDQRpi8uSk2xuJapiwt+DbyAZhDroL/56QGeuL684Ws9U01xqsCJx/yk0LE8\ntUeFKqYE/Vbhv+M//Yz0bEfwKB3MLY++Q0AP3ZCgkxjEvjnNQg8b4yIQMZCpO96u\nxfGHoV7jkylq3+ZghkDblgXCKEuGS0elSTJS+PMwoMvPwgrQiK3pihffSFVvjwjW\njcJnyvFhpQ7xHw05B4D1bLEO+VWvMi0db6Dld3vpGUEHxyaE+Q5batOobMNF+Bza\no6RepjfYe8+Y6NojjnCM+hpf6cBIYCHJCMQZ2DEl+NMiTKc1PiYHRYUfMe51Oey4\nUyMtE84W2LzQWYrBtAA7\n=+Cw9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T00:31:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/bbdf344a42e7acc6ca2f6f670420ba9f7affc572","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKGJiZGYzNDRhNDJlN2FjYzZjYTJmNmY2NzA0MjBiYTlmN2FmZmM1NzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/3f42f5615d1c266b6f6ffd3ae94a0b8226558db6","sha":"3f42f5615d1c266b6f6ffd3ae94a0b8226558db6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/3f42f5615d1c266b6f6ffd3ae94a0b8226558db6"}],"sha":"bbdf344a42e7acc6ca2f6f670420ba9f7affc572","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/bbdf344a42e7acc6ca2f6f670420ba9f7affc572"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/3f42f5615d1c266b6f6ffd3ae94a0b8226558db6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T21:16:19Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T21:16:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(OGC-1054): return the delivery receipt reference (#4347)\n\nAdds receiptId to the /analyzer/fhir acceptance response, and pins the\nwire-level idempotency contract with a test that posts the same bundle\ntwice.\n\nThe Analyzer Bridge now holds a received result until OpenELIS accepts\nit, which makes delivery at-least-once: the bridge cannot tell an answer\nthat was lost from a delivery that failed, so it sends the result again.\nThis side already deduplicates those repeats. What was missing was\nanything for the sender to confirm against. Without a reference, an\noperator asking \"did that result actually land\" had only the bridge''s own\nlogs to go on.\n\nThe receipt id is the identifier of the durable acceptance record, so a\nrepeat of an accepted delivery returns the same value rather than a new\none. That is what makes it usable as proof: identical answer, identical\nreference, no second clinical result.\n\nThe existing service-level tests already prove the deduplication. The new\ntest proves the same thing through the endpoint the bridge actually\ncalls, asserting the two responses are byte-identical and that neither a\nsecond staging row nor a second acceptance was recorded.","tree":{"sha":"87a0a4a2edba951311a50998a7289d2d0fbcc01b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/87a0a4a2edba951311a50998a7289d2d0fbcc01b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/3f42f5615d1c266b6f6ffd3ae94a0b8226558db6","verification":{"payload":"tree 87a0a4a2edba951311a50998a7289d2d0fbcc01b\nparent dba9d0781474f6a1a29b3535e1a89bc1f371281d\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1790802979 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790802979 -0700\n\nfeat(OGC-1054): return the delivery receipt reference (#4347)\n\nAdds receiptId to the /analyzer/fhir acceptance response, and pins the\nwire-level idempotency contract with a test that posts the same bundle\ntwice.\n\nThe Analyzer Bridge now holds a received result until OpenELIS accepts\nit, which makes delivery at-least-once: the bridge cannot tell an answer\nthat was lost from a delivery that failed, so it sends the result again.\nThis side already deduplicates those repeats. What was missing was\nanything for the sender to confirm against. Without a reference, an\noperator asking \"did that result actually land\" had only the bridge''s own\nlogs to go on.\n\nThe receipt id is the identifier of the durable acceptance record, so a\nrepeat of an accepted delivery returns the same value rather than a new\none. That is what makes it usable as proof: identical answer, identical\nreference, no second clinical result.\n\nThe existing service-level tests already prove the deduplication. The new\ntest proves the same thing through the endpoint the bridge actually\ncalls, asserting the two responses are byte-identical and that neither a\nsecond staging row nor a second acceptance was recorded.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvXwjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlqUQACxViOtUy2NuSMwFcVMCmh4o\nmdeqCTL4IuY+AuAIJjIzGrSbTpDD0848DzecY1s2A/KT/HPhYeg7s4g6FpT0CSQ9\nsFJOw6JNmO6c3PL34N7sWQf3qKaFXmMLFGXC20SNp8WY/lGrn1QtTGvJNQ3fHYUc\nZU0yl2dmH3kbZHqwE88yXveB6KSp7I/qU7u3QSNY7SjbWVH4O26fImXzlZ3uJ188\nQQv5/2/wCd71sTFpgYthYZZnJe8Co1/dRh+imkwzwCbax4rCDXOXhTmgkfF7kha8\n/5Yt3DfAgmoKFyi9vyU1QMBxXBBYc5cpIgVH+fiM9ES8EuLJmzSDSduNbG2rlj7f\n6cqD8rSI4kTWQmPNgG6uvwkYhAb1nvrmnLyT7cjTW4b92yqDBeGPziIGeHOxerba\nhrQuiV/eg9cLdkktcJAWtPGCyog122YLizJ+dlRAGe0oYlWeJjd/Hbl8dU1wenBx\nJR0I1DBjUQGhjQzK3eDXfQX+nXLBAD6ehgfl8agSMc+46BmpNDhYd1wLbPqRgc7i\nQYIuYwdwmsx/e2hEIjlup0X0iWJshF9e56QqITfPPr3Bc4ZaduESXyL0ofJPmDus\ntuYt8Wxyk/v2j8gWFPTd2LKbeh5oKMoC1VEfQ60ghWKU7Zw/CXMgD4tRUX/Glkuf\nmZQUSqPh76zoMvRYr1I+\n=AB+r\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T21:16:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.g