tps://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/dba9d0781474f6a1a29b3535e1a89bc1f371281d","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKGRiYTlkMDc4MTQ3NGY2YTFhMjliMzUzNWUxYTg5YmMxZjM3MTI4MWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/df63bf123a4233dc22658f27b09e418a4125b010","sha":"df63bf123a4233dc22658f27b09e418a4125b010","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/df63bf123a4233dc22658f27b09e418a4125b010"}],"sha":"dba9d0781474f6a1a29b3535e1a89bc1f371281d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/dba9d0781474f6a1a29b3535e1a89bc1f371281d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/df63bf123a4233dc22658f27b09e418a4125b010/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:25:50Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:25:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(analyzers): keep a grouping''s new tests on a specimen they can all use (#4485)\n\n* fix(analyzers): keep a grouping''s new tests on a specimen they can all use\n\nEvery new analysis in an accepted grouping is saved on the grouping''s one\nsample item. The hold compared reviewers'' specimen choices but not the\ntests'' own sample types, so two new tests linked to different single\ntypes were saved together on the first test''s type, and on an order with\nan entered sample the item was whichever new row came last. The hold and\nevery sample-item builder now use the one set of types that all new,\nactive analyses in the grouping share: with no shared type the grouping\nstays staged awaiting a specimen, and otherwise its item comes from that\nset.\n\nThe existing-order builders also set the order''s status, entry date and\nuser before knowing whether any result would be saved. Inside the accept\ntransaction the order is managed, so those changes were written at commit\neven when every result was skipped and the grouping discarded. Only a\ngrouping that saves a result now changes its order.\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the stack merge and the seventh review pass\n\nMarks the landing steps and the three stack rows done at their develop\ncommits, records the two post-merge findings on #4448 that the previous\ncommit fixes, and gives the intermittent ogc-1192 failure its cause, fixed\non develop by #4483.\n\n* docs(analyzers): name #4485 and keep the landing''s open maintainer steps","tree":{"sha":"86a2605a19278a2f5cacbb2b1cb8459335148aff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/86a2605a19278a2f5cacbb2b1cb8459335148aff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/df63bf123a4233dc22658f27b09e418a4125b010","verification":{"payload":"tree 86a2605a19278a2f5cacbb2b1cb8459335148aff\nparent cb5682eb3e10a917041d24c08ed21beeeefc86bf\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1790774750 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790774750 -0700\n\nfix(analyzers): keep a grouping''s new tests on a specimen they can all use (#4485)\n\n* fix(analyzers): keep a grouping''s new tests on a specimen they can all use\n\nEvery new analysis in an accepted grouping is saved on the grouping''s one\nsample item. The hold compared reviewers'' specimen choices but not the\ntests'' own sample types, so two new tests linked to different single\ntypes were saved together on the first test''s type, and on an order with\nan entered sample the item was whichever new row came last. The hold and\nevery sample-item builder now use the one set of types that all new,\nactive analyses in the grouping share: with no shared type the grouping\nstays staged awaiting a specimen, and otherwise its item comes from that\nset.\n\nThe existing-order builders also set the order''s status, entry date and\nuser before knowing whether any result would be saved. Inside the accept\ntransaction the order is managed, so those changes were written at commit\neven when every result was skipped and the grouping discarded. Only a\ngrouping that saves a result now changes its order.\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the stack merge and the seventh review pass\n\nMarks the landing steps and the three stack rows done at their develop\ncommits, records the two post-merge findings on #4448 that the previous\ncommit fixes, and gives the intermittent ogc-1192 failure its cause, fixed\non develop by #4483.\n\n* docs(analyzers): name #4485 and keep the landing''s open maintainer steps","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvQ3eCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAz5kQADPZDmlrqCsnNEpDRPVgkHX/\nm8LE+IHuhPmLo6JyR+AcIEHpcWce8ZveX6jVvIuV05jN6UTufEuO9XqEQfcPQUlZ\nJFPyypoHzUdqalBtLIIW6L1vcS0o/+QA2ahkKcnNwdelxG38fCrVT2eskrUe/QFM\n0WtjsSq3baXOQYi0KyqBpkbdY/sOB1sMV18N6YOFNXUOQIOB/543Sh4H5bO8qxMV\nEzqjCYwemNNZvzxkQU39ijK/WHdzKJFLLWFBPc+xrMB8aRVssO7FUxTDRtvI+mQ+\nQgMiuMPNOCuO11Zsc/kWbnHLP94G+5/GHuXSxkw+S48Zr1G7B9vj6C2MfrbknUVk\n91dv+wnwtA/uI2AnrVQWh8z3uvHtRE973SY6ieHvxJNQj/+GlfqdyCslA3Bj1Y6S\nR1WfsoWwNvFH4vrcNAJcQFHz35T+A52oXekxeqZMNPOoYD9qde8i/GzwEr44wo44\nVId5IsgvIGjc61KLouMfgqHMqQiwEtg3QpwgwIaDyaLh3EoO8OR8JYJWN2Yj0gq2\neV0CJiUWvTDPLqk4xt0nyOpzxzlNivEsZi7dyZIVknSeNd7Xy70YbgmJh+Hrr3Oi\nXlQSe05zTMEhWM2SEgUHP79sNtiLJYbu9BUEtan2Lwp6+ikozWR6cwJEdyLKKRhx\ni4ZVngVaiLc86Vx9kR94\n=QwDe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:25:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/df63bf123a4233dc22658f27b09e418a4125b010","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKGRmNjNiZjEyM2E0MjMzZGMyMjY1OGYyN2IwOWU0MThhNDEyNWIwMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/cb5682eb3e10a917041d24c08ed21beeeefc86bf","sha":"cb5682eb3e10a917041d24c08ed21beeeefc86bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/cb5682eb3e10a917041d24c08ed21beeeefc86bf"}],"sha":"df63bf123a4233dc22658f27b09e418a4125b010","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/df63bf123a4233dc22658f27b09e418a4125b010"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29783151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/cb5682eb3e10a917041d24c08ed21beeeefc86bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:50:39Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:50:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(order): OGC-1407 keep one patient per order across saves (#4488)\n\nSaving an order entered with a new patient more than once created a patient record per save and moved the order to the newest one: the patient form rewrote the order''s patient from its own fields on every render and dropped the id the first save returned. The order now adopts the saved patient''s id from the save and keeps it, the New Patient tab shows the saved patient locked with an Edit toggle, and edits are compared against the record as chosen or last saved, so an edit to a selected patient is saved instead of going out as no change. The server keeps an order''s patient when a save asks to add the same person again, and a refused duplicate national id is a 400 naming the patient who holds it instead of a bare 500 (the patient validator''s errors could not be merged into the order''s binding result). The order screens no longer show notifications twice while the New Patient tab is open. Verified live on dev compose through every order-entry lane plus legacy Add Order, with a new Playwright spec, full backend and frontend suites, and CI green.","tree":{"sha":"30ca35414891cbfee3b2cd96e254e0e1b5824472","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/30ca35414891cbfee3b2cd96e254e0e1b5824472"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/cb5682eb3e10a917041d24c08ed21beeeefc86bf","verification":{"payload":"tree 30ca35414891cbfee3b2cd96e254e0e1b5824472\nparent dd4a08178d26850a84b7ba10d7e5cfe32bc8c8cf\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1790772639 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790772639 +0300\n\nfix(order): OGC-1407 keep one patient per order across saves (#4488)\n\nSaving an order entered with a new patient more than once created a patient record per save and moved the order to the newest one: the patient form rewrote the order''s patient from its own fields on every render and dropped the id the first save returned. The order now adopts the saved patient''s id from the save and keeps it, the New Patient tab shows the saved patient locked with an Edit toggle, and edits are compared against the record as chosen or last saved, so an edit to a selected patient is saved instead of going out as no change. The server keeps an order''s patient when a save asks to add the same person again, and a refused duplicate national id is a 400 naming the patient who holds it instead of a bare 500 (the patient validator''s errors could not be merged into the order''s binding result). The order screens no longer show notifications twice while the New Patient tab is open. Verified live on dev compose through every order-entry lane plus legacy Add Order, with a new Playwright spec, full backend and frontend suites, and CI green.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvQWfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAE7MQAKqb7CbnvV9mF02rtylu4jTa\ntOmRuHyw8Xf8Vyo3Yb/LRWQ/OWGwzLnu1Bp75L/S4uk2ZAY6sBGDEvkX2JMCdyVa\naNP49C077v57ED+MGoCxoPPiJBhiYPfdYvR757d98WFAqzz9IjeDNUbQIwUQPK3v\n4KRpgDRt2NxEv+UUaxmveFOMeE5GQpwQWXeXwR7ZRkcXfjyTOWANmHLjiEmbCNPy\nYfKS04HCveo5iPnMI/4mkvACweaYb9TXT8NAGBXXwdn1CRGm4tZQxtd9KiXI0dWC\nkvk/0iwVqYbmKnDycTxGKSRLcDR8JxYgJuQot45PXhXlVeYhQFVCjUDQC3k8sbxL\noKCcFmTOzuTdPAo2ishoGkI8KCKUkMDwzuOFQ+U3wdqCfQWqVqaCyj3zIDJMj2p4\n1/k3ABzKDl0E8o73MjgM4h8AJ7ZPn46jn14KCG6ymKBMX8gWa6m4g++r86KRybu0\nMx0DwNgjl0WRxAMvOr+DwY4BzkCqHJfopOkU8EDU3Un2hiryDsA7Yah4iciGAmJc\n0Zigex01pGXVCcq8p7WnftmPoI7Qy1YfvTLxe0jQ6Uf+/FoL/XQctBP8vL4dUqiy\nDgJJIsmlW9M6i+wNFvRHqBbphvDAyryrHWmIXbTPztvrQjhgiGFdrCxIJBoqDATE\nljyLG6UhNNcwCCP04rNa\n=0zBF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T12:50:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":