events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/c2aed566ff95fbc9554f566542e6e34287b1869b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T03:18:53Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T03:18:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(analyzers): hold only observations with invalid mappings (#4449)\n\n* fix(analyzers): limit invalid mappings to affected observations\n\n* test(analyzers): prove mixed mapping recovery through clinical readback\n\n* test(analyzers): show both saved clinical results in recovery evidence\n\n* docs(analyzers): reflect review-ready mapping validity PR\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the stack restack and gated landing steps\n\nStack #4472 now sits on develop 91db9a80aa. The restack onto #4471 stopped\nonce, in the harness compose file, and was resolved to the union of both\nsides; each rebased branch''s tree equals a merge of its previous head with\ndevelop.\n\nThe remediation plan gains a landing section with one gate per step:\nthe second mapping-hop fix, restack, current-head checks, durable\nevidence links, the R0-REV3 interrupt proof, approval and the atomic\nstack merge. Stale ''in progress'' and ''new heads need fresh checks''\nwording is replaced, and the PR cleanup table reflects merged #4430 and\n#4382 and the failing #4429.\n\n* docs(analyzers): set the stack''s landing goal and evidence plan\n\nThe landing section now states the goal (stack #4472 mergeable and ready\nfor the maintainer''s review), numbered acceptance criteria, an ordered\nplan with a status column, and the alternatives that were rejected.\n\nIt records why the earlier recordings were not usable evidence: since\n#4430 the parity runner passes PLAYWRIGHT_SLOWMO=0, overriding the video\nprojects'' 500 ms default, and the analyzer video tests used none of the\nvideo-gated presentation helpers. The plan adds the runner fix, per-PR\npresentation cards and one packaged recording run from the top of the\nstack.\n\nThe second mapping-visit defect is recorded as suspected until a test\nreproduces it.\n\n* test(analyzers): present the invalid-binding workflow on video\n\nThe per-observation mapping-validity story opens with a chapter card,\nmarks the point where only the result with an inactive clinical test is\nheld, shows the correction and retry of the original row, and closes on\nboth results in the clinical record. Presentation runs only in the video\nprojects; the assertions are unchanged.\n\n* docs(analyzers): mark the second-visit fix and video prerequisites done\n\nL1 was reproduced by a test before it was fixed. The video prerequisites\nlanded with each PR carrying its own presentation cards; the M3 guided\nsetup demo is left without them because no PR here claims it and the\nharness demo guard rejects title-card waits in demo specs. The plan also\nrecords one intermittent develop failure in Modify Order''s environmental\nredirect, with what its trace showed.\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the review fixes and where landing results live\n\nThe first Codex pass on the final heads found two defects, now fixed on\n#4448 and #4470. The status column points at where each remaining result\nis recorded (PR checks, the evidence bundle, #4470''s thread) instead of\nrestating results in this document.\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the second review pass on #4448\n\nThe re-review found two defects in releasing awaiting-specimen results;\nboth are fixed on #4448 with integration tests.\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the third review pass\n\nFour more findings in lines this stack changed, all fixed on #4448 and\n#4470.\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the fourth review pass\n\nTwo more findings on #4448, both fixed with tests.\n\n* test(analyzers): restore the stock RIF test even when the invalid-binding story fails\n\nThe story deactivates the shared stock RIF test to invalidate its\nbinding and reactivates it later in the body. A failure in between left\nthe test inactive for every later scenario and rerun on that database.\nAn afterEach hook now reactivates any stock test a story left inactive;\nit runs after a timeout too, unlike cleanup at the end of the body.\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the fifth review pass\n\nTwo P2 findings, fixed on #4448 and #4449.\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the sixth review pass\n\nOne more finding on #4448, fixed with a test.","tree":{"sha":"5efab58eea8b697536748c0aa25709b5e1515b43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/5efab58eea8b697536748c0aa25709b5e1515b43"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/c2aed566ff95fbc9554f566542e6e34287b1869b","verification":{"payload":"tree 5efab58eea8b697536748c0aa25709b5e1515b43\nparent 2aec1c10daa5ead02aa8f056aa6c93bcb9d34ea4\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1790738333 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790738333 -0700\n\nfix(analyzers): hold only observations with invalid mappings (#4449)\n\n* fix(analyzers): limit invalid mappings to affected observations\n\n* test(analyzers): prove mixed mapping recovery through clinical readback\n\n* test(analyzers): show both saved clinical results in recovery evidence\n\n* docs(analyzers): reflect review-ready mapping validity PR\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the stack restack and gated landing steps\n\nStack #4472 now sits on develop 91db9a80aa. The restack onto #4471 stopped\nonce, in the harness compose file, and was resolved to the union of both\nsides; each rebased branch''s tree equals a merge of its previous head with\ndevelop.\n\nThe remediation plan gains a landing section with one gate per step:\nthe second mapping-hop fix, restack, current-head checks, durable\nevidence links, the R0-REV3 interrupt proof, approval and the atomic\nstack merge. Stale ''in progress'' and ''new heads need fresh checks''\nwording is replaced, and the PR cleanup table reflects merged #4430 and\n#4382 and the failing #4429.\n\n* docs(analyzers): set the stack''s landing goal and evidence plan\n\nThe landing section now states the goal (stack #4472 mergeable and ready\nfor the maintainer''s review), numbered acceptance criteria, an ordered\nplan with a status column, and the alternatives that were rejected.\n\nIt records why the earlier recordings were not usable evidence: since\n#4430 the parity runner passes PLAYWRIGHT_SLOWMO=0, overriding the video\nprojects'' 500 ms default, and the analyzer video tests used none of the\nvideo-gated presentation helpers. The plan adds the runner fix, per-PR\npresentation cards and one packaged recording run from the top of the\nstack.\n\nThe second mapping-visit defect is recorded as suspected until a test\nreproduces it.\n\n* test(analyzers): present the invalid-binding workflow on video\n\nThe per-observation mapping-validity story opens with a chapter card,\nmarks the point where only the result with an inactive clinical test is\nheld, shows the correction and retry of the original row, and closes on\nboth results in the clinical record. Presentation runs only in the video\nprojects; the assertions are unchanged.\n\n* docs(analyzers): mark the second-visit fix and video prerequisites done\n\nL1 was reproduced by a test before it was fixed. The video prerequisites\nlanded with each PR carrying its own presentation cards; the M3 guided\nsetup demo is left without them because no PR here claims it and the\nharness demo guard rejects title-card waits in demo specs. The plan also\nrecords one intermittent develop failure in Modify Order''s environmental\nredirect, with what its trace showed.\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the review fixes and where landing results live\n\nThe first Codex pass on the final heads found two defects, now fixed on\n#4448 and #4470. The status column points at where each remaining result\nis recorded (PR checks, the evidence bundle, #4470''s thread) instead of\nrestating results in this document.\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the second review pass on #4448\n\nThe re-review found two defects in releasing awaiting-specimen results;\nboth are fixed on #4448 with integration tests.\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the third review pass\n\nFour more findings in lines this stack changed, all fixed on #4448 and\n#4470.\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the fourth review pass\n\nTwo more findings on #4448, both fixed with tests.\n\n* test(analyzers): restore the stock RIF test even when the invalid-binding story fails\n\nThe story deactivates the shared stock RIF test to invalidate its\nbinding and reactivates it later in the body. A failure in between left\nthe test inactive for every later scenario and rerun on that database.\nAn afterEach hook now reactivates any stock test a story left inactive;\nit runs after a timeout too, unlike cleanup at the end of the body.\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the fifth review pass\n\nTwo P2 findings, fixed on #4448 and #4449.\n\n* docs(analyzers): record the sixth review pass\n\nOne more finding on #4448, fixed with a test.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvH+dCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACfMQAGzw7jnh62UJAUmyMf94AB8T\nEzT8qFG0mBgVscH7bV9VsRTrrVcxxxu2HaIEgZQ7XtqjCMz5Xesup6lh3n3ohEjO\naWKDRbe6UKs+Ti1oSPuGwzDWe67ddQ/LyOfFiWaeo2ZNH3gs72kNEjtZ/VwTdKtV\n48GSZrBD3WGiga/DoSSlGl4GTFrAwR2SrUOWAzE/ljzzBVqFzMDYiCh9A9Nwuh3K\nVZZVa+1FaRrp4sGdZYG740rKHfsBvK2XReJe6Gy2/W35NiqCBTnUh1FgfnwnBc19\nUHT0gfIJFVvo8wUfLx1VSMYBqyj8GwgWVsy2YyDzsXg9OstTWsKtlNbOPSacpFtF\nOgj1ojipCM4E9VO3I+qr4gmpBNI3eYqz+YAZlnJmEmcmw6ciwMrjcscycela0xSc\nwK1vlTnLtwfTH4Wr0uPFpni384zUPHB1vY8kjEGMGELiq4Fh6aGtPsyeCrWZYYiu\n4dzMor1QKia8j4JS+9qgRbAibJVCPaBnK0JZ66C3TGGj+wSJqZEU9UJ2s8TfMcwn\nvMhlhtdEr9udpP7/1YN0zZ4TsW6GKhH5mkvyZgNIH0MxKpcuSNj6HAtkNAJXHI8R\n/KXaL5vjPtFclErDp4Wnrh0SKrESzUtuCuQlG7fjwj10sqlnmVBCX4SJ6o86mY9l\nLM+bjrqM6hnM0iX5Uhrc\n=zvLS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T03:18:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/c2aed566ff95fbc9554f566542e6e34287b1869b","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKGMyYWVkNTY2ZmY5NWZiYzk1NTRmNTY2NTQyZTZlMzQyODdiMTg2OWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/2aec1c10daa5ead02aa8f056aa6c93bcb9d34ea4","sha":"2aec1c10daa5ead02aa8f056aa6c93bcb9d34ea4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/2aec1c10daa5ead02aa8f056aa6c93bcb9d34ea4"}],"sha":"c2aed566ff95fbc9554f566542e6e34287b1869b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/c2aed566ff95fbc9554f566542e6e34287b1869b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/2aec1c10daa5ead02aa8f056aa6c93bcb9d34ea4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T03:17:42Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T03:17:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(analyzers): retain held observations and unblock review recovery (#4448)\n\n* fix(analyzers): retain held rows and restore review recovery\n\n* docs(analyzers): explain direct held-result recovery\n\n* style(analyzers): wrap recovery guide for Spotless\n\n* Keep mixed held and mapped result groups actionable\n\n* Require confirmed mappings before UI retry\n\n* Keep held controls out of review cleanup\n\n* fix(test): permit canonical video-only demo pacing\n\n* fix(analyzers): require current confirmation before mapping adoption\n\n* test(analyzers): prove held GeneXpert result recovery through UI\n\n* fix(analyzers): preserve review edits across mapping recovery\n\n* test(analyzers): prove mixed GeneXpert recovery through clinical review\n\n* test(analyzers): align held-result recovery fixture with confirmation guard\n\n* test(analyzers): confirm binding before persistence selection\n\n* fix(analyzers): keep unsaved review choices across repeated mapping visits\n\nA choice made on the analyzer worklist survived one trip to a held\nresult''s mapping page but not a second. Returning restored the choice\ninto the reloaded rows, and the table then cleared its record of unsaved\nedits whenever results changed, so the next visit carried nothing back.\n\nThe worklist now passes the edits it restored to the table, which keeps\nthem as unsaved drafts until the user saves. A new test walks the real\nworklist through two mapping visits; it failed on the second visit before\nthis change.\n\nhistory is declared as a direct dependency; the mapping editor already\nimports it at runtime and it had resolved only through react-router-dom.\n\n* test(analyzers): present the held-result recovery workflow on video\n\nThe mixed GeneXpert recovery story opens with a chapter card, marks the\npoint where only the unmapped RIF observation is held, and closes on\nboth results in the clinical record. Presentation runs only in the video\nprojects; the assertions are unchanged.\n\n* test(analyzers): assert each mapping visit without an expect message\n\njest/valid-expect rejects the message argument; each visit is now its\nown call and assertion. The test still fails on the second visit without\nthe fix and passes with it.\n\n* fix(analyzers): keep a skipped inactive-test result staged beside saved siblings\n\nAccept skips a result whose test or lab unit is inactive when no analysis\nexists yet for it. The persist-count check this PR added still counted\nthat result, so the whole save rolled back and its valid siblings could\nnot be accepted; before the check, the skipped row was deleted from\nstaging without a result.\n\nEach sample grouping now records the rows it skipped. Those rows are left\nout of the count and stay staged; the siblings are saved. A new\nintegration test accepts a group with one active and one inactive test:\nit failed with \"would remove 2 observations but persist 1\" before this\nchange.\n\n* fix(analyzers): honor the chosen specimen and the staged order when releasing held results\n\nReleasing an awaiting-specimen result trusted the submitted row for which\norder and test it belonged to, so a changed accession created the result\nunder that accession. Every kept row now takes its order, test, control\nflag and analyzer from its staged row; the reviewer supplies only the\naction, specimen choice, note and result. A row whose staged order differs\nfrom the rest of its grouping stays staged.\n\nThe chosen specimen was also lost in two ways. On an order with an entered\nsample, a new test''s result went to the test''s first sample type. Where a\ngrouping''s new analyses share one new specimen, only the first row''s\nchoice was read, and a choice another result could not use was dropped.\nThe entered-sample path now narrows each result to its own choice. In the\none-specimen paths a grouping with conflicting choices, or a choice a new\nanalysis''s test cannot use, waits for a decision; otherwise the grouping''s\nchoice is used whichever row carries it.\n\nThree new integration tests failed before this change (the result saved\non the first sample type, an order created under the submitted accession,\nand an incompatible grouping saved); a fourth confirms a choice every\nresult can use is still saved.\n\n* docs(analyzers): explain the shared specimen for results received together\n\nResults for an order with no sample entered yet share one new specimen,\nso a specimen choice must suit all of them or they stay staged.\n\n* fix(analyzers): keep the staged component, one specimen per grouping, and no empty orders\n\nThree gaps remained in releasing held results:\n\n- The staged identity restore left the client''s component, so a changed\n  componentId could bind a multiplex value to another component''s test\n  result. The component now comes from the staged row too.\n- persistAnalyzerResults puts every new analysis of a grouping on its one\n  sample item, on an entered order as well. The one-specimen check was\n  limited to orders without an entered sample, so two new tests with\n  different choices on an entered order both saved on one specimen. The\n  check now applies to every grouping.\n- A grouping whose rows were all skipped still inserted its order and\n  sample item with no result. Such groupings are no longer persisted;\n  their rows stay staged.\n\nThree new integration tests failed before this change: the forged\ncomponent''s test result was used, both conflicting analyses were saved,\nand an empty order was created.\n\n* docs(analyzers): the shared specimen applies to every order''s new tests\n\nNew tests added to an order from one analyzer message share one specimen\nwhether or not a sample was entered; the guide said only the latter.\n\n* fix(analyzers): keep a restored review action on the grouping''s visible row\n\nThe worklist shows a grouping''s accept, reject and delete checkboxes on\none representative row, preferring actionable rows. When a held row led\nits grouping, its actionable sibling represented it and carried the\nreviewer''s tick. Recovering the held row during the mapping visit made it\nthe representative on return, so the restored tick sat on a hidden row:\nthe visible checkbox was clear, yet Save still accepted the grouping.\n\nA restored grouping action now moves to the grouping''s current\nrepresentative, and the other rows get their server values back. A new\nworklist test recovers the held row during the visit and failed before\nthis change.\n\n* fix(analyzers): take every server-derived field of a released result from its staged row\n\nThe staged-identity restore covered order, test, component, control flag\nand analyzer, but the accept path also writes the analyzer''s completion\ntime, result type and significant digits from the submitted row. A\nchanged completeDate therefore landed on the clinical analysis.\n\nThe restore now covers every field the review page derives from the\nstaged row and the accept path reads: completion time, result type, test\nname and significant digits are taken from the staged row too. A new\nintegration test submits a different completion date and failed before\nthis change.\n\n* fix(analyzers): record a released analyzer result as an automatic analysis\n\nThe accept path sets the analysis type from the submitted row''s manual\nflag, which neither the review page nor the controller ever sets. A\nsubmitted manual: true therefore recorded an analyzer result as a manual\nanalysis. The staged-identity restore now clears the flag. A new\nintegration test submits manual: true and failed before this change.\n\n* fix(analyzers): give a new test its chosen specimen beside an existing analysis\n\nOn an order with an entered sample, a grouping that held a result for a\ntest with an existing analysis and a new test with a chosen specimen put\nthe new analysis on the existing analysis''s sample item: the first row\nset the shared sample item, so the new test neither found nor created\none of its chosen type.\n\nNew analyses now resolve their own sample item from their allowed types,\nreusing the grouping''s new item when it fits; an existing analysis''s\nitem is used for the grouping only when nothing new is added. A new\nintegration test failed before this change with the result on the\nexisting analysis''s specimen.","tree":{"sha":"24fc57be7005556a0fbe5fe211352537f2175500","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/24fc57be7005556a0fbe5fe211352537f2175500"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/2aec1c10daa5ead02aa8f056aa6c93bcb9d34ea4","verification":{"payload":"tree 24fc57be7005556a0fbe5fe211352537f2175500\nparent 7d94adf63eaa7d9b4d6f740de91755fab777796b\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1790738262 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790738262 -0700\n\nfix(analyzers): retain held observations and unblock review recovery (#4448)\n\n* fix(analyzers): retain held rows and restore review recovery\n\n* docs(analyzers): explain direct held-result recovery\n\n* style(analyzers): wrap recovery guide for Spotless\n\n* Keep mixed held and mapped result groups actionable\n\n* Require confirmed mappings before UI retry\n\n* Keep held controls out of review cleanup\n\n* fix(test): permit canonical video-only demo pacing\n\n* fix(analyzers): require current confirmation before mapping adoption\n\n* test(analyzers): prove held GeneXpert result recovery through UI\n\n* fix(analyzers): preserve review edits across mapping recovery\n\n* test(analyzers): prove mixed GeneXpert recovery through clinical review\n\n* test(analyzers): align held-result recovery fixture with confirmation guard\n\n* test(analyzers): confirm binding before persistence selection\n\n* fix(analyzers): keep unsaved review choices across repeated mapping visits\n\nA choice made on the analyzer worklist survived one trip to a held\nresult''s mapping page but not a second. Returning restored the choice\ninto the reloaded rows, and the table then cleared its record of unsaved\nedits whenever results changed, so the next visit carried nothing back.\n\nThe worklist now passes the edits it restored to the table, which keeps\nthem as unsaved drafts until the user saves. A new test walks the real\nworklist through two mapping visits; it failed on the second visit before\nthis change.\n\nhistory is declared as a direct dependency; the mapping editor already\nimports it at runtime and it had resolved only through react-router-dom.\n\n* test(analyzers): present the held-result recovery workflow on video\n\nThe mixed GeneXpert recovery story opens with a chapter card, marks the\npoint where only the unmapped RIF observation is held, and closes on\nboth results in the clinical record. Presentation runs only in the video\nprojects; the assertions are unchanged.\n\n* test(analyzers): assert each mapping visit without an expect message\n\njest/valid-expect rejects the message argument; each visit is now its\nown call and assertion. The test still fails on the second visit without\nthe fix and passes with it.\n\n* fix(analyzers): keep a skipped inactive-test result staged beside saved siblings\n\nAccept skips a result whose test or lab unit is inactive when no analysis\nexists yet for it. The persist-count check this PR added still counted\nthat result, so the whole save rolled back and its valid siblings could\nnot be accepted; before the check, the skipped row was deleted from\nstaging without a result.\n\nEach sample grouping now records the rows it skipped. Those rows are left\nout of the count and stay staged; the siblings are saved. A new\nintegration test accepts a group with one active and one inactive test:\nit failed with \"would remove 2 observations but persist 1\" before this\nchange.\n\n* fix(analyzers): honor the chosen specimen and the staged order when releasing held results\n\nReleasing an awaiting-specimen result trusted the submitted row for which\norder and test it belonged to, so a changed accession created the result\nunder that accession. Every kept row now takes its order, test, control\nflag and analyzer from its staged row; the reviewer supplies only the\naction, specimen choice, note and result. A row whose staged order differs\nfrom the rest of its grouping stays staged.\n\nThe chosen specimen was also lost in two ways. On an order with an entered\nsample, a new test''s result went to the test''s first sample type. Where a\ngrouping''s new analyses share one new specimen, only the first row''s\nchoice was read, and a choice another result could not use was dropped.\nThe entered-sample path now narrows each result to its own choice. In the\none-specimen paths a grouping with conflicting choices, or a choice a new\nanalysis''s test cannot use, waits for a decision; otherwise the grouping''s\nchoice is used whichever row carries it.\n\nThree new integration tests failed before this change (the result saved\non the first sample type, an order created under the submitted accession,\nand an incompatible grouping saved); a fourth confirms a choice every\nresult can use is still saved.\n\n* docs(analyzers): explain the shared specimen for results received together\n\nResults for an order with no sample entered yet share one new specimen,\nso a specimen choice must suit all of them or they stay staged.\n\n* fix(analyzers): keep the staged component, one specimen per grouping, and no empty orders\n\nThree gaps remained in releasing held results:\n\n- The staged identity restore left the client''s component, so a changed\n  componentId could bind a multiplex value to another component''s test\n  result. The component now comes from the staged row too.\n- persistAnalyzerResults puts every new analysis of a grouping on its one\n  sample item, on an entered order as well. The one-specimen check was\n  limited to orders without an entered sample, so two new tests with\n  different choices on an entered order both saved on one specimen. The\n  check now applies to every grouping.\n- A grouping whose rows were all skipped still inserted its order and\n  sample item with no result. Such groupings are no longer persisted;\n  their rows stay staged.\n\nThree new integration tests failed before this change: the forged\ncomponent''s test result was used, both conflicting analyses were saved,\nand an empty order was created.\n\n* docs(analyzers): the shared specimen applies to every order''s new tests\n\nNew tests added to an order from one analyzer message share one specimen\nwhether or not a sample was entered; the guide said only the latter.\n\n* fix(analyzers): keep a restored review action on the grouping''s visible row\n\nThe worklist shows a grouping''s accept, reject and delete checkboxes on\none representative row, preferring actionable rows. When a held row led\nits grouping, its actionable sibling represented it and carried the\nreviewer''s tick. Recovering the held row during the mapping visit made it\nthe representative on return, so the restored tick sat on a hidden row:\nthe visible checkbox was clear, yet Save still accepted the grouping.\n\nA restored grouping action now moves to the grouping''s current\nrepresentative, and the other rows get their server values back. A new\nworklist test recovers the held row during the visit and failed before\nthis change.\n\n* fix(analyzers): take every server-derived field of a released result from its staged row\n\nThe staged-identity restore covered order, test, component, control flag\nand analyzer, but the accept path also writes the analyzer''s completion\ntime, result type and significant digits from the submitted row. A\nchanged completeDate therefore landed on the clinical analysis.\n\nThe restore now covers every field the review page derives from the\nstaged row and the accept path reads: completion time, result type, test\nname and significant digits are taken from the staged row too. A new\nintegration test submits a different completion date and failed before\nthis change.\n\n* fix(analyzers): record a released analyzer result as an automatic analysis\n\nThe accept path sets the analysis type from the submitted row''s manual\nflag, which neither the review page nor the controller ever sets. A\nsubmitted manual: true therefore recorded an analyzer result as a manual\nanalysis. The staged-identity restore now clears the flag. A new\nintegration test submits manual: true and failed before this change.\n\n* fix(analyzers): give a new test its chosen specimen beside an existing analysis\n\nOn an order with an entered sample, a grouping that held a result for a\ntest with an existing analysis and a new test with a chosen specimen put\nthe new analysis on the existing analysis''s sample item: the first row\nset the shared sample item, so the new test neither found nor created\none of its chosen type.\n\nNew analyses now resolve their own sample item from their allowed types,\nreusing the grouping''s new item when it fits; an existing analysis''s\nitem is used for the grouping only when nothing new is added. A new\nintegration test failed before this change with the result on the\nexisting analysis''s specimen.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvH9WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMzgQACxYopwDrIqTCPjV/lC2w/mD\nS4JcIdTcO+qqq15JlbnkVTvFfV8v2NFscB4kKkwD4lfXP6fjgHl7Cy5K/ARf/u0v\nc3ylXHm91MfUnewTD1B+PzL7Hm7AemK+uHk6XhC0nmxctSrZk52rzEWL59AyHBuL\nB34bbj9s8GDvehjrjDW6RjhtEp3GO5yqnkdA9gfJ9enfX3IdFNnmZjsF4LhZxAs+\npxZ+fGSTUfL0tTQa0fGTTqexaSl032DuCDpC+ZcY2hue4lH23++0mE2zbWLCMVNn\nDke/iRtwkxVY+8OUZd+OT2oE5PAyBkYwrHG/U7MeiaqIbM5KzNdMvwMnzUBkRTtq\nGNRM7vynwekidMvMhjkGW/+Z6Sib4ZbFpovxc9OSY//ewn14BjxcRMj2A84VcR9h\nq8LGCCiHu7oNYNlAcY7Y95oDpqH8uRzrUeb48CZvsUBdXbxWL8LO2eGwRxAdLwHR\nzAvOFt7tErjsy2I22rvjvCICQMqjQHbHTivQcUiB3oYWPuRpcvZK40YEXZyNJiLN\nOmmP7gxvnlOk0RRp0ew3I3hj6HCH6ZHW8sSDmFHXkC7CSf5ZGOlZpLjnAzhrosL9\ntvTcehh1dF+TprK7jMcUqQquNPtZHzPXsQWDxhOwbKMc52sD1cMQjNh+QLa9pe+a\nHB5kznxn8P2h5T1c9PYb\n=Z11T\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T03:17:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/2aec1c10daa5ead02aa8f056aa6c93bcb9d34ea4","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDJhZWMxYzEwZGFhNWVhZDAyYWE4ZjA1NmFhNmM5M2JjYjlkMzRlYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/7d94adf63eaa7d9b4d6f740de91755fab777796b","sha":"7d94adf63eaa7d9b4d6f740de91755fab777796b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/7d94adf63eaa7d9b4d6f740de91755fab777796b"}],"sha":"2aec1c10daa5ead02aa8f056aa6c93bcb9d34ea4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/2aec1c10daa5ead02aa8f056aa6c93bcb9d34ea4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/7d94adf63eaa7d9b4d6f740de91755fab777796b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T03:17:42Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T03:17:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(analyzers): close 4332 review gaps and align local CI (#4470)\n\n* fix(analyzers): address setup review and local CI parity\n\n* fix(ci): include analyzer catalog init in shared image bake\n\n* fix(analyzers): complete CI compose startup and review checks\n\n* fix(analyzers): start proxy after harness upstreams\n\n* docs(analyzers): align remediation gates with current stack evidence\n\n* docs(analyzers): record verified stack workflows and remaining gates\n\n* fix(harness): let the video projects'' slowMo default apply again\n\nSince #4430 the parity runner exported PLAYWRIGHT_SLOWMO=0 whenever the\ncaller set none. The video projects read PLAYWRIGHT_SLOWMO || 500, and\n\"0\" is a set value, so every harness-demo-video recording ran at full\nspeed. No other project reads the variable.\n\nThe runner now passes an empty value by default, so the config''s 500 ms\napplies; an explicit PLAYWRIGHT_SLOWMO or --slowmo, including 0, still\nwins.\n\n* test(analyzers): present the GeneXpert and FluoroCycler workflows on video\n\nThe registered analyzer result stories recorded as bare test captures.\nThey now open with a chapter card, mark the connection and transport\ncheckpoints, and close on the verified clinical result, following the\nPlaywright README''s stakeholder evidence format.\n\nThe cards and pauses go through createDemoPresentation, so they run only\nin the video projects; every assertion and readiness wait is unchanged.\n\n* docs(playwright): point the evidence format at evidence-bundle\n\nThe stakeholder evidence format asks for MP4 packaging and a manifest but\ndid not say which tool produces them, so recordings were packaged by hand.\nIt now names the code-qa evidence-bundle skill, which also drafts the PR\ncomment and never commits media.\n\n* fix(harness): pull image-only services when building parity images\n\nharness-catalog-init runs a stock alpine image and has no build: entry,\nso docker compose build skipped it. On a machine without that image\ncached, --build then failed its own required-image preflight. Build mode\nnow pulls the services that cannot be built; a dry run of the parity\ncompose set pulls alpine:3.21 and skips every built image.\n\n* fix(ci): keep the Playwright blob report of a failed local E2E step\n\nrun-e2e-like-ci.sh exports CI=true, which makes Playwright write a blob\nreport instead of the HTML report. A failed step copied test-results and\nplaywright-report only, so its report was lost when the checkout was\ncleaned up or the next shard reused the directory. blob-report is now\ncopied with the other step artifacts.","tree":{"sha":"69849b98b261e5b17438951f3af28a3fab2aedbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/69849b98b261e5b17438951f3af28a3fab2aedbb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/7d94adf63eaa7d9b4d6f740de91755fab777796b","verification":{"payload":"tree 69849b98b261e5b17438951f3af28a3fab2aedbb\nparent 4d5171bfbe9cc73b087239fd514801e524871e09\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1790738262 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790738262 -0700\n\nfix(analyzers): close 4332 review gaps and align local CI (#4470)\n\n* fix(analyzers): address setup review and local CI parity\n\n* fix(ci): include analyzer catalog init in shared image bake\n\n* fix(analyzers): complete CI compose startup and review checks\n\n* fix(analyzers): start proxy after harness upstreams\n\n* docs(analyzers): align remediation gates with current stack evidence\n\n* docs(analyzers): record verified stack workflows and remaining gates\n\n* fix(harness): let the video projects'' slowMo default apply again\n\nSince #4430 the parity runner exported PLAYWRIGHT_SLOWMO=0 whenever the\ncaller set none. The video projects read PLAYWRIGHT_SLOWMO || 500, and\n\"0\" is a set value, so every harness-demo-video recording ran at full\nspeed. No other project reads the variable.\n\nThe runner now passes an empty value by default, so the config''s 500 ms\napplies; an explicit PLAYWRIGHT_SLOWMO or --slowmo, including 0, still\nwins.\n\n* test(analyzers): present the GeneXpert and FluoroCycler workflows on video\n\nThe registered analyzer result stories recorded as bare test captures.\nThey now open with a chapter card, mark the connection and transport\ncheckpoints, and close on the verified clinical result, following the\nPlaywright README''s stakeholder evidence format.\n\nThe cards and pauses go through createDemoPresentation, so they run only\nin the video projects; every assertion and readiness wait is unchanged.\n\n* docs(playwright): point the evidence format at evidence-bundle\n\nThe stakeholder evidence format asks for MP4 packaging and a manifest but\ndid not say which tool produces them, so recordings were packaged by hand.\nIt now names the code-qa evidence-bundle skill, which also drafts the PR\ncomment and never commits media.\n\n* fix(harness): pull image-only services when building parity images\n\nharness-catalog-init runs a stock alpine image and has no build: entry,\nso docker compose build skipped it. On a machine without that image\ncached, --build then failed its own required-image preflight. Build mode\nnow pulls the services that cannot be built; a dry run of the parity\ncompose set pulls alpine:3.21 and skips every built image.\n\n* fix(ci): keep the Playwright blob report of a failed local E2E step\n\nrun-e2e-like-ci.sh exports CI=true, which makes Playwright write a blob\nreport instead of the HTML report. A failed step copied test-results and\nplaywright-report only, so its report was lost when the checkout was\ncleaned up or the next shard reused the directory. blob-report is now\ncopied with the other step artifacts.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvH9WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmIAQAK+x9yfXIPOlC7+PHkgaIokM\nPSAgnYf3liBSBcml2mA82oe0g5sYVfDDUQktr4sT8QDMnS79ALlH4Nvk7K075ztp\n9VLfM6VSeFAXWawAdKX+/6VGv0gcLO6g8Yz20qVlOmzju1nrhgWGxEag2+yLFLbl\nVW6lbu01qF+VkX4qS4dx9iI7DZHhpmSBe2L9nR+yI+ACm7kjJaqivplnPX3S5RFs\nFvkRGuBjo5iRam+PDwejXFLoIGtUiEsnjFj2Qhw7EdTUc0z2i2bcIHrLOy5sM9zu\nnG59ua1/ABIrr8WAUM5Xw1huIX3ENxquoQiMIiHN3vPqlIjWcP7JPgxdyzL9wqGj\nXUYH7AGiMPybn+B1GAOXhDBFHlJaVG1CbSAK0E/FvjMlntNp8e5pgBl6aPSvElYN\nCHcF+QBH40UdYnOhgYffddHRfZ9LQvUPXf24/NulCbcRgalHE2wS4ywIewY/YtSf\n/fOwPdVK5Vw2R5LWEVK7WelMJBCp0sKE6c0aIv86e7bUru5S6ziyE6Epc/MBgZHG\nkg6LbLZ8l/cK1pFJREK1yaQjwb66v01GrswX+ZJ5ZipRgV0zOYql2iepQbDe9bFE\n9tp7x4MgplIuST5nHySD8L9D21ke9ePWEwbtaK3nZZ4oe94stcCp5rFV95ntUgDJ\n35TDgpXVCFUVxn/gHdGz\n=7XMO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T03:17:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/7d94adf63eaa7d9b4d6f740de91755fab777796b","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDdkOTRhZGY2M2VhYTdkOWI0ZDZmNzQwZGU5MTc1NWZhYjc3Nzc5NmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/4d5171bfbe9cc73b087239fd514801e524871e09","sha":"4d5171bfbe9cc73b087239fd514801e524871e09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/4d5171bfbe9cc73b087239fd514801e524871e09"}],"sha":"7d94adf63eaa7d9b4d6f740de91755fab777796b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/7d94adf63eaa7d9b4d6f740de91755fab777796b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29783151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/4d5171bfbe9cc73b087239fd514801e524871e09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T01:22:10Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T01:22:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(order): OGC-1389 keep the order when a sample-step request fails (#4483)\n\nA failed or slow request on the sample step no longer replaces the order screen: a failed tests list (server error, expired session, dropped connection) keeps what was entered, names the sample type and offers Retry, on Add Order and Modify Order (now behind the route error boundary). Searches typed before a list arrives show their results when it lands, including the site and requester search. Failed referral lists disable the referral with a Retry instead of crashing, and a test ticked after the referral was switched on is no longer left out. Tested with new vitest and Playwright specs that fail on develop, a live walk through order, results, validation and report, an independent review, and green CI including E2E.","tree":{"sha":"58494077287a2a346774665186e1cf7a82b00e86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/58494077287a2a346774665186e1cf7a82b00e86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/4d5171bfbe9cc73b087239fd514801e524871e09","verification":{"payload":"tree 58494077287a2a346774665186e1cf7a82b00e86\nparent 5eabda7ce4684d55d247354a332e3b7485735185\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1790731330 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790731330 +0300\n\nfix(order): OGC-1389 keep the order when a sample-step request fails (#4483)\n\nA failed or slow request on the sample step no longer replaces the order screen: a failed tests list (server error, expired session, dropped connection) keeps what was entered, names the sample type and offers Retry, on Add Order and Modify Order (now behind the route error boundary). Searches typed before a list arrives show their results when it lands, including the site and requester search. Failed referral lists disable the referral with a Retry instead of crashing, and a test ticked after the referral was switched on is no longer left out. Tested with new vitest 