ale/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelmale/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelmale","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/26502892164548bd204637c9c672882b39db1e99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T19:00:30Z","email":"samuelsmalek@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Male"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T19:00:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(eqa): mark only the deciding event of a sample as its verdict (OGC-1252) (#4464)\n\nAnalyst Competency collapses every event about one sample into a single\nfact, and a later triage verdict decides how that sample counts. The\nevidence table listed each event with its own flags, so a score and the\ntranscription dismissal answering it showed as two failures against a\nfailure count of one.\n\nThe evidence table now uses the same grouping as the count. The event that\ndecides a sample (the latest triage verdict, otherwise the score) carries its\nverdict, and every other event about that sample says it was decided by\ntriage or counted with the score. How samples count does not change.","tree":{"sha":"afee9cb7d67e55306f35e4fe5ee0fc75a0de778b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/afee9cb7d67e55306f35e4fe5ee0fc75a0de778b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/26502892164548bd204637c9c672882b39db1e99","verification":{"payload":"tree afee9cb7d67e55306f35e4fe5ee0fc75a0de778b\nparent 2a106d269acd620b5b19c1821f22f1572a81551f\nauthor Samuel Male <samuelsmalek@gmail.com> 1790708430 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790708430 +0300\n\nfix(eqa): mark only the deciding event of a sample as its verdict (OGC-1252) (#4464)\n\nAnalyst Competency collapses every event about one sample into a single\nfact, and a later triage verdict decides how that sample counts.