rs/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/08fcf5116d9b3a87c323cbf16e630cbf36749a5c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:35:32Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:35:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(order): OGC-1387 OGC-1388 order only what the sample step shows (#4480)\n\nAdd Order and Modify Order now carry exactly what the sample step shows: changing the sample type clears the test and panel search, and unticking, removing a panel, switching the referral off or choosing Select sample type empties the order instead of keeping stale tests, with Back no longer restoring them. The next order after Done starts empty, removing a sample keeps each sample''s own state, and each sample''s XML carries only its panels. Also fixed: the Modify Order patient name flash, the inverted rejected flag, and placeholder/key/label warnings on the case views and notebook forms. Tested with new vitest and Playwright suites (fail on develop) and a live walk of order entry, results, validation, the patient report, Modify Order, the case views and the notebook.","tree":{"sha":"a6f7f39c6d89a9a6f5af8f9c1bf58b2747dd7684","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/a6f7f39c6d89a9a6f5af8f9c1bf58b2747dd7684"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/08fcf5116d9b3a87c323cbf16e630cbf36749a5c","verification":{"payload":"tree a6f7f39c6d89a9a6f5af8f9c1bf58b2747dd7684\nparent 91db9a80a