","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/08fcf5116d9b3a87c323cbf16e630cbf36749a5c","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDA4ZmNmNTExNmQ5YjNhODdjMzIzY2JmMTZlNjMwY2JmMzY3NDlhNWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/91db9a80aa1c47679025f4762eb33bb136c3f6d4","sha":"91db9a80aa1c47679025f4762eb33bb136c3f6d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/91db9a80aa1c47679025f4762eb33bb136c3f6d4"}],"sha":"08fcf5116d9b3a87c323cbf16e630cbf36749a5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/08fcf5116d9b3a87c323cbf16e630cbf36749a5c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29783151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/91db9a80aa1c47679025f4762eb33bb136c3f6d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:30:27Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:30:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(concurrency): OGC-1376 refuse stale saves on Modify Order, the Test Catalog editor and Patient Management (#4478)\n\n* fix(concurrency): OGC-1376 refuse stale saves on Modify Order, the Test Catalog editor and Patient Management\n\nResults Entry refuses a save made from data someone has since changed; these\nthree screens did not. Modify Order and the test editor saved everything they\nshowed, silently undoing the other user''s change, and Patient Management\nanswered a raw 500 with Hibernate''s message and no word on screen.\n\nEach screen now sends the version it loaded, and a save against a newer one\nis refused before anything is written with a 409 that names who saved last\nand when, in the site''s date format. The screen shows a translatable message\nwith Refresh and disables Save until the user refreshes. The check, the 409\nbody and the who-and-when lookup are one shared StaleSaveGuard.\n\nModify Order forces the sample''s version forward on every save, so a\nrequester-only or tests-only save also invalidates older screens. The test\neditor and the patient form adopt the version each save returns, so saving\ntwice from the same screen is not refused; the patient form refused its own\nsecond save before this. An optimistic-lock failure that still slips through\non the patient save answers the same 409 instead of a 500.\n\n* fix(concurrency): OGC-1376 hand the new version back after activation and notebook saves\n\nTwo flows moved the version forward without giving it to the screen that\nholds the old one, so the user''s own next save was refused. Activating a test\nfrom Basic Info bumps the test''s version; the activation result now carries\nit and the editor adopts it. The notebook posts SampleEdit once per added\nsample from a form it loaded once; it now reloads that form after each save.","tree":{"sha":"7628d6672189e7ef0d7b92a5d4815b47643f43a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/7628d6672189e7ef0d7b92a5d4815b47643f43a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/91db9a80aa1c47679025f4762eb33bb136c3f6d4","verification":{"payload":"tree 7628d6672189e7ef0d7b92a5d4815b47643f43a0\nparent c6959aac7f60aa4af59cb0ac65b23006a5f8f2ad\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1790692227 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790692227 +0300\n\nfix(concurrency): OGC-1376 refuse stale saves on Modify Order, the Test Catalog editor and Patient Management (#4478)\n\n* fix(concurrency): OGC-1376 refuse stale saves on Modify Order, the Test Catalog editor and Patient Management\n\nResults Entry refuses a save made from data someone has since changed; these\nthree screens did not. Modify Order and the test editor saved everything they\nshowed, silently undoing the other user''s change, and Patient Management\nanswered a raw 500 with Hibernate''s message and no word on screen.\n\nEach screen now sends the version it loaded, and a save against a newer one\nis refused before anything is written with a 409 that names who saved last\nand when, in the site''s date format. The screen shows a translatable message\nwith Refresh and disables Save until the user refreshes. The check, the 409\nbody and the who-and-when lookup are one shared StaleSaveGuard.\n\nModify Order forces the sample''s version forward on every save, so a\nrequester-only or tests-only save also invalidates older screens. The test\neditor and the patient form adopt the version each save returns, so saving\ntwice from the same screen is not refused; the patient form refused its own\nsecond save before this. An optimistic-lock failure that still slips through\non the patient save answers the same 409 instead of a 500.\n\n* fix(concurrency): OGC-1376 hand the new version back after activation and notebook saves\n\nTwo flows moved the version forward without giving it to the screen that\nholds the old one, so the user''s own next save was refused. Activating a test\nfrom Basic Info bumps the test''s version; the activation result now carries\nit and the editor adopts it. The notebook posts SampleEdit once per added\nsample from a form it loaded once; it now reloads that form after each save.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu8uDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwb8QAJACoYPZ5ez9PgwVOmZiaKx+\n7Plt2iXEt6+UZVcbWTTW+AmavZwa4fcUGtOrx9MR10vr9AGBzhyuDxcXX7QZ+1Fp\nwVy/LuNg/C2pJR91YpBlkfBPxakyCGq5GMtXeCRAz5t5pj7Rc7WmndyLRGeCuPGW\n0/gRyBbz3rcDquOB8jOG2brZWrb/xx+rbdFCXnccT7gBs4XqnwKSr8oYiVo+No/F\n+Rt5C1oFnlG1G67YdyFepWToeaCtxk9z1kSq2grZY/5u8P6jJUZ2QFB7eFsy9VNw\n9N3Zl7nRm4b8vIxNLpJTvsoHciPxpJXO8K8dhuhQ1POOdshDnkhJPe4291gEWubs\n0IJdXvE4xXX3UIuE2SamZrqC+7lW/goV9bZK6ESqFDFaSJfCNRsz1jIAspNoqpJ6\ngWoVy8//AYdkajILZwfYnEsZQqMrrdXY4oNSVwzRboHJXJv6rwwVqzdIf7oV+LGK\nwM+MnoAclff7/yzQ9iFOrmxVVP3DUcygzr6XcmRa8EjhwA65LgNHJBkBpY3glFkX\nozmZkIqW9mtV7Ijm48RkzUe9Rf52VRuzl7fpwpWgbirIMffxovFHP2OI2iQS1F8Q\nQYBnkUUPajPocz65bXhDaCQduEyfmkEZWaHBWw8qArPVsh2idQxmrsRaYJ01etqL\nbBTl8AamQCIS7yYD3QJd\n=fLdX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T14:30:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/91db9a80aa1c47679025f4762eb33bb136c3f6d4","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDkxZGI5YTgwYWExYzQ3Njc5MDI1ZjQ3NjJlYjMzYmIxMzZjM2Y2ZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/c6959aac7f60aa4af59cb0ac65b23006a5f8f2ad","sha":"c6959aac7f60aa4af59cb0ac65b23006a5f8f2ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/c6959aac7f60aa4af59cb0ac65b23006a5f8f2ad"}],"sha":"91db9a80aa1c47679025f4762eb33bb136c3f6d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/91db9a80aa1c47679025f4762eb33bb136c3f6d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/c6959aac7f60aa4af59cb0ac65b23006a5f8f2ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:06:03Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:06:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): restore develop CI (Maven cache key, Carbon select race, WHONET isolation, proxy Host port) (#4471)\n\n* fix(ci): compute the backend Maven cache key after checkout\n\nThe Build + Test cache step ran before checkout, so hashFiles(''**/pom.xml'')\nmatched nothing and the key was always the constant \"Linux-maven-\". An exact\nkey hit never saves, so the cache stayed frozen at its 2026-09-26 snapshot and\nevery dependency added since (jasperreports-fonts in #4447) was fetched from\nMaven Central on every run. A 429 from Central on one of those fetches failed\ndevelop after #4332.\n\nCheckout now runs first, so the key follows the pom files and a new cache is\nsaved whenever dependencies change. The dedicated actions/cache step stays\ninstead of setup-java''s cache: maven because the Formatting job already writes\nthat key with a spotless-only repository; sharing it would pin Build + Test to\nthe small cache.\n\n* fix(e2e): choose Carbon select options through one helper that waits for the choice\n\nCarbon''s Dropdown, ComboBox and MultiSelect are built on downshift, which\nsince downshift 6 calls onChange from an effect after the click has\nrendered (5.2.1 called it inside the click). The Vite migration (#3312)\nmoved Carbon 1.15 to 1.104 and downshift 5.2.1 to 9.0.10, so every\nspec that clicked an option and moved straight on started racing the\napplication. develop failed on one of them: custom-data-export''s\ndetailedLayout typed into the field picker before the CSV layout change\nreached the builder, the layout change then remounted the picker empty,\nand the next click waited for a button that never appeared.\n\nplaywright/helpers/carbon-select.ts adds chooseCarbonOption (Dropdown,\nComboBox) and tickCarbonMultiSelectOption (MultiSelect,\nFilterableMultiSelect). Each opens the control, picks from that control''s\nown listbox (aria-controls), and returns once the control shows the\nchoice: the button text or input value, or the option''s aria-selected.\nFor a controlled component that is the point where onChange has run.\nEvery component behind the converted call sites is controlled.\n\nConverted: custom-data-export (detailedLayout, configuredReport),\nogc-479 reporting MVP (same layout race), ogc-1054 m2 result mapping,\nstorage-dispose reason and method, capa-register status (its second\nfilter could previously pass on the first filter''s rows), order dashboard\nstatus filter, the four test-catalog copy pickers, the multicomponent\nresult multi-select, and selectWhonetFilterOption. Sites that already\nassert the application''s outcome (ogc-307 priority, storage-assign\ndevice cascade) are unchanged. The Playwright guide gains the rule.\n\n* fix(e2e): scope the WHONET M4 export demo to its own seeded case\n\nThe M4 demo previewed every WHONET-exportable isolate on the seed''s date\nand asserted Generate CSV is disabled because its own case has mapping\ngaps. The preview enables generation whenever any row is exportable, so\nthe assertion held only when no other spec had seeded exportable data on\nthat date. microbiology-whonet-export and\nmicrobiology-whonet-worklist-handoff do, and in one database (the local\nparity runner, or any shard that runs them first) their mapped rows made\nthe preview generatable and the demo failed. CI passed only because its\ntwo shards happened to give those specs a different database.\n\nBoth tests now filter the export to the seed''s own specimen type, the\nsame scoping the R9 filters demo already uses. Verified on a fresh\nparity database with the two seeding specs run first: failed before\n(toBeDisabled at the preview step), passes after.\n\n* fix(proxy): keep the request''s port in the Host header sent upstream\n\nnginx''s $host drops the port, so a stack served on any port other than\n443 received Host: localhost and built its login redirect as\nhttps://localhost/api/OpenELIS-Global/LoginPage. The browser followed it\nto whatever owns port 443. On the per-worktree CI-parity stacks, which\nrun on ephemeral ports, that is a different OpenELIS instance: Cypress\nlogins spun forever and the analyzer-harness login readiness wait timed\nout, although each stack''s own OpenELIS was up. $http_host forwards the\nHost the client sent, port included. On port 443 browsers omit the port,\nso standard deployments and CI see no change.\n\nThe hunks are identical to #4470''s change to this file, so the two\nmerge cleanly in either order; nginx.conf.template already uses\n$http_host.\n\n* fix(harness): start the analyzer-harness proxy only after OpenELIS is healthy\n\nThe harness proxy had no depends_on, so on a slow start nginx came up\nbefore oe.openelis.org was resolvable, exited with\n\"[emerg] host not found in upstream \\\"oe.openelis.org\\\"\", and was\nrestarted. The CI-parity stacks publish ephemeral host ports, and a\nrestarted container can be given a new one: in one run the runner read\nthe proxy as 34924 while the restarted proxy listened on 34934, so the\nlogin readiness wait probed a dead port for its full 240 s although\nOpenELIS was up. The same lane passed or failed depending on start order.\n\nThe proxy now waits for certs to complete, the frontend to start and\nOpenELIS to be healthy (it has /healthcheck.sh); fhir and the bridge wait\nfor certs. These hunks are identical to #4470''s ordering changes in this\nfile; its harness-catalog-init dependency for OpenELIS stays in #4470.\n\n* fix(harness): run the harness certs container once so its dependents start\n\nThe previous commit made fhir, the bridge and the proxy wait for certs\nwith service_completed_successfully, but build.docker-compose.yml gives\ncerts restart: always. It exited 0, was restarted, and never stayed\ncompleted, so compose up waited on it indefinitely and the harness lane\nhung before its readiness wait. The harness base now overrides certs to\nrestart: \"no\", which is the line #4470 adds for the same dependency.\nWith it, certs exits, the proxy starts after OpenELIS is healthy, and\nlogin readiness and the analyzer connection gate pass.\n\n#4470 also adds harness-catalog-init directly above certs, so merging\nthe two may need that adjacent block resolved by hand.","tree":{"sha":"b96ed1b1d8f301356787b61935287c48a2682829","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/b96ed1b1d8f301356787b61935287c48a2682829"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/c6959aac7f60aa4af59cb0ac65b23006a5f8f2ad","verification":{"payload":"tree b96ed1b1d8f301356787b61935287c48a2682829\nparent 57092119cdf2deafe0e1b994cbfaeacc7c32ea1c\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1790690763 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790690763 -0700\n\nfix(ci): restore develop CI (Maven cache key, Carbon select race, WHONET isolation, proxy Host port) (#4471)\n\n* fix(ci): compute the backend Maven cache key after checkout\n\nThe Build + Test cache step ran before checkout, so hashFiles(''**/pom.xml'')\nmatched nothing and the key was always the constant \"Linux-maven-\". An exact\nkey hit never saves, so the cache stayed frozen at its 2026-09-26 snapshot and\nevery dependency added since (jasperreports-fonts in #4447) was fetched from\nMaven Central on every run. A 429 from Central on one of those fetches failed\ndevelop after #4332.\n\nCheckout now runs first, so the key follows the pom files and a new cache is\nsaved whenever dependencies change. The dedicated actions/cache step stays\ninstead of setup-java''s cache: maven because the Formatting job already writes\nthat key with a spotless-only repository; sharing it would pin Build + Test to\nthe small cache.\n\n* fix(e2e): choose Carbon select options through one helper that waits for the choice\n\nCarbon''s Dropdown, ComboBox and MultiSelect are built on downshift, which\nsince downshift 6 calls onChange from an effect after the click has\nrendered (5.2.1 called it inside the click). The Vite migration (#3312)\nmoved Carbon 1.15 to 1.104 and downshift 5.2.1 to 9.0.10, so every\nspec that clicked an option and moved straight on started racing the\napplication. develop failed on one of them: custom-data-export''s\ndetailedLayout typed into the field picker before the CSV layout change\nreached the builder, the layout change then remounted the picker empty,\nand the next click waited for a button that never appeared.\n\nplaywright/helpers/carbon-select.ts adds chooseCarbonOption (Dropdown,\nComboBox) and tickCarbonMultiSelectOption (MultiSelect,\nFilterableMultiSelect). Each opens the control, picks from that control''s\nown listbox (aria-controls), and returns once the control shows the\nchoice: the button text or input value, or the option''s aria-selected.\nFor a controlled component that is the point where onChange has run.\nEvery component behind the converted call sites is controlled.\n\nConverted: custom-data-export (detailedLayout, configuredReport),\nogc-479 reporting MVP (same layout race), ogc-1054 m2 result mapping,\nstorage-dispose reason and method, capa-register status (its second\nfilter could previously pass on the first filter''s rows), order dashboard\nstatus filter, the four test-catalog copy pickers, the multicomponent\nresult multi-select, and selectWhonetFilterOption. Sites that already\nassert the application''s outcome (ogc-307 priority, storage-assign\ndevice cascade) are unchanged. The Playwright guide gains the rule.\n\n* fix(e2e): scope the WHONET M4 export demo to its own seeded case\n\nThe M4 demo previewed every WHONET-exportable isolate on the seed''s date\nand asserted Generate CSV is disabled because its own case has mapping\ngaps. The preview enables generation whenever any row is exportable, so\nthe assertion held only when no other spec had seeded exportable data on\nthat date. microbiology-whonet-export and\nmicrobiology-whonet-worklist-handoff do, and in one database (the local\nparity runner, or any shard that runs them first) their mapped rows made\nthe preview generatable and the demo failed. CI passed only because its\ntwo shards happened to give those specs a different database.\n\nBoth tests now filter the export to the seed''s own specimen type, the\nsame scoping the R9 filters demo already uses. Verified on a fresh\nparity database with the two seeding specs run first: failed before\n(toBeDisabled at the preview step), passes after.\n\n* fix(proxy): keep the request''s port in the Host header sent upstream\n\nnginx''s $host drops the port, so a stack served on any port other than\n443 received Host: localhost and built its login redirect as\nhttps://localhost/api/OpenELIS-Global/LoginPage. The browser followed it\nto whatever owns port 443. On the per-worktree CI-parity stacks, which\nrun on ephemeral ports, that is a different OpenELIS instance: Cypress\nlogins spun forever and the analyzer-harness login readiness wait timed\nout, although each stack''s own OpenELIS was up. $http_host forwards the\nHost the client sent, port included. On port 443 browsers omit the port,\nso standard deployments and CI see no change.\n\nThe hunks are identical to #4470''s change to this file, so the two\nmerge cleanly in either order; nginx.conf.template already uses\n$http_host.\n\n* fix(harness): start the analyzer-harness proxy only after OpenELIS is healthy\n\nThe harness proxy had no depends_on, so on a slow start nginx came up\nbefore oe.openelis.org was resolvable, exited with\n\"[emerg] host not found in upstream \\\"oe.openelis.org\\\"\", and was\nrestarted. The CI-parity stacks publish ephemeral host ports, and a\nrestarted container can be given a new one: in one run the runner read\nthe proxy as 34924 while the restarted proxy listened on 34934, so the\nlogin readiness wait probed a dead port for its full 240 s although\nOpenELIS was up. The same lane passed or failed depending on start order.\n\nThe proxy now waits for certs to complete, the frontend to start and\nOpenELIS to be healthy (it has /healthcheck.sh); fhir and the bridge wait\nfor certs. These hunks are identical to #4470''s ordering changes in this\nfile; its harness-catalog-init dependency for OpenELIS stays in #4470.\n\n* fix(harness): run the harness certs container once so its dependents start\n\nThe previous commit made fhir, the bridge and the proxy wait for certs\nwith service_completed_successfully, but build.docker-compose.yml gives\ncerts restart: always. It exited 0, was restarted, and never stayed\ncompleted, so compose up waited on it indefinitely and the harness lane\nhung before its readiness wait. The harness base now overrides certs to\nrestart: \"no\", which is the line #4470 adds for the same dependency.\nWith it, certs exits, the proxy starts after OpenELIS is healthy, and\nlogin readiness and the analyzer connection gate pass.\n\n#4470 also adds harness-catalog-init directly above certs, so merging\nthe two may need that adjacent block resolved by hand.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu8XLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/Q4QACVHLlE5fl2+527/c7tIOaFn\nOlGLf48nKvzEXNCBlPDRqpRTEtFZvCK1cAap/sVKGolFBq9g4dEW02SMklL2iJyV\nmfMFoA8uBQ05ebVWuhijxEcLBt+Vz64UltW530BBjrCWBOHRpm+oUUapv0VH1v7q\nfk5fnOjDKCzRKwEgqrxioiFZpZcfhDYpnpo3hM1z1WP96W1C89AZK5SPpJnuW+bj\nFJ3NemHj