"https://api.github.com/users/samuelmale","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/e900c8104f096bc84f1ac789f47940d0080e18bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:15:25Z","email":"samuelsmalek@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Male"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:15:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(eqa): stop giving away blinded in-house orders on the Results page (OGC-1249) (#4457)\n\nA blinded in-house panel is distributed as ordinary orders so the analyst\nrunning it cannot tell proficiency material from patient work. The Results\npage gave those orders away twice: the row carried the EQA badge, and\nentering a critical value raised the clinician callback prompt for a sample\nthat has no patient.\n\nResult rows now say whether their scheme is in-house, and the badge is left\noff those rows. EQA samples are left out of the needs-callback list, since\nthere is nobody to call back for any EQA material. The EQA flag itself is\nunchanged, so result routing and the callback exclusion keep working.","tree":{"sha":"6ab0354138724f98935a7724bfbf44c743f8e041","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/6ab0354138724f98935a7724bfbf44c743f8e041"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/e900c8104f096bc84f1ac789f47940d0080e18bf","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ab0354138724f98935a7724bfbf44c743f8e041\nparent 7561a95f2cffb7ae5011b6bb714638dea953792a\nauthor Samuel Male <samuelsmalek@gmail.com> 1790676925 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790676925 +0300\n\nfix(eqa): stop giving away blinded in-house orders on the Results page (OGC-1249) (#4457)\n\nA blinded in-house panel is distributed as ordinary orders so the analyst\nrunning it cannot tell proficiency material from patient work. The Results\npage gave those orders away twice: the row carried the EQA badge, and\nentering a critical value raised the clinician callback prompt for a sample\nthat has no patient.\n\nResult rows now say whether their scheme is in-house, and the badge is left\noff those rows. EQA samples are left out of the needs-callback list, since\nthere is nobody to call back for any EQA material. The EQA flag itself is\nunchanged, so result routing and the callback exclusion keep working.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu4+9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2CUQAAxSncmYtXBlKQAkU0wxChiK\nhHICshiBj8EM3afLp2PHk7ysxJ1b7ygifRW6hswpwrnB8Ag/aUpUCtZ8amLW83Wp\nErr8p5c1LrEG7fOZqJ3j4of0AnAVePCTmEXXi44I38gZeUXCJXf7AZvZ3qEEIefa\n5HxUDNcm1cGFuMQ/rtihu2XzN/Fj7lczSvaezX8wnAFl6Z9p5cvDntMT0bI11fC9\nfmmHCHtkknu84d4uuCPmH6F1jkr+EqkoJ3fM1yTFQWP5tzbHMQT/eQ5WqXmtbX5c\nEYnWK1hHW74cdG5FgvtaAu6yGzt04fNFtE5InMQx73qthHDVkkW/FlBt/sFZoLWa\n3MmI+oJ6UKZz8HEdu2+1qw1fX5tbGWzWO+4FTKDb+rYnrdIwHCPp/hkw9B8sbZlj\noSOrWzpVFuyaFIpZuOExIuzMDZmmR3T/75csBhA/UoM77qhNnpofSFCxR1L17qFJ\nHq4ETz4/sZ36tsJA4mhzpDW8IKy7Lkh/uau1o7uGjAGRR84SloTcaEahMGobLlRo\nmM8Oq7Qy9IbGjva/v4dZKq8504flCew6+j+061mgcFnbCsrGg5FwrWMrYP7GoOcg\nJA9Rn7095b2k5iFV71kkpUFHJ2UsNgDE0zI0k066sejl1+ZBjz8MUATZgdtOzhrO\nDMgdwQa8Ylgxpx3CHiic\n=2Wnk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T10:15:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/e900c8104f096bc84f1ac789f47940d0080e18bf","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKGU5MDBjODEwNGYwOTZiYzg0ZjFhYzc4OWY0Nzk0MGQwMDgwZTE4YmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/7561a95f2cffb7ae5011b6bb714638dea953792a","sha":"7561a95f2cffb7ae5011b6bb714638dea953792a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/7561a95f2cffb7ae5011b6bb714638dea953792a"}],"sha":"e900c8104f096bc84f1ac789f47940d0080e18bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/e900c8104f096bc84f1ac789f47940d0080e18bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26084581?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelmale/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelmale/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelmale/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelmale/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelmale","id":26084581,"login":"samuelmale","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2MDg0NTgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelmale/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelmale/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelmale/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelmale/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelmale/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelmale","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/7561a95f2cffb7ae5011b6bb714638dea953792a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:09:51Z","email":"samuelsmalek@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Male"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:09:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(reports): return the CSV export connection on every path (OGC-1360) (#4453)\n\nExport Routine CSV opened a Hibernate session per run and never closed it,\nso each run kept one pooled connection. The base CSV builder, used by the\nRejection Report, began a thread-bound transaction and never ended it,\nleaving a connection idle in transaction. With a pool of 20 and an\nunlimited wait, about twenty runs hung the whole application.\n\nBoth builders now own their session and close it with the result set, or\nat once when the query fails. The two runReport() bases close it in a\nfinally block.\n\nThe datasource also gets a safety net: a 30 second borrow wait instead of\nwaiting forever, and abandoned-connection removal with logging, so a\nfuture leak fails requests and names its caller instead of hanging.","tree":{"sha":"77d64d5ff3a5f58b0cc4f55394b6205017919e22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/77d64d5ff3a5f58b0cc4f55394b6205017919e22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/7561a95f2cffb7ae5011b6bb714638dea953792a","verification":{"payload":"tree 77d64d5ff3a5f58b0cc4f55394b6205017919e22\nparent 3ce6929607baf56b5db22c580e5b696a6719186b\nauthor Samuel Male <samuelsmalek@gmail.com> 1790676591 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790676591 +0300\n\nfix(reports): return the CSV export connection on every path (OGC-1360) (#4453)\n\nExport Routine CSV opened a Hibernate session per run and never closed it,\nso each run kept one pooled connection. The base CSV builder, used by the\nRejection Report, began a thread-bound transaction and never ended it,\nleaving a connection idle in transaction. With a pool of 20 and an\nunlimited wait, about twenty runs hung the whole application.\n\nBoth builders now own their session and close it with the result set, or\nat once when the query fails. The two runReport() bases close it in a\nfinally block.\n\nThe datasource also gets a safety net: a 30 second borrow wait instead of\nwaiting forever, and abandoned-connection removal with logging, so a\nfuture leak fails requests and names its caller instead of hanging.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu45vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX8MQAE9JtbBQt6Ag1oFEZbtIhWbj\ng/8Y9ckDwEml3p1aMC/uUfZODvnlASzKm3Aw8W1G5Bn0X9by9Uvm43wiw9Un5akC\n0O1+XIRvW9ftzQ4PNp/0q/7GAe22cLhGkx4pHGzFRvQ+R9tUXAnl4hmM6GqTyWGO\nmVrUJ0q8UseJDVfcRr6rJPFpJ3eBggy4BnPskGNO6epgarK9zEW2J8JskifOxfM2\nRmNMNrg9TmgDEPFX67e8yJdw4rOSUMj/aaGl61zfVujdKv5Z1WeKHWysW7jjOTgL\nWcoAJ2vCU7+O91agaQ30w9pUiCRWOumfvQ1AdChTlo5hmUJOJ9K4H17YhBTiLLkm\n3/qTV6TF4t6rnfmz2o506gQmn8RZpnsFUbiSNjvHX6x/5FC/LXLa+uhhWkKne/08\npGEJgF4F8VxedX/ElWgflK2UVNRk6Wx8oTESaBG19FzaAlSpoiQnWJg5T8GpudH5\nL5y17WDqE9BAfmP57iLhHCQ14gCnEapB51r9SRs1UMYwGNcYpKZ9bCk8Coh+6yqj\n10AXEqXgn3gpFxfFNbmxc0tVwhg+3H6vRrIpIT0F9qepv0Etj/5uqCC1oMeP/JvO\ndzwLZiflP5GRmvfWw3rQuF99AiAHHIoQbdO42uDr2RqfFWyx5Q8HA8QfSszfoDwq\nQPiCHOkZPg/5oU29J4Oj\n=coHk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T10:09:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/us