r_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mozzy11","id":29783151,"login":"mozzy11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NzgzMTUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozzy11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/238b2cbfc87bb7f12c116eaedbf09c8eefb268b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T08:13:37Z","email":"mozzymutesa@gmail.com","name":"Mutesasira Moses"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T08:13:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(order): OGC-1366 change an order''s priority back to Routine on Modify Order (#4469)\n\nThe priority selects sent the labels Routine and Timed instead of the OrderPriority codes, so SampleEdit answered 400. Both selects now send the codes with the existing translated sample.priority labels, and an unreadable request body answers 400 with a translatable messageKey that Modify Order shows.\n\nAlso fixes, found walking the Modify Order save: every save cloned the referring site (the id now wins); a picked requester was copied instead of linked; a blank requester created an empty provider and clearing one now unlinks it; requester names follow REQUESTER_REQUIRED as in order entry; a priority change is audited against the state read before the edit.\n\nUnblocks testing deploys: the publish gate waits up to two hours for the backend checkpoint, and qa-057 is skipped (precondition only, checksum unchanged) when stored alerts use types it would drop; qa-084 installs the full union.","tree":{"sha":"f6798002999de716efeef3b32cb4bb51a493ec6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/f6798002999de716efeef3b32cb4bb51a493ec6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/238b2cbfc87bb7f12c116eaedbf09c8eefb268b9","verification":{"payload":"tree f6798002999de716efeef3b32cb4bb51a493ec6d\nparent 46fd82b9e6763c999effbdf92a038e1034e3f052\nauthor Mutesasira Moses <mozzymutesa@gmail.com> 1790669617 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790669617 +0300\n\nfix(order): OGC-1366 change an order''s priority back to Routine on Modify Order (#4469)\n\nThe priority selects sent the labels Routine and Timed instead of the OrderPriority codes, so SampleEdit answered 400. Both selects now send the codes with the existing translated sample.priority labels, and an unreadable request body answers 400 with a translatable messageKey that Modify Order shows.\n\nAlso fixes, found walking the Modify Order save: every save cloned the referring site (the id now wins); a picked requester was copied instead of linked; a blank requester created an empty provider and clearing one now unlinks it; requester names follow REQUESTER_REQUIRED as in order entry; a priority change is audited against the state read before the edit.\n\nUnblocks testing deploys: the publish gate waits up to two hours for the backend checkpoint, and qa-057 is skipped (precondition only, checksum unchanged) when stored alerts use types it would drop; qa-084 installs the full union.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu3MxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAADkQAAXUGzLDpbPzwRHaJ2J07LNx\n6Vu/I62qB9qTeRdLhtAwY/mASFgxjFq0fzePidGb55jYBO/MJHrSQDN69v+QKgbn\n8EdYw4q1ttTzmKb/SROPszPNK9UPaTRniwPbJiKNN8BHeVUWZSMiWugYhs9MXZuq\ntoMYDzuohHsSm/9V2RDe9ez3d2GDRXK5mns2Ht9sM+Ie6+2G0y41Dv7iNc144eF+\nS24gjypKuct2wvi0f8DoXav9Mgs6h0LzvGzUcS2Hba1pF7H97f+FlIidXctK0991\npBBRm8jFz/uyE2SquvwTkX+98H0RmOB6sx2Y5UngDyHXoeEy+Bj7DR/27+7ofIFU\nm7HyR1DA0yN/CESlu6Uu+pjPFwWkLNReA3HQ2KcbeNzrb+hAa5DfNSYIc+fMRARH\nT2bNUjotuij72hTFn105i0IkD1+BHZlBtg9lwUNe3iQm6KT3rr7oS+9nPT1R7m0G\nzzzUpUO1EBegi27HQfWkJBJ5e2MJ60KF65ipurE7cMdeiBlm8eDL4cs3vsj40cHZ\nBSMSErJoJxtl+nbSEtzpA+UT8Oas4KtoMQJiQu9sIjTvI7WTFNk0QzuPX4Qqffit\nPwuBn7LE5hXobf9bwct6RMd3Wz83J1Rtx2DuwoNNba2sZOmxPyTsJpx5f8XxIa5A\nP9bIoKgsT4MkqEie9ELt\n=1SQi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T08:13:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/238b2cbfc87bb7f12c116eaedbf09c8eefb268b9","node_id":"C_kwDOCePx2toAKDIzOGIyY2JmYzg3YmI3ZjEyYzExNmVhZWRiZjA5YzhlZWZiMjY4Yjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/46fd82b9e6763c999effbdf92a038e1034e3f052","sha":"46fd82b9e6763c999effbdf92a038e1034e3f052","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/46fd82b9e6763c999effbdf92a038e1034e3f052"}],"sha":"238b2cbfc87bb7f12c116eaedbf09c8eefb268b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/238b2cbfc87bb7f12c116eaedbf09c8eefb268b9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22994890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HerbertYiga/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HerbertYiga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HerbertYiga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HerbertYiga/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/HerbertYiga","id":22994890,"login":"HerbertYiga","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTk0ODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HerbertYiga/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HerbertYiga/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HerbertYiga/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HerbertYiga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HerbertYiga/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HerbertYiga","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/46fd82b9e6763c999effbdf92a038e1034e3f052/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T06:04:58Z","email":"herbertyiga24@gmail.com","name":"HerbertYiga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T06:04:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(sample-type): stop silently discarding description on Add sample type (#4466)\n\n* fix(sample-type): stop silently discarding description on Add sample type\n\nAdmin Management → Test catalogue management → Manage sample types → Add\nsample type: the form has a Description TextArea, but the create payload\nnever included its value. The backend then filled type_of_sample.description\nwith the sample type''s English name, so the description column always came\nback looking like the name. Now the frontend sends the description, the\nform bean accepts it (@NotBlank + @SafeHtml), and the controller persists\nit in place of the name-copy.\n\nAlso drops two name-fallbacks on the frontend that masked the same class\nof bug on the editor: refreshSampleTypes no longer substitutes name for\nan empty description on rehydrate, and the edit-save payload no longer\nfalls back to name when description is cleared.\n\nNote: name-uniqueness (nameInUse, conflictingField) still compares against\ntype_of_sample.description. Existing admins who create both fields with\nthe same text keep the same dedupe behavior; the integration tests are\nupdated to send description alongside the name, preserving that invariant.\n\n* fix(sample-type): keep create working without a description; refuse a taken description on its field\n\n@NotBlank on SampleTypeCreateForm.description made every create that\npredates the field fail: the legacy SampleTypeCreate screen, the JSP\ncreate page, and API callers (the ogc-1234 Playwright spec got 400 where\nit expected 200). Under some MockMvc setups the constraint does not fire\nat all and createTypeOfSample NPE''d on description.trim(). The description\nis now optional and falls back to the English name, so those callers keep\ntheir old behaviour while the editor''s typed description is stored.\n\nA description that another sample type in the domain already has was\nrefused as a duplicate name (409 on sampleTypeEnglishName, \"A sample type\nnamed X already exists\"). The create now checks conflictingField and\nanswers 409 on the description field, and the editor marks that field.\n\nThe initial list load still substituted the name, then \"Sample type from\ndatabase\", for an empty description; it now shows none, matching refresh.\n\nTests: the existing integration tests go back to the pre-description\npayload so they cover the legacy callers; new integration tests guard the\nstored description (fails with the fix reverted), the no-description\ncreate, and the description conflict; new Vitest cases cover the create\npayload, the description 409 and the list mapping.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: HerbertYiga <herbertyiga24@egmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu>","tree":{"sha":"4f2c50f487ccbeac9afe059154150fa00df7e9b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/4f2c50f487ccbeac9afe059154150fa00df7e9b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/46fd82b9e6763c999effbdf92a038e1034e3f052","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f2c50f487ccbeac9afe059154150fa00df7e9b8\nparent e0c98726bab7e7f6258bbf07fa7d8173335da20c\nauthor HerbertYiga <herbertyiga24@gmail.com> 1790661898 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790661898 -0700\n\nfix(sample-type): stop silently discarding description on Add sample type (#4466)\n\n* fix(sample-type): stop silently discarding description on Add sample type\n\nAdmin Management → Test catalogue management → Manage sample types → Add\nsample type: the form has a Description TextArea, but the create payload\nnever included its value. The backend then filled type_of_sample.description\nwith the sample type''s English name, so the description column always came\nback looking like the name. Now the frontend sends the description, the\nform bean accepts it (@NotBlank + @SafeHtml), and the controller persists\nit in place of the name-copy.\n\nAlso drops two name-fallbacks on the frontend that masked the same class\nof bug on the editor: refreshSampleTypes no longer substitutes name for\nan empty description on rehydrate, and the edit-save payload no longer\nfalls back to name when description is cleared.\n\nNote: name-uniqueness (nameInUse, conflictingField) still compares against\ntype_of_sample.description. Existing admins who create both fields with\nthe same text keep the same dedupe behavior; the integration tests are\nupdated to send description alongside the name, preserving that invariant.\n\n* fix(sample-type): keep create working without a description; refuse a taken description on its field\n\n@NotBlank on SampleTypeCreateForm.description made every create that\npredates the field fail: the legacy SampleTypeCreate screen, the JSP\ncreate page, and API callers (the ogc-1234 Playwright spec got 400 where\nit expected 200). Under some MockMvc setups the constraint does not fire\nat all and createTypeOfSample NPE''d on description.trim(). The description\nis now optional and falls back to the English name, so those callers keep\ntheir old behaviour while the editor''s typed description is stored.\n\nA description that another sample type in the domain already has was\nrefused as a duplicate name (409 on sampleTypeEnglishName, \"A sample type\nnamed X already exists\"). The create now checks conflictingField and\nanswers 409 on the description field, and the editor marks that field.\n\nThe initial list load still substituted the name, then \"Sample type from\ndatabase\", for an empty description; it now shows none, matching refresh.\n\nTests: the existing integration tests go back to the pre-description\npayload so they cover the legacy callers; new integration tests guard the\nstored description (fails with the fix reverted), the no-description\ncreate, and the description conflict; new Vitest cases cover the create\npayload, the description 409 and the list mapping.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: HerbertYiga <herbertyiga24@egmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu1UKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMTwQAIz+KCmu0DFUKbZUfolvdGg5\nSV3U+CEq2vylBSDQl2UssFi0lkgdZZflOyvSKffUT+/lTCpn52aV3m760ghStckb\nJUKoWvNF7Hfy0OH5ciJz4TeWwReIkcjA+llPXGIUsPXw7ITouXFh2nZ+49OXN++v\nm6fqPs7QvEvzsCa1jXz1OMLBj+yq3UXjc+QOMoXGt95KS8w1AAfQd61hbwIX9xG7\n9vmbzXP/RTTRmqW2ilCLFmLQFXiAUoyD7l8cAxUJlCRaWYJl0d5Zx7Nbztllj2mO\n+qK8uZrYfSFfBu8FJl7GW9chz1cARiJNHJmDC3OjLoOuPH51N5Daii0WGKvGkWTy\nS/+wup/9wy3xcn8GR1rLFf5LYW1CUJ5fHERZYHl2cogJiVTy+/Vu2xMZv2oqBUA7\nnLz/vvPwBt3sjg9528zcHmERzi1zdQM2B9NXEqFtzbXeCjepaiuEBAZanOFY4SSH\neo4oMs1DQFFROcLIdwSgyXjd94ClNVTlcILdEPOZzL3fnO19cKGnza