"parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commit/ea65d2e43024a7cded8435afe5a86ee268769e97","sha":"ea65d2e43024a7cded8435afe5a86ee268769e97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/ea65d2e43024a7cded8435afe5a86ee268769e97"}],"sha":"889166b649236c0516f1bfc663f06bb5ad2f556a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/889166b649236c0516f1bfc663f06bb5ad2f556a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/711826?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pmanko","id":711826,"login":"pmanko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTgyNg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pmanko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/commits/ea65d2e43024a7cded8435afe5a86ee268769e97/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T18:55:29Z","email":"pmanko@uw.edu","name":"Piotr Mankowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T18:55:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): restore develop formatting and Transifex push (#4462)\n\n* fix(ci): restore develop formatting and surface Transifex upload errors\n\nCLAUDE.md: apply the Prettier rewrap that Backend / Formatting requires.\n#4382 last ran CI before the Formatting job existed (#4446), so the\nparagraph merged unchecked.\n\ntx-push: run `tx push --silent`. Without a TTY the CLI truncates every\nmessage to 78 characters, which cut off the reason Transifex rejects\nen.json since #4409. In silent mode errors print untruncated.\n\n* fix(i18n): make the #4409 plural strings uploadable to Transifex\n\nTransifex parses any value that starts with `{var, plural,` as a single\npluralized entry and rejected en.json on:\n\n  parse_error: Invalid format of pluralized entry with key:\n  \"validation\\.qcHold\\.withheld\"\n\nvalidation.qcHold.withheld and eqa.prep.needExplained both open with a\nplural and contain further plurals.\n\n- validation.qcHold.withheld: one whole-sentence plural. The key is not\n  referenced by any code, so nothing renders differently.\n- eqa.prep.needExplained: four independent counts cannot share one\n  plural, so the string now starts with \"Aliquots needed:\". The\n  PrepWorkbench default message and its test follow.\n\nValidation / i18n now runs check-transifex-plurals.py on PRs that touch\nthe language files, so a string like these fails before merge instead\nof breaking the post-merge Transifex push.\n\n* chore(i18n): drop the Transifex plural pre-check\n\nThe failure has happened once; the --silent push now names the rejected\nkey, which is enough to diagnose a recurrence. Revisit a PR-time check if\nit happens again.","tree":{"sha":"f39e3af8784ba90e1d65d5bf7d88012338cc757b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/trees/f39e3af8784ba90e1d65d5bf7d88012338cc757b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2/git/commits/ea65d2e43024a7cded8435afe5a86ee268769e97","verification":{"payload":"tree f39e3af8784ba90e1d65d5bf7d88012338cc757b\nparent e05d9ed2dc61e71a235fd4b2d65e5a071fb66421\nauthor Piotr Mankowski <pmanko@uw.edu> 1790621729 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790621729 -0700\n\nfix(ci): restore develop formatting and Transifex push (#4462)\n\n* fix(ci): restore develop formatting and surface Transifex upload errors\n\nCLAUDE.md: apply the Prettier rewrap that Backend / Formatting requires.\n#4382 last ran CI before the Formatting job existed (#4446), so the\nparagraph merged unchecked.\n\ntx-push: run `tx push --silent`. Without a TTY the CLI truncates every\nmessage to 78 characters, which cut off the reason Transifex rejects\nen.json since #4409. In silent mode errors print untruncated.\n\n* fix(i18n): make the #4409 plural strings uploadable to Transifex\n\nTransifex parses any value that starts with `{var, plural,` as a single\npluralized entry and rejected en.json on:\n\n  parse_error: Invalid format of pluralized entry with key:\n  \"validation\\.qcHold\\.withheld\"\n\nvalidation.qcHold.withheld and eqa.prep.needExplained both open with a\nplural and contain further plurals.\n\n- validation.qcHold.withheld: one whole-sentence plural. The key is not\n  referenced by any code, so nothing renders differently.\n- eqa.prep.needExplained: four independent counts cannot share one\n  plural, so the string now starts with \"Aliquots needed:\". The\n  PrepWorkbench default message and its test follow.\n\nValidation / i18n now runs check-transifex-plurals.py on PRs that touch\nthe language files, so a string like these fails before merge instead\nof breaking the post-merge Transifex push.\n\n* chore(i18n): drop the Transifex plural pre-check\n\nThe failure has happened once; the --silent push now names the rejected\nkey, which is enough to diagnose a recurrence. Revisit a PR-time check if\nit happens again.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqurghCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAY4EQAEfBoAj384IIGdM+M6meQ31c\nLxU3FNOImpKPJ69HEfC1sC9qmb2eVSdGIbh22iU/LUrZxRJDr2vKiRDzSUY99Bl3\npx5beVLjRqFMjbMP+9RwmzGrhJkgFqktalssnyhmZlKNpJeJWIH4+Bu6YHP0ZAeg\ncgDcwfHIUCE3onE1+DIDMlKPAHO1pSiYU1zm7f2DKzKGdOU01ITvQaNhS1NWxD+c\nutgPJTMDAUaRIeXNv4qEVCP7Hqdd+Y/71RFcaDgsRNk3f83TFQYxsgijbzvYF7NU\nRO3Lxto+Ie6d2B30Hy4QVtTGClWT/+bzIEH4Cs+3kbJAjQJH08RfbPTndZ