ceived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unazko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unazko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unazko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/unazko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/commits/207121f3ec6fd6422aecf17dc8a859826c1abac0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T11:20:20Z","email":"boyan.rakilovski@sap.com","name":"Boyan Rakilovski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T11:20:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ui5-color-palette): focus hue slider handle when More Colors dialog opens (#14095)\n\n**Issue**\nWhen the color picker was opened via the ''More Colors…'' button of the color\npalette, initial focus was not placed on the first meaningful control. The\ndialog''s default focus traversal did not land on the hue slider handle, so\nkeyboard and screen reader users had no clear starting point.\n\n**Solution**\nMade the color picker expose its hue slider as its focus target via\ngetFocusDomRef(), and focused the picker from the color palette on the\ndialog''s open event so focus reliably lands on the hue slider handle.\n\nRelated to: BGSOFUIBALKAN-10479","tree":{"sha":"074db789def23a4fe38a86cef8778045ddfd90ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/git/trees/074db789def23a4fe38a86cef8778045ddfd90ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/git/commits/207121f3ec6fd6422aecf17dc8a859826c1abac0","verification":{"payload":"tree 074db789def23a4fe38a86cef8778045ddfd90ad\nparent c941b95326b2cbafdaf18a4e0e7bbeee0f48f981\nauthor Boyan Rakilovski <boyan.rakilovski@sap.com> 1790594420 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790594420 +0300\n\nfix(ui5-color-palette): focus hue slider handle when More Colors dialog opens (#14095)\n\n**Issue**\nWhen the color picker was opened via the ''More Colors…'' button of the color\npalette, initial focus was not placed on the first meaningful control. The\ndialog''s default focus traversal did not land on the hue slider handle, so\nkeyboard and screen reader users had no clear starting point.\n\n**Solution**\nMade the color picker expose its hue slider as its focus target via\ngetFocusDomRef(), and focused the picker from the color palette on the\ndialog''s open event so focus reliably lands on the hue slider handle.\n\nRelated to: BGSOFUIBALKAN-10479","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquk10CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAH/4QAEALJhWM2P08nPfcDabDK2t5\nq0IA6PtGR1fMYTq6eKxxk2oEgI263bt4ruRhNVd9Zl9iTrrghdZMV4NundL97WsP\nALcvw+0h6Bpn3gjXswXKo3u0sPanugdiRuGWzJvNzKhOhwjqxE7ynOfSaQsg8S6g\ns4x9waTChZvKbYEhHbknXmmckci5a0hmYHLJ8H4mg5q9oYw25T+iizk38FT2KOGZ\na1cp/1CCF/EkCccmKhqwanS45xizrdBHq/dzXq9BWepa3QHKvBVXUbLvXcojXQzJ\n1vFofILMHDUeNio1ApWz4Y9KeLRQ0y6jPqo3cui3mEkIHfr37dikQOT9yGS5FER2\nalEn4dSm945dNM81gJCmaxlVRw0jTLjZD1mQyp7QIDDGXD711zmcMEWSdqJhJSC4\n9Qu6t32U0+WkH+apoZWLZe/H/WEy+8WPdfDeJEx9kEuVqTIkKKmgqvn96gusCSwc\nK4LL7GD5tV2XGWdGF2KMDOWEERwTinzsnUYMl6hXa0Hd2WGI1mLwowlgEPrpAVyi\nxLqJhlbMYBA7U/CyetY9crQZcoxhIsPpdjdvczSgzSXw3qd7OYoY8IIeC0AEvum/\nXnHccx7/6+clpxjYU9/oP3rJ5jZFJl24ZB/qloeKhmesj7C+NrY0ivljfvE9trqP\ndfrUjxpbZcTkHl6M6OVK\n=CzV7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T11:20:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/UI5/webcomponents/commit/207121f3ec6fd6422aecf17dc8a859826c1abac0","node_id":"C_kwDOCfpnRtoAKDIwNzEyMWYzZWM2ZmQ2NDIyYWVjZjE3ZGM4YTg1OTgyNmMxYWJhYzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/UI5/webcomponents/commit/c941b95326b2cbafdaf18a4e0e7bbeee0f48f981","sha":"c941b95326b2cbafdaf18a4e0e7bbeee0f48f981","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/commits/c941b95326b2cbafdaf18a4e0e7bbeee0f48f981"}],"sha":"207121f3ec6fd6422aecf17dc8a859826c1abac0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/commits/207121f3ec6fd6422aecf17dc8a859826c1abac0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106313486?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SvilenDarvenyashki/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SvilenDarvenyashki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SvilenDarvenyashki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SvilenDarvenyashki/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SvilenDarvenyashki","id":106313486,"login":"SvilenDarvenyashki","node_id":"U_kgDOBlY3Dg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SvilenDarvenyashki/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SvilenDarvenyashki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SvilenDarvenyashki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SvilenDarvenyashki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SvilenDarvenyashki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SvilenDarvenyashki","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/commits/c941b95326b2cbafdaf18a4e0e7bbeee0f48f981/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T07:15:36Z","email":"106313486+SvilenDarvenyashki@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Svilen Darvenyashki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T07:15:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ui5-user-settings-dialog): announce selection state to screen readers (#13928)\n\n* fix(ui5-user-settings-dialog): announce selection state to screen readers\n\n* refactor(ui5-user-settings-dialog): use native single selection for side navigation\n\nReplace the hand-emulated single-selection scheme (list in selectionMode\n\"None\" plus a private _forceAriaSelected flag on ListItem and manual\nInvisibleMessage announcements) with the List''s native selectionMode\n\"Single\", which provides row highlight, aria-selected, the hidden\n\"Selected/Not Selected\" describedby text and a polite announcement.\n\nSelection logic now listens to the List selection-change event; a\nseparate item-click handler keeps the narrow-mode drill-in. The public\nselection-change detail ({ item }) is unchanged.\n\n* refactor(ui5-user-settings-dialog): drop leftover i18n bundle and revert no-op properties change\n\nRemove the now-unused i18nBundle static (and its i18n/I18nBundle imports)\nfrom UserSettingsAppearanceView — the getText/announce usages it backed\nwere removed when the view moved to the List''s native single selection.","tree":{"sha":"b0b50ee1ba77563ad19ea023df36f26d646392ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/git/trees/b0b50ee1ba77563ad19ea023df36f26d646392ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/git/commits/c941b95326b2cbafdaf18a4e0e7bbeee0f48f981","verification":{"payload":"tree b0b50ee1ba77563ad19ea023df36f26d646392ac\nparent a5d95d3a7a827d1f4b96f24b814c4c9653f81ee0\nauthor Svilen Darvenyashki <106313486+SvilenDarvenyashki@users.noreply.github.com> 1790579736 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790579736 +0300\n\nfix(ui5-user-settings-dialog): announce selection state to screen readers (#13928)\n\n* fix(ui5-user-settings-dialog): announce selection state to screen readers\n\n* refactor(ui5-user-settings-dialog): use native single selection for side navigation\n\nReplace the hand-emulated single-selection scheme (list in selectionMode\n\"None\" plus a private _forceAriaSelected flag on ListItem and manual\nInvisibleMessage announcements) with the List''s native selectionMode\n\"Single\", which provides row highlight, aria-selected, the hidden\n\"Selected/Not Selected\" describedby text and a polite announcement.\n\nSelection logic now listens to the List selection-change event; a\nseparate item-click handler keeps the narrow-mode drill-in. The public\nselection-change detail ({ item }) is unchanged.\n\n* refactor(ui5-user-settings-dialog): drop leftover i18n bundle and revert no-op properties change\n\nRemove the now-unused i18nBundle static (and its i18n/I18nBundle imports)\nfrom UserSettingsAppearanceView — the getText/announce usages it backed\nwere removed when the view moved to the List''s native single selection.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquhQYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACjgQAB6MuYlODyfsHwtY9p4ZygX0\nk3m6aj23esT63L6GNrzsOxSuXLZZJRZmztZChv2evZY9xPELOhSqL37UGofeZkGy\n0xxsat94XFALyIbtpUObkXzhlar7S+oqbTLfgxXWbImems9dSyM5DJ1OnQpaIIga\nuwORY7jjc6WYBiK1j7m/DNxE1Y/evIgR29G08SjY+5zROTejItdiwMiHrh9OIeCx\nSLr727YfG6c1G1BrUiFInnXslEM5CYn4JRYCx5V5KLsX+fdzpjN2EF9v6MQHOxv+\ngG5cVnJyLjl7V3J/mWd5RtLxAc7FSQplRr0vEdIxMx0wSBk3TwIPyCDELGcHKeJT\nrWj1yI+aMFYFAKjJ1eCnFvPhd77okNR17QK3FXsOnSq8cmHzFcQ3+UMVLXL07egj\n24SI7KvrjHaO1YPdPDbxMbpyHkSlE23GOebyL6WUgeBtnzbGWgYHZDnXwgqsqtwK\nO+WulklhVnH9DICWTZUg+gJNV36dq3dw0VEtFx33uJ76uSxZiA7h9sNrxBFyshMw\nyq0Ox6XT1et93V4mrRWv87R4gvKOoGjv1lMS8unaovoH4ORk9Ggcb1Zt/SmPXGyL\n6/RPoSZ0eF+POP1635GysuWNG/mAyy9sRZewf5PV0ptGH0qSHdofjqOm08aa