ld value.\n\nWith this change we clear the native input `placeholder` in `ui5-datetime-input` whenever `value` is non-empty, so screen readers are not given redundant hint text while the control is filled.\n\nThe same behavior applies to `ui5-date-time-picker`, `ui5-date-range-picker`, and `ui5-time-picker`.","tree":{"sha":"e19dffd12b307ee654362e4797c9887bcfd8e284","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/git/trees/e19dffd12b307ee654362e4797c9887bcfd8e284"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/git/commits/172aaee4ba8fd1f5c8a1ab441d36f30f76d1b7f3","verification":{"payload":"tree e19dffd12b307ee654362e4797c9887bcfd8e284\nparent 849466d29075aac4265190b62b3c8dcaafe08f4e\nauthor Stoyan <88034608+hinzzx@users.noreply.github.com> 1789547157 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789547157 +0300\n\nfix(ui5-date-picker): prevent placeholder announcement when value is set (#14049)\n\nPreviously, when a `ui5-date-picker` had a valid date, JAWS could still announce the default example placeholder (for example `e.g. Dec 31, 2026`) on focus, together with the role description and the actual field value.\n\nWith this change we clear the native input `placeholder` in `ui5-datetime-input` whenever `value` is non-empty, so screen readers are not given redundant hint text while the control is filled.\n\nThe same behavior applies to `ui5-date-time-picker`, `ui5-date-range-picker`, and `ui5-time-picker`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqlKVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFSUQAJ4H/e+bdM3ogHW/CV0z93q4\nOnl/wl+q4L2Yk27xZuf50hpAaaQdBkTShPb+CwP2yYIkdp42OABnDuHjE6zBJB2O\nHHV0pF4NLotrMvNsy4enOkz7LFQBXjLajcjIbunDSJRDbnzNqgMQsxaVRHoYLHyE\nrwGlQ47KQGvAnl1qUgQ/wFC8gw/Yk1i36viJ0Bc6qqmxyr9FwsETnkg/O//YmUir\nlCSUDFlYxau5zPFx4hetF3rOeUwQLqshGtldgoptZTYB8SZxllRSAwn7yW3Xkkmc\n1DfkYSoZ/GKMyfiU8CU/BwQPRIw1BNymK8ON89qxkeZbYKttmynTdzeYur25EIIN\n5ygW9wAdCtXhtSADxme9S1W5FTLo3l2lRcYVfAYsoDm2R4ESoyhoKDSPnCDiUzqf\np7ux2X3CRGMMposbAQRhsXpcBu7H0s