ithub.com/users/plamenivanov91/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamenivanov91/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamenivanov91/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamenivanov91/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/plamenivanov91","id":13866865,"login":"plamenivanov91","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODY2ODY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamenivanov91/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamenivanov91/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamenivanov91/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamenivanov91/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamenivanov91/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamenivanov91","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/commits/849466d29075aac4265190b62b3c8dcaafe08f4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T07:32:41Z","email":"plamen.ivanov01@sap.com","name":"Plamen Ivanov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T07:32:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ui5-avatar-badge): add colorScheme property for extended color palette (#14009)\n\nAdds a new colorScheme property accepting values \"1\" through \"10\",\nbacked by the SAP indication color tokens (sapIndicationColor_N_*).\nThis follows the same pattern used by ui5-tag and avoids introducing\na new enum, keeping the API intentionally loose to match established\nconventions.\n\nEach value maps directly to its own CSS rule setting background,\nborder-color, and text color from the indication palette, plus a\nbox-shadow via sapContent_Shadow1 for visual depth. The semantic\nstate property takes precedence over colorScheme when set to any\nvalue other than None.\n\nFixes: #13925\nJIRA: BGSOFUIPIRIN-7121","tree":{"sha":"3ff2e534133b50c3ed23160797ad773ad3a8bacf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/git/trees/3ff2e534133b50c3ed23160797ad773ad3a8bacf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/git/commits/849466d29075aac4265190b62b3c8dcaafe08f4e","verification":{"payload":"tree 3ff2e534133b50c3ed23160797ad773ad3a8bacf\nparent bf491e75b16f6e51c95f69db63a8a15951e0fdcb\nauthor Plamen Ivanov <plamen.ivanov01@sap.com> 1789543961 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789543961 +0300\n\nfeat(ui5-avatar-badge): add colorScheme property for extended color palette (#14009)\n\nAdds a new colorScheme property accepting values \"1\" through \"10\",\nbacked by the SAP indication color tokens (sapIndicationColor_N_*).\nThis follows the same pattern used by ui5-tag and avoids introducing\na new enum, keeping the API intentionally loose to match established\nconventions.\n\nEach value maps directly to its own CSS rule setting background,\nborder-color, and text color from the indication palette, plus a\nbox-shadow via sapContent_Shadow1 for visual depth. The semantic\nstate property takes precedence over colorScheme when set to any\nvalue other than None.\n\nFixes: #13925\nJIRA: BGSOFUIPIRIN-7121","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqkYZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbbsQAF+qEeHZPZjiHb1diWrF+Svk\nJziQ2QQZ/HukhD56XrH5NN1gjukH+c+aGUXp1+m7wT+MTjbjOV5EkvwiGlyKrhzW\n8mS3uiUEEZ5DoyP9mBDiosIuGV8sknzMegEoRgpLoZT2QQpQeXi/HW3k0wU1R8ji\nZHwGH6g9zvGiG9QaEoQN79S23ALAG91oIXTdfiXDkaY3x+9vMrAIEcS7SRdCRl4f\nLSj+F0IDJ6+hnCWPYM5iCOLtfkam7ZzKbQ7n/j3TnmZfSPGQ+9NL7X8f/dtvamWk\n9OuP/sn5QWdc7gdBKmo/3Kbz91F6wPFC6JI8Cu7Rfx6g+5EBoSydo+UzR9b8qCPQ\nGI9d/39NCQ2X5Ys1lrOmvRf6899JGc7nJUuRZdgqmzN3JrSiO6gI8XllA0FE9yuT\nb3IpePitv0G5g8GlfXkZffMlGaSfLlkMU9HE6PXibzCp3pcbq6afwgUNwrgTqPH0\nO/mWHBORDzM6YeRsGLTI1CQX7ZDm4kvkbb+QHc/KBKpyAJ5I327CGooJVNP8nsSs\niOlgDVOladrNZrkI+cCv/v1ZSklmAnp8FA4Y2vh1HANEoQRdWI4zwuBCKi2cVw6c\nr8u3pX4acZL9ijq2XCtxlmqcvp2lMfUUG4DNnUP/NMCmYoxITdTYdd851t9/2SR9\nN5qz3hpRCCHQ3Q4jrySf\n=KFMt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T07:32:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/UI5/webcomponents/commit/849466d29075aac4265190b62b3c8dcaafe08f4e","node_id":"C_kwDOCfpnRtoAKDg0OTQ2NmQyOTA3NWFhYzQyNjUxOTBiNjJiM2M4ZGNhYWZlMDhmNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/UI5/webcomponents/commit/bf491e75b16f6e51c95f69db63a8a15951e0fdcb","sha":"bf491e75b16f6e51c95f69db63a8a15951e0fdcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/commits/bf491e75b16f6e51c95f69db63a8a15951e0fdcb"}],"sha":"849466d29075aac4265190b62b3c8dcaafe08f4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/commits/849466d29075aac4265190b62b3c8dcaafe08f4e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22766569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dobrinyonkov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dobrinyonkov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dobrinyonkov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dobrinyonkov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dobrinyonkov","id":22766569,"login":"dobrinyonkov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNzY2NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dobrinyonkov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dobrinyonkov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dobrinyonkov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dobrinyonkov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dobrinyonkov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dobrinyonkov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/commits/bf491e75b16f6e51c95f69db63a8a15951e0fdcb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T20:33:00Z","email":"dobrin.dimchev@sap.com","name":"Dobrin Dimchev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T20:33:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ui5-toolbar): add overflow-group property for atomic group overflow (#13949)\n\n* feat(ui5-toolbar): add overflow-group for atomic group overflow\n\nIntroduce a free-form ''overflowGroup'' string property on ToolbarItemBase.\nItems sharing the same non-empty group overflow as one atomic unit:\neither all visible in the bar, or all in the overflow popover, never\nsplit. The visible bar always preserves slot order; group members\nbecome adjacent only inside the popover.\n\n- ToolbarItemBase: new @property() ''overflowGroup'' (default '''').\n- Toolbar.distributeItems: bucket movable items into ''distribution\n  units'' before iterating right-to-left. Each unit is either a single\n  ungrouped item or a group of items sharing a non-empty overflowGroup,\n  ordered by the rightmost member''s slot index. Atomic group push is\n  allowed to over-shoot the recovered-width target (per ADR-0001).\n- Toolbar.onInvalidation: re-distribute when the per-child grouping\n  signature changes, not only when itemsWidth changes.\n- Six new Cypress tests in Toolbar.cy.tsx covering contiguous overflow,\n  non-contiguous overflow, resize round-trip, reverseOverflow popover\n  order, runtime overflowGroup change, and slot-order preservation.\n- New dev sample at packages/main/test/pages/ToolbarOverflowGroup.html\n  demonstrating all four scenarios.\n\nDefault behavior for overflowGroup='''' is unchanged; minContentWidth\ncalculation is unchanged.\n\nRefs: docs/adr/0001-toolbar-overflow-group.md\n\n* feat(ui5-toolbar): warn on invalid overflow-group configurations\n\nSurface developer mistakes in `overflowGroup` configuration with\none-shot `console.warn` messages and keep the toolbar''s overflow\nalgorithm tolerant of the violations:\n\n- A grouped item with `overflowPriority` set to `AlwaysOverflow` or\n  `NeverOverflow` violates ADR-0001. The new\n  `ToolbarItemBase.effectiveOverflowPriority` getter emits a one-shot\n  warning naming the element and downgrades the priority to `Default`\n  for the layout pass; the group continues to overflow atomically.\n- A `ui5-toolbar-spacer` with a non-empty `overflowGroup` cannot\n  participate in grouping. The new `effectiveOverflowGroup` getter\n  emits a one-shot warning and returns `\"\"` so the spacer is not\n  yoked to the group; its existing overflow behavior is unchanged.\n\n`Toolbar` now consults these effective getters in `alwaysOverflowItems`,\n`movableItems`, the `minContentWidth` calculation, and\n`buildDistributionUnits`. Warnings are suppressed across re-renders via\nper-instance flags, consistent with `ToolbarItem.checkForWrapper`.\n\nJSDoc on `overflowGroup` now lists both restrictions explicitly.\n\n* test(ui5-toolbar): cover canonical flex-spacer overflow-group case\n\nAddress code-review feedback on the validation-warnings change:\n\n- Add a test for the canonical case — a default `ui5-toolbar-spacer`\n  (no width, default priority) with a non-empty `overflow-group` — and\n  assert the spacer-rule warning still fires. The previous coverage\n  only exercised a fixed-width spacer, leaving the more common flex\n  case implicit.\n- Drop redundant double parentheses around `($tb[0] as Toolbar)` casts\n  before `.onResize()` calls.\n\n* docs(ui5-toolbar): add grouped-overflow website sample\n\nAdd a documentation-website sample under `_samples/main/Toolbar/GroupedOverflow/`\ndemonstrating the `overflow-group` property on `ui5-toolbar`. A \"Filter:\"\nlabel-button and its sibling `ui5-toolbar-select` share\n`overflow-group=\"filters\"` so they overflow into the popover together.\n\nThe toolbar is constrained to 320px so the group cannot fit alongside the\nungrouped Add/Reject buttons — both group members move into the overflow\npopover atomically, while the ungrouped items stay in the bar. The teaching\ncomment describes this static end-state honestly (no responsive narration).\n\nWires the sample into the Toolbar docs page under \"More Samples\".\n\n* chore: wip snapshot before emergency context switch\n\nSaving scratch notes, docs, and validation test page from\ntoolbar-overflow-group work in progress.\n\n* chore: remove scratch and working files\n\n* refactor(ui5-toolbar): address review comments for overflow-group\n\n- build the slotIndex map once in distributeItems and pass it into\n  buildDistributionUnits instead of allocating it twice per layout pass\n- move overflow-group validation warnings out of the effectiveOverflow*\n  getters into validateOverflowGroupConstraints (called from\n  onAfterRendering) so the getters stay pure\n- remove leftover ADR-0001 references from source and test comments\n- consolidate the standalone overflow-group test pages into Toolbar.html","tree":{"sha":"928662d4628a8e1f7acab7d09b4f25c3c42c239b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/git/trees/928662d4628a8e1f7acab7d09b4f25c3c42c239b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/git/commits/bf491e75b16f6e51c95f69db63a8a15951e0fdcb","verification":{"payload":"tree 928662d4628a8e1f7acab7d09b4f25c3c42c239b\nparent ecea7e748bd3e5eba71522286057ba20db2e961e\nauthor Dobrin Dimchev <dobrin.dimchev@sap.com> 1789504380 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789504380 +0300\n\nfeat(ui5-toolbar): add overflow-group property for atomic group overflow (#13949)\n\n* feat(ui5-toolbar): add overflow-group for atomic group overflow\n\nIntroduce a free-form ''overflowGroup'' string property on ToolbarItemBase.\nItems sharing the same non-empty group overflow as one atomic unit:\neither all visible in the bar, or all in the overflow popover, never\nsplit. The visible bar always preserves slot order; group members\nbecome adjacent only inside the popover.\n\n- ToolbarItemBase: new @property() ''overflowGroup'' (default '''').\n- Toolbar.distributeItems: bucket movable items into ''distribution\n  units'' before iterating right-to-left. Each unit is either a single\n  ungrouped item or a group of items sharing a non-empty overflowGroup,\n  ordered by the rightmost member''s slot index. Atomic group push is\n  allowed to over-shoot the recovered-width target (per ADR-0001).\n- Toolbar.onInvalidation: re-distribute when the per-child grouping\n  signature changes, not only when itemsWidth changes.\n- Six new Cypress tests in Toolbar.cy.tsx covering contiguous overflow,\n  non-contiguous overflow, resize round-trip, reverseOverflow popover\n  order, runtime overflowGroup change, and slot-order preservation.\n- New dev sample at packages/main/test/pages/ToolbarOverflowGroup.html\n  demonstrating all four scenarios.\n\nDefault behavior for overflowGroup='''' is unchanged; minContentWidth\ncalculation is unchanged.\n\nRefs: docs/adr/0001-toolbar-overflow-group.md\n\n* feat(ui5-toolbar): warn on invalid overflow-group configurations\n\nSurface developer mistakes in `overflowGroup` configuration with\none-shot `console.warn` messages and keep the toolbar''s overflow\nalgorithm tolerant of the violations:\n\n- A grouped item with `overflowPriority` set to `AlwaysOverflow` or\n  `NeverOverflow` violates ADR-0001. The new\n  `ToolbarItemBase.effectiveOverflowPriority` getter emits a one-shot\n  warning naming the element and downgrades the priority to `Default`\n  for the layout pass; the group continues to overflow atomically.\n- A `ui5-toolbar-spacer` with a non-empty `overflowGroup` cannot\n  participate in grouping. The new `effectiveOverflowGroup` getter\n  emits a one-shot warning and returns `\"\"` so the spacer is not\n  yoked to the group; its existing overflow behavior is unchanged.\n\n`Toolbar` now consults these effective getters in `alwaysOverflowItems`,\n`movableItems`, the `minContentWidth` calculation, and\n`buildDistributionUnits`. Warnings are suppressed across re-renders via\nper-instance flags, consistent with `ToolbarItem.checkForWrapper`.\n\nJSDoc on `overflowGroup` now lists both restrictions explicitly.\n\n* test(ui5-toolbar): cover canonical flex-spacer overflow-group case\n\nAddress code-review feedback on the validation-warnings change:\n\n- Add a test for the canonical case — a default `ui5-toolbar-spacer`\n  (no width, default priority) with a non-empty `overflow-group` — and\n  assert the spacer-rule warning still fires. The previous coverage\n  only exercised a fixed-width spacer, leaving the more common flex\n  case implicit.\n- Drop redundant double parentheses around `($tb[0] as Toolbar)` casts\n  before `.onResize()` calls.\n\n* docs(ui5-toolbar): add grouped-overflow website sample\n\nAdd a documentation-website sample under `_samples/main/Toolbar/GroupedOverflow/`\ndemonstrating the `overflow-group` property on `ui5-toolbar`. A \"Filter:\"\nlabel-button and its sibling `ui5-toolbar-select` share\n`overflow-group=\"filters\"` so they overflow into the popover together.\n\nThe toolbar is constrained to 320px so the group cannot fit alongside the\nungrouped Add/Reject buttons — both group members move into the overflow\npopover atomically, while the ungrouped items stay in the bar. The teaching\ncomment describes this static end-state honestly (no responsive narration).\n\nWires the sample into the Toolbar docs page under \"More Samples\".\n\n* chore: wip snapshot before emergency context switch\n\nSaving scratch notes, docs, and validation test page from\ntoolbar-overflow-group work in progress.\n\n* chore: remove scratch and working files\n\n* refactor(ui5-toolbar): address review comments for overflow-group\n\n- build the slotIndex map once in distributeItems and pass it into\n  buildDistributionUnits instead of allocating it twice per layout pass\n- move overflow-group validation warnings out of the effectiveOverflow*\n  getters into validateOverflowGroupConstraints (called from\n  onAfterRendering) so the getters stay pure\n- remove leftover ADR-0001 references from source and test comments\n- consolidate the standalone overflow-group test pages into Toolbar.html","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqat8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQF8QAA4Ta67/YDfuHE9gyTvzvMxZ\nL1jykTz9JKbDjVAAL5LqLy/KLWkTra52eUopX3JtuFi1xYeNqpo9B/vv96SeQpb7\ny/gJy5Xa3M9Ejh928mHCxdTquP4eVdNqs4VqxVbZNTYNWXfiine8XbXt4JMJbPCN\n/yszFRAZWVQvldOkUpJFe8U3VzkKOKL6YfAfrmd4i1Nwqxd+JsImAppygLIEcjP8\nZX/1z8s43AYT54tYqZSp8a4RMvdia/fyreIZl//tLHCfIm5vTIAjGH7mkXX+06Ng\nAcbyLAnLxmD69Erm4QqpqlBy/1g+Q9JhWGxTFEy4oDoHXa7Vt3qdi6HAKOmU3P89\nhUAfmLnU1b1k+eTmxGVZfLfwLlh6TUycLnk5V/qSCxe29FUw/qjt8JQ2MmPIH/tN\nH31LNrLCnqoLq60TDOC+Y2qE5uM36p/7S5vG9zPfCZ3i4KsbdMZwNK29fq4a23YL\n5Yz1frTcmgyKnYzqzJ47GKYth8/zKV/Ni8H2DJm7ruagN+vnZrny3Hb6jww4QCi6\n6izZAIr1jNZQTadexxUBoJZggXPEDdiVQQSt8dp+gqVSkQ9vFlAl56rqYZEAcG6e\nkNkDWO2WFIiir7ZIQIl7wkUs0nUu2A3qg9W+CDEpIsMteT6y+DWcsAakoD6H0hLw\nq3sJJrQDGPxAMyqxAUsT\n=wVCc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T20:33:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/