//api.github.com/users/hinzzx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hinzzx","id":88034608,"login":"hinzzx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MDM0NjA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hinzzx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hinzzx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hinzzx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hinzzx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hinzzx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hinzzx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/commits/fa3e8543d49345dd25ea903015bd4575e924b30e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T12:59:36Z","email":"88034608+hinzzx@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Stoyan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T12:59:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ui5-time-picker): separate mobile and desktop value-help tap handling (#14048)\n\nPreviously, on phone, tapping the value-help control on `ui5-time-picker` often opened the numeric inputs popover instead of the clocks dialog, sometimes needed a second tap to open the clocks, or moved focus to a footer button when the clocks dialog opened.\n\nA single `click` handler on `DateTimeInput` could not reliably separate icon taps from input taps, and blanket `preventDefault()` on mobile `focusin` interfered with the first activation of the icon.\n\nWith this change we open the inputs popover from `focusin` on the native input only, leave value-help activation on the icon, skip mobile handling in `_handleInputClick`, and set `preventInitialFocus` on the responsive popover when it is shown as a dialog on phone.\n\nThe two mobile Cypress tests that use the value-help button (`.ui5-time-picker-input-icon-button` with `realClick`) are enabled again and will be observed.","tree":{"sha":"ca104eeec138ad5d627d6adda2b8d7e6db6e0d00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/git/trees/ca104eeec138ad5d627d6adda2b8d7e6db6e0d00"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UI5/webcomponents/git/commits/fa3e8543d49345dd25ea903015bd4575e924b30e","verification":{"payload":"tree ca104eeec138ad5d627d6adda2b8d7e6db6e0d00\nparent a042bc832401fab01d7959cbacdf842616a01241\nauthor Stoyan <88034608+hinzzx@users.noreply.github.com> 1789390776 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789390776 +0300\n\nfix(ui5-time-picker): separate mobile and desktop value-help tap handling (#14048)\n\nPreviously, on phone, tapping the value-help control on `ui5-time-picker` often opened the numeric inputs popover instead of the clocks dialog, sometimes needed a second tap to open the clocks, or moved focus to a footer button when the clocks dialog opened.\n\nA single `click` handler on `DateTimeInput` could not reliably separate icon taps from input taps, and blanket `preventDefault()` on mobile `focusin` interfered with the first activation of the icon.\n\nWith this change we open the inputs popover from `focusin` on the native input only, leave value-help activation on the icon, skip mobile handling in `_handleInputClick`, and set `preventInitialFocus` on the responsive popover when it is shown as a dialog on phone.\n\nThe two mobile Cypress tests that use the value-help button (`.ui5-time-picker-input-icon-button` with `realClick`) are enabled again and will be observed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp++4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA378QACp3sftFZEE1ngpCuLWxotvG\ng5DATfvXgSVS2ogR0jA6r2ChXy9m8fqJ3Nr7Fph9CSkOnfTmkPINpNK1iTdioIxJ\nr4Ys3RSIOU2s0g6+Orx3hGMf5hgJ1PKGtuMLM9bUV9AekPo8oIi3hwK7yZx2EJyQ\nJHA2msHtU8oDKHBTFP/5Q7qf3w5c86WeFjrFQJaoN7v3Zlvjk0CBIXzAEvwcukkV\nwPIazyMd6TDg/PoUltpzGHmV3b6J+z5Nkm9fIU0Psk0QSTKhBRFa/9u2LKVaG6Cc\nHwbnsYrzfLFby8CC5P19Rkxcp7c9/eQAevNlRdCfhPEpr24z4TaMiERFAGdgB5fA\ntaUHGayzl9/8Td8RxMT8Dhbi9KPDVeF8wDnSiMOgb7zzrhpQmxbKRMrAHozrlfid\nrOZw5+FHgNfauRtje9m9fd